window.DATA=window.DATA||{};DATA.en=[{"id":"petualangan-fotosintesis","kat":"kertas","katN":"Paper & ink","n":"Photosynthesis Adventure","mapel":"Science","jenjang":"Grade 4 – middle school (Grades 7–9)","topik":"Photosynthesis: water & xylem, stomata & CO₂, chlorophyll & chloroplast, glucose & oxygen","img":"img/petualangan-fotosintesis.jpg","preview":"https://preview.edugamelabs.com/kertas-tinta/games/petualangan-fotosintesis/","prompt":"# ROLE\n- You are an art director + lead developer. Rebuild the educational platformer game \"Petualangan Fotosintesis\" in ONE file `index.html` (pure HTML+CSS+JS, no libraries, no build, no server/API/login). All images are drawn with Canvas 2D, all sounds are synthesized with WebAudio. Product language: Indonesian.\n\n# PRODUCT\n- Title: **Petualangan Fotosintesis**. Genre: 4-chapter narrative platformer, science subject, topic photosynthesis (water & xylem, stomata & CO₂, chlorophyll & chloroplast, glucose & oxygen), grade level elementary school grade 4 – middle school.\n- Character: **Clawd** — an orange square creature with ink outlines, two rectangular black eyes, two short arms, four legs alternating while walking. Shrinks through a magnifying glass then enters inside a leaf.\n- Flow: Menu → (opening story) → 4 side-scroller chapters → (closing story) → Results. Each chapter: intro card → arena → 2 question gates → magnifying glass portal.\n- 3 difficulty levels: **Penjelajah Cilik** (elementary 4–6), **Penjelajah Hebat** (elementary 6–middle school 7), **Ilmuwan Muda** (middle school). 3 lives per chapter, refilled fully each chapter.\n\n# VISUAL STYLE\n- Palette (write once as CSS vars, reference by name):\n  - `--paper:#efebe2` paper background; `--paper-2:#faf8f2` cards/fills; `--ink:#2e2620` ink; `--muted:#6d665b` weak text; `--line:#d6d0c3` gray line.\n  - `--accent:#d8714f` Clawd orange accent; `--accent-dark:#b4553a`; `--clawd-h:#a94c33` body shading.\n  - `--leaf:#6fa83c`; `--leaf-dark:#4c8128`; `--leaf-light:#9cc95a`; `--leaf-outline:#36561c`; `--vein:#dde8a6` pale vein.\n  - `--water:#8cc8d6`; `--water-dark:#4f9db3`.\n  - `--epi:#e2eac6` epidermis; `--epi-light:#eef3dc`; `--epi-line:#b5c68a`; `--epi-dark:#8fa363`.\n  - `--dark:#173826` chloroplast; `--dark-3:#11291b`; `--mem:#57b44e` membrane; `--mem-light:#a5e09b`; `--bead:#a9dba0`.\n  - `--gold:#e2a93b`; `--sun:#f2a93b`; `--co-o:#d9663f` oxygen; `--co-c:#3b3434` carbon; `--glu:#f3e6c4` glucose.\n- Google Fonts: **Source Serif 4** (400;700) titles/questions/card numbers; **Caveat** (600;700) handwriting & sound words; **IBM Plex Mono** (400;500) small capital labels; **Geist** (400;600;800) buttons & UI.\n- All shapes are drawn as **hand-drawn ink lines**: each line is split every ±9 px, each point is offset by a small random amount (seeded hash), the randomization changes **7 times/second** (\"boil\" effect). Shadows = thin diagonal hatching (0.7 px lines, alpha 0.35), not blur.\n- Paper grain: 128×128 px noise pattern, alpha 0–24, stacked at alpha 0.5–1. Soft radial vignette from `rgba(255,253,246,0.7)` to `rgba(214,204,186,0.55)`.\n- Cards: `background:var(--paper-2)`, `border:1.5px solid var(--ink)`, `border-radius:12px`, padding 20px. Buttons: 1.5px ink border, radius 8px, padding 12px 14px, hover `#fff`, active `translateY(2px)`, focus-visible outline 2px `--accent`.\n- Answer cards: paper box with ink lines, small orange scribble in the top-left corner, circular A/B/C label 5.2 px radius with 6.5 px mono text. Correct → fill `--accent`, white text. Wrong → fill `#d8d2c6` with diagonal hatching + ink cross + blob.\n- Correct effect: large italic sound word (\"TING!\") in orange + 14 rays + 4-point stars + paper scraps scattering + small screen shake + small mono \"+points\" rising. Wrong: ink \"SPLAT!\" + falling ink drops + thin dark flash. Character hit: \"AUW!\" + invulnerability blink. Streak ≥3 → handwritten \"beruntun x3\".\n- Motion: cards pop in (ease-out cubic 0.4s), character squash & stretch on jump/land, hitstop 60 ms on hit, clouds drift slowly, orange sun with ray lines.\n- Page: white card with 1.5 px ink border, radius 10 px, large serif question above the arena with a wavy orange underline (SVG path `M2 6 C 30 2, 60 9, 100 5 S 170 3, 198 6` stroke `#d8714f` 2.6 px), HUD in capital mono letters.\n\n# SCREENS & LAYOUT\n- **Menu** (from top): capital mono label \"IPA · fotosintesis · petualangan platformer\"; brand block (left: 300px preview canvas, aspect 3/2, ink border, radius 10px; right: large serif title `clamp(32px,7vw,52px)` \"Petualangan Fotosintesis\" with a green SVG underline `#6fa83c` 2.8px under the word \"Fotosintesis\", 1-sentence description); 4-chapter list in a 4-column grid (2 columns at ≤620px), each item with dashed ink border, radius 8px, with a chapter color circle (Chapter1 `#8cc8d6`, Chapter2 `#e4ecc9`, Chapter3 `#57b44e`, Chapter4 `#173826`); 3-level button grid (1 column at ≤560px), each button with 20px serif title + 13px subtitle + 11px orange mono best score; footer handwritten note in Caveat 21px dark orange \"4 bab, 8 teka-teki, kumpulkan bahan fotosintesis!\".\n- **Play** (from top): 12px capital mono HUD (Bab x/4 · ♥♥♥ orange 18px letter-spacing 3px · Bahan x/y · Skor); photosynthesis equation row in serif 700 `clamp(14px,2.6vw,19px)` with 5 dashed chips (6H₂O + 6CO₂ + cahaya → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂) that light up one per chapter; question row `#qText` serif 700 `clamp(19px,3.8vw,30px)` with wavy orange underline + `#qOpts` choice chips; 16:9 arena canvas with ink border, radius 10px; button pad ◀ ▶ LOMPAT (3-column grid, min-height 66px, LOMPAT orange); tools row (keyboard hint + \"Suara: hidup\" & \"Keluar\" buttons).\n- **Results**: level label; serif title `clamp(28px,6vw,40px)`; ★ stars 42px letter-spacing 8px orange (off = `--line`); message; 3-stat dashed grid (Skor / Benar pertama kali / Bahan terkumpul); 4-point recap with border-left 3px `--leaf`; best score; \"Main lagi\" button (orange), \"Coba lagi dari bab ini\" (shown on loss), \"Ganti tingkat\".\n- In-arena overlays: `.say` Clawd speech bubble (left 32%, right 3%, top 4%, ink border, radius 14px, shadow `4px 4px 0 rgba(46,38,32,.85)`, \"CLAWD\" label in orange mono, text in Geist 600, \"ketuk untuk lanjut ▸\" in Caveat); `.ccard` chapter card (inset 7% 12%, radius 14px, shadow `5px 5px 0 rgba(46,38,32,.85)`, chapter tag + serif title + fact + goal in green Caveat + \"Mulai jelajah ▸\" button); `.toast` message (top center, ink border, radius 10px, ✓ green / ✗ orange).\n- At ≤620px `.say` and `.ccard` become static (top border only, no shadow).\n\n# MECHANICS\n- World 1600 px, logic canvas 480×270 (16:9), ground GROUND=226. Camera follows player `clamp(p.x+p.w/2 - W*0.4, 0, LEN-W)` lerp `dt*6`. Parallax background 0.5.\n- Fixed-step physics 1/120 second. Gravity ~900 px/s², run speed ~120 px/s, jump can be shortened (release button → vy cut), coyote time + jump buffer.\n- One-way platforms (can be passed from below, land from above).\n- **Question gates**: locked wall marked \"?\" + 3 floating A/B/C answer blocks (text wrapped max 2 lines, block width 50–84 px, height 30 px). Bump block from below: correct → \"TING!\" + confetti + wall splits (1.3 s animation) + short explanation; wrong → \"SPLAT!\" + life −1 + block crossed out. Question + choices shown large above the arena when Clawd is within 110 px of the gate.\n- **Materials** per chapter (8–10 items): water drops, CO₂ molecules, light motes, glucose rings. \"ting!\" effect + score.\n- **Enemies** per chapter: aphids (Chapter1), pollution smoke (Chapter2), spiky free radicals (Chapter3–4). Stomp from above = \"PLOK!\" +5 + bounce. Side hit = life −1 + invulnerable 1.6 s.\n- Falling into a gap = life −1, respawn slightly behind (last safe position). Lives exhausted → loss results screen.\n- Magnifying glass portal at x=1532 opens after 2 gates are completed → next chapter visible inside the lens → \"BAB SELESAI!\" + one part of the equation lights up in the HUD.\n- Score: +5 per stomped enemy, +points per material, first-time-correct bonus. Streak ≥3 → handwritten \"beruntun x3\".\n\n# LEVELS & QUESTIONS\n- **Chapter 1 · Jalan Air** (music key 0, item \"tetes air\"/H₂O): fact \"Clawd kini sekecil semut, berdiri di atas urat daun. Air dari akar naik lewat pembuluh kayu (xilem) sampai ke sini.\"; goal \"Kumpulkan tetes air 💧 dan buka 2 gerbang urat daun.\"; complete \"Air (H₂O) sudah sampai di daun!\".\n- **Chapter 2 · Gerbang Stomata** (key 2, \"molekul CO₂\"): fact \"Permukaan daun penuh lubang mungil bernama stomata. Lewat 'mulut daun' ini, karbon dioksida (CO₂) dari udara masuk.\"; goal \"Tangkap molekul CO₂ ●●● dan buka mulut-mulut daun.\"; complete \"CO₂ berhasil masuk lewat stomata!\".\n- **Chapter 3 · Panel Surya Hijau** (key −3, \"butir cahaya\"): fact \"Di dalam sel ada kloroplas. Tumpukan tilakoidnya berisi klorofil yang menangkap cahaya, mirip deretan panel surya.\"; goal \"Kumpulkan butir cahaya ☀ untuk menyalakan klorofil.\"; complete \"Klorofil menyala menangkap cahaya!\".\n- **Chapter 4 · Pabrik Gula** (key 5, \"glukosa\"/C₆H₁₂O₆): fact \"Energi cahaya memecah air dan melepas oksigen (O₂). Lalu CO₂ dirakit menjadi gula glukosa, makanan tumbuhan.\"; goal \"Rakit glukosa ⬡ dan lepaskan oksigen untuk dunia!\"; complete \"Glukosa jadi, O₂ terlepas ke udara!\".\n- **Question bank** (correct answer = first option, shuffled on display; each question has a 1-sentence explanation). Each chapter has 4 questions per level; 2 questions are picked randomly per chapter.\n- **Easy level** (Penjelajah Cilik):\n  - Chapter1: \"Tumbuhan menyerap air dari tanah lewat …\" → **akar** (daun, bunga). \"Rumus kimia air adalah …\" → **H₂O** (CO₂, O₂). \"Air dari akar naik menuju …\" → **daun** (tanah, awan). \"Bagian yang mengalirkan air dari akar ke daun adalah …\" → **batang** (bunga, buah).\n  - Chapter2: \"Gas dari udara yang diambil daun adalah …\" → **CO₂** (O₂, H₂O). \"Lubang kecil di daun tempat udara masuk disebut …\" → **stomata** (akar, batang). \"CO₂ di udara salah satunya berasal dari napas …\" → **manusia** (batu, pasir). \"Stomata paling banyak ada di …\" → **bawah daun** (akar, bunga).\n  - Chapter3: \"Energi untuk fotosintesis berasal dari …\" → **Matahari** (Bulan, angin). \"Zat hijau daun disebut …\" → **klorofil** (glukosa, oksigen). \"Klorofil tersimpan di dalam …\" → **kloroplas** (akar, tanah). \"Klorofil menangkap cahaya seperti …\" → **panel surya** (payung, cermin).\n  - Chapter4: \"Makanan yang dibuat daun adalah …\" → **gula** (garam, minyak). \"Gas yang dilepas tumbuhan untuk kita hirup adalah …\" → **O₂** (CO₂, asap). \"Fotosintesis paling banyak terjadi di …\" → **daun** (akar, buah). \"Gula dari daun dipakai tumbuhan untuk …\" → **tumbuh** (tidur, bernyanyi).\n- **Hard level** (Ilmuwan Muda):\n  - Chapter1: \"Pembuluh pengangkut air dari akar ke daun disebut …\" → **xilem** (floem, stomata). \"Penguapan air lewat stomata disebut …\" → **transpirasi** (respirasi, fermentasi). \"Floem bertugas mengangkut …\" → **gula** (air tanah, udara). \"Berapa molekul air untuk membuat 1 glukosa?\" → **6** (1, 12).\n  - Chapter2: \"Sel yang membuka dan menutup stomata disebut …\" → **sel penjaga** (sel darah, sel akar). \"CO₂ masuk ke daun dengan cara …\" → **difusi** (dipompa, fotolisis). \"Berapa molekul CO₂ untuk membuat 1 glukosa?\" → **6** (2, 3). \"Stomata menutup saat tumbuhan …\" → **kekurangan air** (kena cahaya, kebanyakan air).\n  - Chapter3: \"Tumpukan tilakoid di kloroplas disebut …\" → **grana** (stroma, krista). \"Reaksi terang terjadi di …\" → **tilakoid** (stroma, inti sel). \"Warna cahaya yang paling sedikit diserap klorofil adalah …\" → **hijau** (merah, biru). \"Energi cahaya disimpan sementara dalam molekul …\" → **ATP** (DNA, NaCl).\n  - Chapter4: \"Pemecahan air oleh energi cahaya disebut …\" → **fotolisis** (glikolisis, transpirasi). \"Siklus Calvin (reaksi gelap) terjadi di …\" → **stroma** (tilakoid, stomata). \"Rumus kimia glukosa adalah …\" → **C₆H₁₂O₆** (CO₂, H₂O). \"Enzim pembuat ATP yang berputar seperti kincir adalah …\" → **ATP sintase** (amilase, lipase). \"Oksigen hasil fotosintesis berasal dari …\" → **air** (CO₂, glukosa).\n- **Medium level** (Penjelajah Hebat): mix 1 easy question + 1 hard question per chapter.\n- **Layout per chapter** (ground [x0,x1], platforms [x,y,w], enemies [a,b]):\n  - Chapter1: ground [[0,330],[372,700],[742,1100],[1142,1600]]; platforms [[140,174,60],[250,150,52],[470,168,64],[600,142,56]]; enemies [[420,650]].\n  - Chapter2: ground [[0,300],[344,520],[564,700],[742,1100],[1144,1600]]; platforms [[120,172,62],[300,150,58],[420,170,58],[596,148,62]]; enemies [[150,250],[380,480]].\n  - Chapter3: ground [[0,262],[304,462],[508,700],[742,1100],[1144,1600]]; platforms [[110,170,56],[220,142,52],[380,162,60],[520,150,60],[636,174,52]]; enemies [[320,430],[540,650]].\n  - Chapter4: ground [[0,282],[326,482],[528,700],[742,1100],[1146,1600]]; platforms [[130,164,58],[258,136,52],[400,162,58],[560,144,58]]; enemies [[140,240],[350,440],[560,660]].\n  - Gates at x=770 and x=1172; portal at x=1532.\n- **Opening story** (3 bubbles): \"Halo, aku Clawd! Tanaman ini tidak pernah makan, tapi terus tumbuh. Kok bisa, ya?\" → \"Ternyata daun bisa MEMASAK makanannya sendiri dengan cahaya Matahari. Namanya fotosintesis!\" → \"Yuk, kita kecilkan diri dan masuk ke dalam daun lewat kaca pembesar ini!\" (scene: orange sun, potted plant, Clawd walks in then lifts the magnifying glass; transition: golden circle iris zooming into the leaf).\n- **Closing story** (4 bubbles): \"Gula dari daun dirakit jadi kayu. Setiap tahun batang pohon menambah satu cincin baru.\" → \"Pohon demi pohon tumbuh menjadi hutan yang lebat…\" → \"…dan hutan di seluruh Bumi melepaskan oksigen untuk semua makhluk hidup.\" → \"Terima kasih, daun! Berkat fotosintesis, aku bisa bernapas lega. Hore!\" (scene: tree rings growing → forest from above → Earth surrounded by O₂ → Clawd smiling with O₂ bubbles).\n\n# MOTION, FEEDBACK & SOUND\n- WebAudio sound (oscillator + gain, no files):\n  - `jump`: triangle 320→640 Hz 0.13s vol 0.08. `land`: triangle 130→80 Hz 0.07s. `ting`: sine 1760 Hz 0.2s + sine 2637 Hz 0.28s delay 0.05. `bump`: triangle 170→100 Hz 0.1s. `correct`: triangle [523,659,784,1047,1319] every 0.07s + sine octave. `wrong`: sawtooth 220→90 Hz 0.35s. `stomp`: triangle 440→70 Hz 0.14s. `hurt`: sawtooth 330→80 Hz 0.3s. `open`: sine [392,523,659] every 0.09s. `zoom`: sine 200→1600 Hz 0.9s + triangle 300→2400 Hz. `clear`: triangle [523,659,784,1047,784,1047,1319,1568] every 0.09s. `over`: triangle [392,330,262,196] every 0.16s. `pop`: sine 600→900 Hz 0.06s.\n  - Background music: pentatonic arpeggio 104 BPM (spb = 60/104/2), pattern `[0,1,2,3,2,1,2,1]` from progression `[[0,4,7,12],[9,12,16,21],[5,9,12,17],[7,11,14,19]]`, key changes per chapter (0, 2, −3, 5). Bass every 4 steps, high note every odd step 6 of the bar.\n- Animation: card pop `ease-out cubic` 0.4s; speech bubble `rise` 0.35s (translateY 14px → 0, opacity 0 → 1); toast `tin` 0.3s; question `qpop` 0.4s (scale 0.85 rotate −2° → 1.04 rotate 1° → 1); \"ketuk untuk lanjut\" `nudge` 1s infinite (translateX 4px).\n- Chapter transition: golden circle iris, radius 0→560 px, zoom 1→6, duration 1.15s, cubic ease.\n- Particle effects: ring (radius grows 18–30), ray (14 rays, length 9, speed 70), star (4-point star, gravity 40), drop (ink drop, gravity 420), scrap (paper scrap, gravity 330), o2 (two-ball orange bubble rising).\n- Hitstop 60 ms on enemy stomp. Screen shake max 2 px, damped 22 px/s. Screen flash alpha max 0.22.\n\n# CONTROLS & RESPONSIVE\n- Keyboard: ← → / A D move, Space / ↑ / W jump (can be shortened), Enter continue dialog/card.\n- Touch: large ◀ ▶ LOMPAT buttons (min-height 66px, `touch-action:none`, `user-select:none`, does not trigger scroll/zoom). Tap arena during dialog to continue.\n- Canvas scaled sharply per `devicePixelRatio` (max 2), CSS width 100%, aspect 16:9.\n- 360 px phone: no horizontal scroll, chapter grid 2 columns, level buttons 1 column, pad stays 3 columns.\n- `prefers-reduced-motion`: disable screen shake, reduce particle count to 1/3, disable CSS animations.\n\n# TECHNICAL\n- ONE file `index.html` (pure HTML+CSS+JS). No libraries, no build, no server/API/login. All images drawn with Canvas 2D. Sound synthesized with WebAudio. Ready for Netlify Drop.\n- CSS: use variables + reused classes (`.card`, `.btn`, `.tag`, `.note`, `.lv`, `.hud`, `.eq`, `.pad`, `.tools`, `.stats`, `.recap`, `.row`).\n- JS: one `state` object + render function per screen (`drawMenuPreview`, `drawCut`, `drawWorld`, `render`). Repeated markup via loops. Question data in a compact array `BANK[mudah|sulit][bab]`. Layout in array `LAYOUT`. No long comments.\n- `localStorage` wrapped in try/catch, keys `pf-best-mudah`, `pf-best-sedang`, `pf-best-sulit`.\n- Loop: `requestAnimationFrame`, fixed physics step 1/120 second, `dt` max 0.05.\n- Each chapter's background is drawn once to a backup canvas (width `W + (LEN-W)*0.5 + 4`, scale `SC`), then `drawImage` with parallax offset.\n- Ink drawing functions: `inkLine`, `wobRect`, `inkCircle`, `scratch`, `star4`, `hexPath`, `rrect`, `trace`, `stroke`. Seed changes `Math.floor(time*7)`.\n- Clawd illustration redrawn with Canvas: orange square body `#d8714f` with 1.5 px ink outline with short stroke shading `#a94c33`; two rectangular black eyes (mood happy = ^ ^ eyes, hurt = x eyes, blink = thin line); two short left-right arms; four legs alternating while walking. Happy expression on win.\n- Magnifying glass: glass circle `rgba(240,244,236,0.92)` + white glint + gold frame `#e2a93b` 4.2 px + ink line + wooden handle `#7a4a2a` 4.4 px.\n- Potted plant: green stem `#36561c` 4.2 px, 4 leaves (bezier shape, fill `#6fa83c`, vein `#dde8a6`, shading `#4c8128`), pot `#c4613f` with shading `#8f3e26`, pot rim `#cf6b46`.\n- Sun: circle `#f2a93b` with outline `#c9781f` + 12 rays `#e08a2c` rotating slowly.\n- Chapter1 background: green leaf `#6fa83c` full of strokes + pale veins `#dde8a6` containing water flow `#8cc8d6`. Chapter2: epidermis `#e2eac6` with puzzle-cell pattern (lines `#b5c68a`) with stomata (two green guard cells `#6fa83c`, dark slit `#132a1c`). Chapter3: chloroplast `#173826` with thylakoid stacks like solar panels `#3f8f4a` + yellow light beams. Chapter4: thylakoid membrane `#57b44e` with lipid rows `#a9dba0`, ATP synthase turbines, O₂ bubbles (two orange balls `#d9663f`) rising.\n- Enemies: aphid (ellipse `#7c9a3a` + legs), pollution smoke (three circles `#6d6a66`), spiky free radical (12-point star `#c9473a`).\n- Materials: water drop (drop shape `#8cc8d6`), CO₂ molecule (three circles: 2 orange `#d9663f` + 1 dark `#3b3434`), light mote (4-point star `#ffe9a0` + circle `#f2c14e`), glucose ring (hexagon `#f3e6c4`).\n\n# CHECK BEFORE FINISHING\n1. Game is playable from menu to results screen without errors.\n2. All correct answers are right (first option = correct answer, shuffled on display).\n3. No horizontal scroll on 360 px phone.\n4. `prefers-reduced-motion` disables shake.\n5. `localStorage` wrapped in try/catch.\n6. One file `index.html`, ready for Netlify Drop."},{"id":"sejarah-malaysia","kat":"kertas","katN":"Paper & ink","n":"Malaysian History Wander","mapel":"History","jenjang":"Year 4 – Form 3","topik":"Malaysian history: Malacca Malay Sultanate, colonization, 1957 independence, 1963 formation of Malaysia","img":"img/sejarah-malaysia.jpg","preview":"https://preview.edugamelabs.com/kertas-tinta/games/sejarah-malaysia/","prompt":"# ROLE\n- You are an art director + lead developer. Rebuild the 2D educational platformer game \"Pengembaraan Sejarah Malaysia\" in ONE index.html file (pure HTML+CSS+JS, Canvas 2D, no libraries, no build).\n- Product language: Malay (all UI text, dialogue, questions, buttons). This prompt is in Indonesian.\n\n# PRODUCT\n- Title: \"Pengembaraan Sejarah Malaysia\". Genre: story-driven platformer with 4 chapters, subject: Malaysian History (Malay Sultanate of Malacca, colonization, independence 1957, formation of Malaysia 1963).\n- Grade level: Year 4 – Form 3. Character: Clawd (walking orange square) holding the Time Lens (a magnifying glass with a gold frame carved with a clock) to travel through time.\n- 3 difficulty levels: Pengembara Cilik (Year 4–6), Pengembara Hebat (mixed), Ahli Sejarah Muda (Form 1–3).\n- 4 chapters: 1400 Pelabuhan Melaka · 1511 Kota A Famosa · 1957 Jalan ke Merdeka · 1963 Malaysia Terbentuk.\n- Screen flow: Menu → Play (4 chapters in sequence) → Results. 3 lives, fully refilled each chapter.\n\n# VISUAL STYLE\n- Palette (write once, refer by name): --paper:#efebe2 (paper background) · --paper-2:#faf8f2 (card) · --ink:#2e2620 (ink) · --muted:#6d665b · --line:#d6d0c3 · --accent:#d8714f (Clawd orange) · --accent-dark:#b4553a · --navy:#142a6b · --red:#c8102e · --gold:#e8b31f · --gold-d:#a67c00 · --leaf-dark:#3f6b22.\n- Canvas palette: INK #2e2620, PAPER #efebe2, PAPER2 #faf8f2, CL #d8714f, CL_H #a94c33, RED #c8102e, NAVY #142a6b, GOLD #f2c21b, GOLD_D #a67c00, SEA #5fa7bf, SEA_L #bfe3ec, WOOD #a8703f, WOOD_D #6b4423, LAT #b9784a, LAT_D #8a5332, LAND #8fbf5a, LAND_D #4f7f2a, GRASS #6fa83c, SOIL #8a5a35.\n- Google Fonts: Source Serif 4 (400;700) titles/questions/numbers · Caveat (600;700) handwriting & sound words · IBM Plex Mono (400;500) capital labels · Geist (400;600;800) buttons/UI.\n- All shapes drawn as hand-drawn ink lines: lines split every ±9 px, each point randomly offset slightly (seeded hash), randomization changes 7×/second (\"boil\" effect). Shadows = thin diagonal hatching (scratch), not blur.\n- Cards: bg --paper-2, border 1.5px solid --ink, radius 12px, padding 20px. Buttons: border 1.5px --ink, radius 8px, padding 12px 14px, hover bg #fff, active translateY(2px). Primary: bg --accent, text #fff, hover --accent-dark.\n- Soft radial vignette + paper grain (128px noise pattern alpha 0–24). No colorful gradients.\n- Large italic orange sound words: \"TING!\", \"SPLAT!\", \"DOR!\", \"BAM!\", \"PLOK!\", \"AUW!\". Correct → 14 rays + 4-point stars + paper scraps + small shake + \"+points\" mono rising. Wrong → ink + ink drops + thin dark flash. Streak ≥3 → handwritten \"beruntun x3\".\n\n# SCREENS & LAYOUT\n- Menu (card): mono capital label \"Sejarah · Malaysia · pengembaraan platformer\"; 300px preview canvas aspect 3/2 (Malacca map + Clawd + Time Lens + waving Jalur Gemilang); H1 \"Pengembaraan Sejarah Malaysia\" (span \"Sejarah Malaysia\" underlined with wavy orange SVG); 1-sentence description; grid of 4 chapters (1400/1511/1957/1963, red serif numbers); 3 difficulty buttons with best scores; handwritten note \"4 bab, 8 teka-teki, kumpul khazanah sejarah!\".\n- Play: mono capital HUD (Bab 1/4 · ♥♥♥ red · Khazanah 0 · Markah 0); timeline of 5 dots (1400 Melaka → 1511 Penjajahan → 1957 Merdeka → 1963 Malaysia → kini Kita) lit when chapter completes; large serif question above arena with wavy orange underline; 16:9 canvas arena; Clawd dialogue (bottom-left card, \"ketik untuk teruskan ▸\"); chapter card (center dialog: tag, red year, title, fact, navy handwritten goal, button \"Mula meneroka ▸\"); toast; button pad ◀ ▶ LOMPAT (min 66px); tools (kbd hint + \"Bunyi: hidup\" + \"Keluar\").\n- Results: difficulty tag, H2 \"Pengembaraan tamat!\", 3 gold stars (★ 42px, off --line), message, 3 stats (Markah / Betul kali pertama / Khazanah dikumpul), 4-line timeline recap, best score, buttons \"Main lagi\" + \"Cuba lagi bab ini\" (on loss) + \"Tukar tahap\".\n\n# MECHANICS\n- Logic canvas 480×270 (16:9), GROUND=226, LEN=1600, background parallax 0.5. Fixed-step physics 1/120 second.\n- Player: w30 h28, walk speed ±150 px/s, gravity ~1400, jump ~-420, coyote time, jump buffer, squash & stretch on jump/land.\n- 2 question gates per chapter: locked wall \"?\" + 3 answer blocks A/B/C hit from below. Correct → \"TING!\", red-blue-yellow confetti, gate splits (0.6s animation), explanation; wrong → \"SPLAT!\", life −1, block turns hatched ash + cross mark.\n- Small enemies per chapter (crab/rat/beetle/monitor lizard): stomp from above = \"PLOK!\" +5, hit = life −1 + blinking invulnerability.\n- Treasures per chapter: 8–10 items (star anise/scroll/14-point star/map fragment) with \"ting!\" +10.\n- Large lens at chapter end (PORTAL_X=1532) → gold circle transition → \"BAB TAMAT!\" (\"MERDEKA!\" in chapter 3, 7 shouts sound) → timeline lights up.\n- Score: item +10, correct answer +50, stomp enemy +5. Stars: 3 if wrong ≤1, 2 if ≤3, 1 if >3.\n\n# LEVELS & QUESTIONS\n- Question bank 3 levels × 4 chapters × 4 questions = 48 questions. Each chapter takes 2 questions (easy/hard: random 2 of 4; medium: 1 easy + 1 hard). Options shuffled, key = index 0 before shuffle.\n- EASY Chapter 1: (1) Founder of Malacca? → Parameswara (not Tunku/Francis Light). (2) Malacca named after? → tree. (3) Malacca famous as? → port. (4) Most sought-after goods? → spices.\n- EASY Chapter 2: (1) Malacca fell to Portuguese in? → 1511. (2) Portuguese fort? → A Famosa. (3) After Portuguese? → Dutch. (4) Francis Light opened? → Penang.\n- EASY Chapter 3: (1) Independence? → 31 August 1957. (2) Father of Independence? → Tunku Abdul Rahman. (3) \"Merdeka!\" how many times? → 7. (4) Where declared? → Stadium Merdeka.\n- EASY Chapter 4: (1) Malaysia formed? → 16 September 1963. (2) Flag? → Jalur Gemilang. (3) Number of states? → 13. (4) National anthem? → Negaraku.\n- HARD Chapter 1: (1) Malacca founded? → 1400. (2) Wise Bendahara? → Tun Perak. (3) Chinese Admiral? → Cheng Ho. (4) Port manager? → Syahbandar.\n- HARD Chapter 2: (1) Dutch controlled Malacca? → 1641. (2) 1824 Treaty? → Anglo-Dutch. (3) Straits Settlements: Penang, Malacca, ? → Singapore. (4) Portuguese commander? → Alfonso de Albuquerque.\n- HARD Chapter 3: (1) Japanese occupation? → 1941–1945. (2) 1946 British plan opposed? → Malayan Union. (3) UMNO 1946 led by? → Dato' Onn Jaafar. (4) Federation of Malaya? → 1948.\n- HARD Chapter 4: (1) Jalur Gemilang how many stripes? → 14. (2) Borneo states joined? → Sabah & Sarawak. (3) Singapore left? → 1965. (4) Rukun Negara? → 1970.\n- Each question has a 1-sentence explanation (why). Shuffled without repeats within a session.\n- Chapter layout (ground [x0,x1], platforms [x,y,w], enemies [a,b]):\n  - Chapter 1: ground [0,330][372,700][742,1100][1142,1600]; platforms [140,174,60][250,150,52][470,168,64][600,142,56]; enemies [420,650].\n  - Chapter 2: ground [0,300][344,520][564,700][742,1100][1144,1600]; platforms [120,172,62][300,150,58][420,170,58][596,148,62]; enemies [150,250][380,480].\n  - Chapter 3: ground [0,262][304,462][508,700][742,1100][1144,1600]; platforms [110,170,56][220,142,52][380,162,60][520,150,60][636,174,52]; enemies [320,430][540,650].\n  - Chapter 4: ground [0,282][326,482][528,700][742,1100][1146,1600]; platforms [130,164,58][258,136,52][400,162,58][560,144,58]; enemies [140,240][350,440][560,660].\n- GATE_X=[770,1172], PORTAL_X=1532.\n- Background per chapter (drawn once to offscreen canvas, parallax 0.5):\n  - Chapter 1 Malacca: warm sky #f3e2bd→#f7efdb, orange sun, green hills, stilted Malay houses, coconut trees, sea #5fa7bf, jong ship with red sail, Malacca tree.\n  - Chapter 2 A Famosa: dusk #f2cf9f→#f8ead2, roofless St. Paul's church, laterite walls #b9784a, cannons, Porta de Santiago, red Stadthuys #9e3b2c, dark green moat.\n  - Chapter 3 1941–1957: sky #d9e8ef→#f4efe2, rubber plantation (trunks + white cups), kampung houses, Stadium Merdeka (dome + red/blue/yellow/white pennants).\n  - Chapter 4 1963: sky #dfece2→#f4f0e2, Mount Kinabalu #8fa5b3, rainforest, longhouse, sea, hornbill (black body, yellow beak, red eye).\n- Malaysia map drawn from actual longitude/latitude coordinates: x=(longitude−99.6)×5, y=(7.2−latitude)×5. Peninsula + Borneo, 13 labeled states, Mount Kinabalu, compass rose, \"PETA MALAYSIA\" serif.\n- Jalur Gemilang: 14 red/white stripes, blue canton #010066, gold crescent + 14-point star #fc0. Waved slice by slice (sine wave).\n\n# MOTION, FEEDBACK & SOUND\n- Cards pop in (ease-out cubic 0.4s), character squash & stretch, hitstop ±60ms on hit, slow-moving clouds, orange sun with ray lines.\n- Chapter transitions: gold circle expanding (0.9s duration, ease), old canvas snapshot zoomed 5×.\n- WebAudio synthesized sound (no files): jump (320→640Hz triangle 0.13s), land (130→80Hz), ting (1760Hz sine + 2637Hz), bump (170→100Hz), correct (523/659/784/1047/1319Hz triangle arpeggio), wrong (220→90Hz sawtooth), stomp (440→70Hz), hurt (330→80Hz), open (392/523/659Hz sine), zoom (200→1600Hz sine 0.9s), clear (8 rising notes), merdeka (7× 392+523Hz), over (392/330/262/196Hz descending).\n- Background music: pentatonic arpeggio + soft drums, 100 BPM, key changes each chapter (PROG 4 bars × 4 keys, ARP [0,1,2,3,2,1,2,1]).\n- \"Bunyi: hidup/mati\" button toggles muted.\n\n# CONTROLS & RESPONSIVE\n- Keyboard: ← → / A D walk, Space / ↑ / W jump, Enter continue dialogue.\n- Mobile: large ◀ ▶ LOMPAT buttons (min 66px, touch-action none, no scroll/zoom trigger), pointer capture.\n- Tap stage to continue dialogue. Window blur → clear input + stop music.\n- Responsive on 360px phones without horizontal scroll. prefers-reduced-motion: disable shake, reduce particles, seed=0.\n\n# TECHNICAL\n- ONE index.html file (pure HTML+CSS+JS; no libraries, no build, no server/API/login). All images drawn with Canvas 2D code. WebAudio synthesized sound.\n- Logic canvas 480×270, scaled sharply per devicePixelRatio (max 2). Fixed-step physics 1/120 second.\n- localStorage wrapped in try/catch: keys \"sm-best-mudah\", \"sm-best-sedang\", \"sm-best-sulit\" (best score per difficulty).\n- Token-efficient: CSS variables + reused classes (.card, .btn, .tag, .note, .muted, .hud, .eq, .pad, .tools, .stats, .recap, .row); one state object + render function per screen; repeated markup via loops; data in compact arrays (BANK, CHAPTERS, LAYOUT, NEGERI); no long comments; write complete code directly without explanation.\n- Netlify Drop ready. Game is played by the player themselves (DO NOT auto-play; only optional internal test hook).\n- Structure: util (ri/rf/pick/shuffle/approach/clamp/ease/eOut/ov/store/rng), audio (toneAt/tone/SFX/musTick), ink drawing tools (hsh/jt/trace/stroke/inkLine/wobRect/inkCircle/scratch/star4/starPath/rrect/grain/paperBg), FLAG (Jalur Gemilang canvas), drawFlag/flagPole, map (ll/PEN/BOR/NEGERI/mapPoly/drawMap/drawMapSheet), drawClawd/drawLens/drawSun, CHAPTERS/BANK/LAYOUT, state/player/world, buildChapter/makeGate/pickQs, buildBg (4 chapters), emit/rings/rays/sparkles/drops/confetti/sfxText/scoreText/doShake, hudUpdate/eqLight/setQ, update/render/drawWorld/drawGround/drawPlat/drawItem/drawAmbient/drawWall/drawBlock/drawEnemy/drawPortal/drawPart/drawText, endGame/retryChapter/refreshBest, drawMenuPreview, fit, frame, input handlers.\n\n# CHECK BEFORE FINISHING\n1. Game is playable from menu to results screen without errors.\n2. All answer keys are correct (index 0 before shuffle).\n3. No horizontal scroll on 360px phones.\n4. 4 chapters in sequence, 2 question gates per chapter, 3 lives, timeline lights up.\n5. localStorage best score per difficulty saved (try/catch).\n6. prefers-reduced-motion disables shake.\n7. Netlify Drop ready, one file, no external dependencies except Google Fonts."},{"id":"arena-clawd","kat":"besar","katN":"3D & big","n":"Clawd Arena","mapel":"Math","jenjang":"Grade 2 – 6","topik":"Basic arithmetic: addition, subtraction, multiplication, division","img":"img/arena-clawd.jpg","preview":"https://preview.edugamelabs.com/arena-clawd/","prompt":"# ROLE\n- Art director + lead developer of 2D Canvas educational games; writes single-file replica prompts for other AIs.\n- Output: a 3-lane arena game in \"paper & ink\" style in **Malay** (all UI text, dialogue, questions, item names, monster names in Malay), one file `index.html`.\n\n# PRODUCT\n- Title: **Arena Clawd** — 3-lane arena (solo MOBA) + quick math questions.\n- Subject: Mathematics. Topic: basic arithmetic operations (addition, subtraction, multiplication, division). Grade level: elementary school grades 2–6.\n- Character: **Clawd** (orange square with two eyes, short arms, four legs, ink-line style). Enemy: **Raja Comot** (blue ink king with teeth, gold crown, purple scepter).\n- Win: destroy 6 enemy towers → defeat Raja Comot. Lose: Clawd's base is destroyed.\n- Product language: **Malay** (examples: \"Masuk arena\", \"Kedai\", \"Jeda\", \"Main semula\", \"Tukar hero\", \"Sambung\", \"Cuba lagi\", \"Betul!\", \"Jawapannya\").\n\n# VISUAL STYLE\n- Palette (refer to these names throughout the prompt):\n  - `--paper:#efebe2` page background; `--paper2:#faf8f2` cards/panels; `--ink:#2e2620` ink lines & text; `--muted:#6d665b`; `--line:#d6d0c3`\n  - `--accent:#d8714f` (Clawd orange, primary buttons); `--accent-dark:#b4553a`; `--leaf:#6fa83c`; `--leaf-dark:#3f6b22`; `--gold:#e2a93b`; `--enemy:#2c3e6b` (enemy ink blue)\n  - Canvas colors: `INK #2e2620`, `PAPER #efebe2`, `PAPER2 #faf8f2`, `GOLD #e2a93b`, `CL #d8714f`, `CL_H #a94c33`, `NAVY #2c3e6b`, `PLUM #5a2d58`, `SKY #6fa8dc`\n- Google Fonts: `Source Serif 4` (400;700) headings, `Geist` (400;600;800) UI, `Caveat` (600;700) handwriting, `IBM Plex Mono` (400;500) HUD/numbers.\n- Style: cream paper + wobbly ink lines (functions `wobRect`, `inkCircle`, `scratch` with hash jitter). Diagonal hatching for shadows. Comic-style sound words.\n- Map: grass `#dfe5c6` + grain noise; dirt lanes `#ecd9ae` with dashed lines; diagonal ink river `#bcd8e3` with white streaks; round trees `#8cb35a`/`#7aa64c` with highlight `rgba(220,240,170,.5)`.\n- Clawd base circle `#f6d1bd` outline `#d8714f`; Raja Comot's Palace circle `#c9d2e8` outline `#2c3e6b`. Caveat handwriting labels 40px `rgba(46,38,32,.45)`: \"Pangkalan Clawd\", \"Istana Raja Comot\", \"~ sungai dakwat ~\".\n- Phone-style round buttons: ATTACK orange `--accent` white text; skill white with icon; ultimate `--gold`; large cooldown number above buttons on cooldown; joystick transparent circle with dashed outline.\n- Question card: `.paper` white paper, border 1.5px `--ink`, radius 14px, `box-shadow:6px 6px 0 rgba(46,38,32,.85)`, animation `drop .42s cubic-bezier(.2,1.4,.4,1)`.\n\n# SCREENS & LAYOUT\nOrder: **Menu → Play → (Shop / Question / Pause as sheets) → Win / Lose**.\n\n**1. Menu** (`#menu`, `.card` white paper, border 1.5px ink, radius 12px, padding 20px, gap 18px), from top:\n- `.brand`: left `<canvas id=\"heroCv\">` 220×220 (aspect 1, border 1.5px ink, radius 10px, background `#dfe5c6`) showing mini-map animation + selected hero Clawd walking + Raja Comot; right: mono tag \"Arena 3 lorong · Main seorang · Matematik asas\", `<h1>Arena Clawd</h1>` clamp(36px,7vw,58px), paragraph: \"Raja Comot mahu tawan pangkalan Clawd! Pilih hero, pilih battle spell, kemudian turun ke lorong. Kumpul syiling, beli item di kedai, buru **Kelomang** dan buff hutan, runtuhkan menara, dan tumbangkan **Raja Comot**.\" + `.note` Caveat 22px `--accent-dark`: \"Sesekali soalan kilat muncul. Jawab betul, dapat kuasa!\"\n- Step 01 \"Pilih hero\": grid of 3 cards (`.heroes`, 3 columns; ≤760px 1 column). Each card: canvas 84×84 Clawd icon, mono uppercase role, serif name 19px, `<ul>` 3 skills.\n- Step 02 \"Pilih battle spell\": grid 5 columns (≤760px 2 columns), each button: 22px icon, 15px name, 13px text.\n- `.how` grid 4 columns (≤760px 2): \"Gerak & serang\", \"Naik tahap\", \"Hutan\", \"Menang\" (dashed ink border, radius 8px).\n- `.start`: level segment (2 buttons: \"Mudah · tambah & tolak\" / \"Sederhana · + − × ÷\"), `.primary` button \"Masuk arena ▸\", best score mono text.\n\n**2. Play** (`#game`): `.stage` height `min(80vh,700px)` min 440px, border 1.5px ink, radius 12px, background `#dfe5c6`, `<canvas id=\"cv\">` absolute inset 0. Top right: ⏸ and 🔊 buttons (44×44, background `rgba(250,248,242,.92)`). Toast at top center (animation `tin .3s`). Below stage: `.hint` Caveat 19px `--accent-dark`: \"Ikut askar Clawd kecil ke lorong. Jangan lupa buru Kelomang di sungai untuk tambah nyawa!\"\n\n**3. Sheet** (`#sheet` fixed inset 0, background `rgba(46,38,32,.45)`, grid center) containing `.paper` (max 560px, radius 14px, padding clamp(16px,4vw,26px), scroll). Used for: Shop, Quick question, Pause, Win, Lose.\n\n**4. Win**: \"MENANG!\" stamp (border 4px `--leaf-dark`, rotate -6deg, animation `stamp .5s`), 3 stars 46px `--gold` (off ones `--line`), `<h2>Raja Comot tumbang! Pangkalan Clawd selamat.</h2>`, 2-column stats grid (Time, Minions defeated, Enemy towers destroyed x/6, Forest monsters, Correct questions x/y, Clawd level), score, \"Main semula\" + \"Tukar hero\" buttons, confetti.\n\n**5. Lose**: \"KALAH\" stamp (`--accent-dark`), `<h2>Pangkalan Clawd ditawan</h2>`, tips, \"Cuba lagi\" + \"Tukar hero\" buttons.\n\n# MECHANICS\n- World 2000×2000, camera follows hero, only visible objects are drawn.\n- 3 lanes: `atas` (bottom-left → top-left → top-right), `tengah` (diagonal), `bawah` (bottom-right → top-right). Diagonal river from (260,260) to (1740,1740).\n- Clawd base (190,1810); Raja Comot's Palace (1810,190).\n- 6 enemy towers (2 per lane: outer hp 1900, inner hp 2600, range 300) + 3 of our towers (hp 2400) + our core (hp 4500, range 320).\n- Inner towers are invulnerable until the outer tower of the same lane is destroyed. Raja Comot is invulnerable until one lane is cleared.\n- Minion wave every 28 seconds: 4 minions per lane per team (3 melee + 1 ranged), staggered spawn 0.7s. Melee HP 280, ranged 190; dmg 18/24; spd 105.\n- Coins: enemy minions +28 (hero kill) / +12 (our minion kill); towers +220; monsters: Kelomang 60, Kumbang/Siput 110, Penyu 260. Passive +1.6 coins/second.\n- XP: minions 34/22, towers 160, monsters 30/80/160. Level 1–15, requires `90 + lvl*60` XP. Level 4 unlocks ultimate.\n- 3 heroes:\n  - **Clawd Pahlawan** (Fighter · melee, orange `#d8714f`, hp 1150, atk 58, range 95, cd 0.75, spd 255): Terjah Pensel (cd 6), Pusing Puting (cd 9), Hentakan Bumi (cd 30, ultimate).\n  - **Clawd Pemanah** (Marksman · ranged, yellow `#f2c14e`, hp 860, atk 52, range 270, cd 0.62, spd 250): Panah Tinta (cd 5), Langkah Angin (cd 8), Hujan Panah (cd 28).\n  - **Clawd Ahli Sihir** (Mage · skill power, blue `#7f9fd9`, hp 820, atk 46, range 235, cd 0.85, spd 245, sp 1.25): Bola Bintang (cd 4), Rantai Kilat (cd 8), Hujan Bintang (cd 30).\n- Skills level up (max 5, ultimate max 3 requires level 4/8/12). Yellow + button above skill when points available.\n- 5 battle spells (choose 1 before playing): Kilas ⚡ (cd 40, teleport 240px), Pulih 💚 (cd 50, +30% hp), Hukuman 🗡 (cd 30, 650+lvl*40 to monsters / 500 to minions), Pecut 👟 (cd 45, +60% spd 5s), Perisai 🛡 (cd 50, shield 30% 4s).\n- Shop 8 items (max 6, game pauses when opened): Pedang Pensel 🗡 300 (+22 atk), Kasut Lari 👟 250 (+40 spd), Jaket Kertas 🧥 300 (+350 hp), Jam Pasir ⏳ 400 (cdr 15%), Tongkat Bintang 🪄 450 (sp +30%), Perisai Buku 📘 400 (dr 15%), Daun Penawar 🍃 450 (ls 12%), Busur Laju 🏹 350 (as 20%).\n- 🏠 Return to base button (3 seconds, cancels if moving/hit).\n- 4 forest monsters with buffs: Kelomang (hp 520, respawn 45s, +35% hp & speed 8s), Kumbang Merah (hp 1300, dmg 32, respawn 70s, red buff 70s = burning attack), Siput Biru (hp 1300, dmg 28, respawn 70s, blue buff 70s = skill cd −25%), Penyu Dakwat (hp 3200, dmg 60, appears at minute 1, respawn 120s, shield 40% + turtle buff 30s).\n- Quick question every 60–75 seconds (first at 50s): game pauses, correct answer = choose random buff from 5 (Kuasa Pensel +40% atk 25s, Kasut Ajaib +speed 25s, Perisai Kertas −50% dmg 25s, Pulih Penuh, Peti Syiling +200 coins).\n- When hero falls: question appears 0.9s later. Correct = revive immediately; wrong = wait for countdown (6 + lvl*0.6 seconds).\n- Large Caveat 38px banners: \"Tiga Sekaligus!\" (3 minions within 2.5s), \"Ganas! Lima minion!\" (5), \"Menara musuh runtuh! (x/6)\", \"Buff Merah! Serangan membakar 🔥\", \"Buff Biru! Skill cepat sedia 💧\", \"Penyu Dakwat tumbang! Perisai + syiling 🐢\", \"Ultimate terbuka! <nama>\".\n- Final score: `kills*20 + towers*300 + monsKilled*80 + correct*150 + max(0,1000-t)*2`. Stars: 1 base + 1 if deaths ≤1 + 1 if question accuracy ≥75%.\n\n# LEVELS & QUESTIONS\n- **Mudah** level: addition & subtraction. **Sederhana**: addition, subtraction, multiplication, division.\n- Questions generated randomly (not a static bank) with rules:\n  - Easy addition: a,b ∈ 1–9, a+b ≤ 10, displayed with emoji visuals (🍎⭐🐟🍬🌼🎈) `a emoji + b emoji`.\n  - Easy subtraction: a ∈ 4–18, b ∈ 1–min(9,a−1), if a ≤ 10 display visuals (a−b emoji + b emoji crossed out).\n  - Medium addition: a ∈ 11–59, b ∈ 5–39. Medium subtraction: a ∈ 30–99, b ∈ 8–29.\n  - Multiplication: a ∈ {2,3,4,5,10}, b ∈ 1–9. Division: b ∈ {2,3,4,5}, result ∈ 1–9, a = b×result.\n- Question format: `<text> = ?` (examples \"7 + 5 = ?\", \"12 − 4 = ?\", \"3 × 6 = ?\", \"20 ÷ 4 = ?\").\n- Choices: 3 (easy) or 4 (medium), correct answer + distractors from `ans ± {1,2,3,10}` (non-negative, non-duplicate), shuffled.\n- Key examples (verify): 7+5=**12**; 9+1=**10**; 12−4=**8**; 15−7=**8**; 3×6=**18**; 5×9=**45**; 10×4=**40**; 20÷4=**5**; 18÷3=**6**; 35÷5=**7**; 24+17=**41**; 63−28=**35**.\n- Correct feedback: \"Betul! <buff name> <icon>\" or \"Betul! Clawd bangkit sekarang.\" Wrong: \"Jawapannya <ans>. Tak apa, teruskan berjuang!\" (correct answer highlighted green `--leaf`).\n\n# MOTION, FEEDBACK & SOUND\n- CSS animations: `tin .3s ease-out` (toast), `drop .42s cubic-bezier(.2,1.4,.4,1)` (cards), `pop .4s` (correct answer), `shake .4s` (wrong answer, ±7px), `stamp .5s cubic-bezier(.2,1.6,.4,1)` (stamp), `conf 1s ease-out` (26 confetti pieces, random `--dx/--dy/--r`).\n- Canvas effects: floating damage numbers (rise 40px/second, life 0.9s), skill area circles, lightning (white+blue zigzag lines), falling stars, screen shake (`shake` 0.9 when tower destroyed, 1.4 when boss dies), particles `star/ink/paper/chip/smoke/fire/water`.\n- WebAudio sound (oscillator + 0.6s noise buffer):\n  - `shot` triangle 820→1200Hz 0.06s; `slash` noise lowpass 2600Hz + triangle 500→200Hz; `hit` square 220→120Hz; `pop` square 700→160Hz; `zap` sawtooth 1200→300Hz; `boom` noise 500Hz + sine 90→30Hz 0.6s; `dash` noise 3000Hz + sawtooth 300→900Hz; `spin` triangle 400/600/800/1000Hz staggered; `thunder` noise 4000Hz + sawtooth 1800→200Hz; `ult` sine 523/784/1047/1568Hz; `star` noise 1200Hz + sine 200→80Hz; `slam` noise 300Hz + sine 70→35Hz; `lvl` triangle 659/784/988/1319Hz; `coin` square 1568Hz + 2093Hz; `hurt` sawtooth 300→90Hz; `heal` sine 523/659/784Hz; `correct` triangle 523/659/784/1047/1319Hz; `wrong` sawtooth 220→90Hz; `win` triangle 8 ascending notes; `over` triangle 392/330/262/196Hz descending; `tap` sine 700→900Hz; `blink` sine 2000→400Hz.\n  - Background music: 126 BPM loop, chord progression `[[0,3,7],[8,12,15],[5,8,12],[7,11,14]]`, sine bass every 4 beats, triangle hi-hat every 2 beats.\n- 🔊/🔇 button toggle; `localStorage` key `arena-mute` = \"1\"/\"0\".\n\n# CONTROLS & RESPONSIVE\n- Touch: bottom-left joystick (radius 58px, knob 26px), large ATTACK button (r 46px) bottom-right, 3 skills (r 32px) above-left of ATTACK, spell (r 25px) left, return 🏠 (r 22px) above-left of spell. Buttons minimum 66px touch area.\n- Keyboard: WASD/arrows move, J/Space attack, Q/E/R skills, F spell, B return, I shop, P/Esc pause. Ctrl/Shift + Q/E/R level up skill.\n- `touch-action:none`, `user-select:none`, `preventDefault` on pointerdown; `setPointerCapture`.\n- Responsive: 360px phone without horizontal scroll; `padding-left/right: max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-*))`; menu grid drops to 1–2 columns at ≤760px; HUD scale `u = clamp(0.78, min(CW,CH)/430, 1.25)`.\n- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` → disable animations `.paper, .stamp, .confetti i, .toast`.\n\n# TECHNICAL\n- ONE file `index.html` (pure HTML+CSS+JS). No libraries, no build, no server/API/login, no external images/audio — everything drawn on `<canvas>` and synthesized with WebAudio.\n- Google Fonts via `<link>` (Source Serif 4, Caveat, IBM Plex Mono, Geist). Favicon SVG data-URI (orange square + 2 eyes + 4 legs).\n- Map drawn once to offscreen canvas 2000×2000 (`MAP`), then `drawImage`; minimap 220×220 (`MINI`). Grain noise 128×128 via `createPattern`.\n- Camera follows hero, culls objects outside viewport. `DPR = min(2, devicePixelRatio)`.\n- Simple AI: minions walk lanes & attack nearest, towers shoot targets in range (prioritize minions), Raja Comot summons extra waves every 10s + slam every 4s.\n- `localStorage` wrapped in try/catch: `arena-best` (score), `arena-mute`.\n- Token-efficient: CSS variables + reused classes (`.card`, `.paper`, `.pick`, `.opts`, `.stats`, `.shop`, `.bag`); one `G` object (state) + render function per screen (`renderShop`, `ask`, `win`, `lose`, `pause`); repeated markup via loops (`HEROES`, `SPELLS`, `ITEMS`, `MONSTERS`); data in compact arrays; no long comments; write full code directly without explanation.\n- Ready for Netlify Drop.\n\n# PRE-FINISH CHECK\n1. Menu → select hero → select spell → select level → Enter arena → play → win/lose → Play again, without errors.\n2. All question answer keys correct (verify the 12 examples above).\n3. No horizontal scroll on 360px phone; touch buttons ≥66px; joystick & ATTACK do not overlap.\n4. Inner towers invulnerable until the outer tower of the same lane is destroyed; Raja Comot invulnerable until one lane is cleared.\n5. Quick question appears every 60–75s and when hero falls; correct answer = buff/revive, wrong = countdown.\n6. WebAudio sound works, 🔊/🔇 button functions, `arena-mute` is saved.\n7. `prefers-reduced-motion` disables CSS animations.\n8. All UI text in Malay; monster, item, skill, spell names match the list."},{"id":"vesper","kat":"besar","katN":"3D & big","n":"Water Mission","mapel":"Science","jenjang":"Grade 5 – Middle School","topik":"Water cycle and causes of flooding","img":"img/vesper.jpg","preview":"https://preview.edugamelabs.com/vesper-misi-air/","prompt":"# ROLE\nYou are an art director + lead developer of web games. Rebuild **Misi Air** — a 3D isometric voxel horror educational science game themed around the water cycle & floods — in ONE `index.html` file that can be played directly in the browser without build/server. The result must be almost 100% similar to the specification below.\n\n# PRODUCT\n- Title: **Misi Air** · Subject: Science · Topic: Water cycle & causes of floods · Level: Grade 5 Elementary – Middle School.\n- Language inside the game: **Indonesian** (short, clear sentences).\n- Genre: atmospheric 3D isometric voxel horror, flooded city during night rain, wet road reflections, neon lights, flashlight as the only tool.\n- Flow: Menu → Chapter card → Play → Notes+Questions → Results/Ending.\n- Goal: collect **7 scientist notes** in the sunken city; each note unlocks material + 1 multiple-choice question; correct answer = flashlight battery +25%.\n\n# VISUAL STYLE\n- Palette (CSS var + Three.js colors):\n  - `--bg:#07090c` background; `--ink:#c8ccd0` primary text; `--ink2:#9aa0a6` secondary; `--ink3:#7d848a` dim.\n  - `--cream:#e6e1d6` bright accent; `--cream2:#d8d2c4`; `--gold:#e6d29a` battery/score; `--amber:#fff3d8` lightning.\n  - `--paper:#e8e0cc` note paper; `--paperInk:#2a2622`; `--paperHead:#6a5a48`; `--paperFoot:#8a7a68`.\n  - `--phoneBg:#0b0d10`; `--phoneInk:#cfe4ff`; `--phoneHead:#6f8aa8`; `--phoneFoot:#4f6a88`; `--phoneBorder:rgba(160,200,255,.25)`.\n  - `--danger:#d8503a` low battery; `--neonPink:#ff5fa0`; `--neonCyan:#5fe8ff`; `--neonRed:#ff3030`; `--neonGreen:#40ff70`.\n  - Asphalt `#1b1c20`/`#202226`, sidewalk `#4a4a48`/`#424240`, yellow line `#8a7a2a`, white `#9a9a92`, pit `#0a0908`.\n- Font: `\"Segoe UI\", system-ui, sans-serif` for HUD; `\"Courier New\", Courier, monospace` for note paper & phone.\n- Voxel: 1 voxel = 0.1 m; matte material (roughness .42, metalness .12), shiny (.35/.15), emit (MeshBasicMaterial), glass.\n- Fog: `fogColor 0x0a0d12` chapter 1, `0x0b0e14` chapter 3; near/far set per chapter.\n- All models from primitive shapes (BoxGeometry, ConeGeometry, PlaneGeometry) — no image files.\n\n# SCREENS & LAYOUT\nScreen order (top to bottom):\n1. **3D Canvas** full-screen (`100vw×100vh`, `touch-action:none`, cursor crosshair).\n2. **HUD** (fixed, pointer-events none):\n   - Top left `#title`: small label `IPA · siklus air & banjir` (12px, letter-spacing .32em, uppercase, `--ink2`), below it `<b>Misi Air</b>` (20px, letter-spacing .22em, `--cream`, text-shadow `0 0 18px rgba(255,200,140,.25)`), then `Skor IPA 0/7` (`--gold`).\n   - Top center `#objective` (13px, letter-spacing .18em, uppercase, `--cream2`, max-width 70vw, animation `objflash` 1.6s when changed).\n   - Top right `#stats`: `— fps` + `high` (11px, `--ink3`, tabular-nums).\n   - Bottom left `#hint`: `klik jalan / pakai · seret putar · scroll zoom · F senter · M suara` (12px, `--ink3`, keywords `--cream2`).\n   - Bottom right `#status`: battery bar 120×8px border `#6a7077` + fill `--gold` (transition width .3s linear, `.low` → `--danger` + blink .9s), 3 sanity diamonds (10×10px, rotate 45°, `--cream2`, `.off` transparent), 4 static bars (6px width, height 4/7/10/14px, `.on` → `--cream` + glow).\n3. **Prompt** `#prompt` (fixed, 12px, uppercase, `--amber`, bg `rgba(6,8,10,.75)`, border `1px solid rgba(255,240,220,.25)`, padding 4px 8px, opacity transition .15s).\n4. **Toast** `#toast` (fixed, bottom 84px, center, 14px, `--cream`, bg `rgba(6,8,10,.7)`, border-left 2px `#c8b890`, padding 8px 16px, opacity .4s).\n5. **Fade** `#fade` (fixed, bg #000, opacity .7s ease).\n6. **Chapter card** `#card` (grid center, opacity 1.2s): h1 44px letter-spacing .34em uppercase `--cream`; p 15px `--ink2` max-width 520px.\n7. **Note** `#note` overlay (bg `rgba(4,5,7,.55)`, opacity .35s): paper `.paper` width min(520px,86vw), bg `--paper`, color `--paperInk`, padding 34px 40px, box-shadow `0 30px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.8)`, rotate(-1.2deg), font Courier. h2 13px uppercase `--paperHead`; pre 15px line-height 1.65; `#quiz` grid gap 8px; answer button 14px padding 9px 12px bg `#f4ecd8` border `1px solid #a8987e`; `.ok` bg `#cfe8c4` border `#3f7a32`; `.no` bg `#f0c8bc` border `#9a3a2a`; small 11px uppercase `--paperFoot`.\n8. **Phone** `#call` overlay: `.phone` width min(560px,86vw), bg `--phoneBg`, color `--phoneInk`, padding 30px 38px, border `1px solid var(--phoneBorder)`, box-shadow `0 0 60px rgba(120,160,255,.15)`, font Courier. h2 12px letter-spacing .3em `--phoneHead`; pre 16px line-height 1.8 text-shadow glow.\n9. **Death** `#death` (bg #000, opacity .5s): p 18px uppercase `--cream2`.\n10. **Menu** `#menu` (bg `rgba(4,5,7,.62)`, opacity .6s): h1 52px letter-spacing .4em uppercase `--cream`; p 14px `--ink2` max-width 560px; button `Mulai`/`Lanjutkan` (14px uppercase letter-spacing .3em, border `1px solid rgba(236,230,216,.4)`, padding 12px 34px, hover bg `rgba(236,230,216,.1)`); `.controls` 12px `--ink3`.\n11. **Ending** `#ending` (same style as menu): h1 + p + `CLICK TO RETURN` (11px `#6a7077`).\n\n# MECHANICS\n- **Click to walk**: raycast to ground → destination point; character walks automatically (speed ~1.2 m/s), procedural walk animation (leg swing ±0.62 rad, knee 0.95 rad, left arm opposite, head look-around when idle).\n- **Drag** to rotate isometric camera (yaw/pitch), **scroll** zoom.\n- **Flashlight** (F): SpotLight `0xfff0d0`, intensity 320, distance 34, angle 0.42, penumbra 0.45, decay 2, castShadow 1024×1024, bias -0.002, normalBias 0.08. Volumetric cone beam (ray-march 10 steps, Gaussian radial, axial & ground fade).\n- **Battery**: 100% initial, decreases 0.55%/second when flashlight on; <25% → red bar + blink; 0% → flashlight off + toast \"Senter mati.\"; +25% per correct answer; +45% per battery pickup.\n- **Sanity**: 3 lives (diamonds). Hit by hazard/hollow → -1 + stinger; 0 → death screen 3.6s → restart chapter.\n- **Hollow (\"The Answered\")**: dark voxel figure (tone 0x0e1113, eyes 0xff5a48 emit 0.7), spawns at random point >12m from player, interval per chapter. States: `stalk` (chase, speed 1.25–1.65 ×1.7 if flashlight off ×1.3 if player facing away) → `creep` (at beam edge, speed 0.4) → `frozen` (at beam core, heat rises) → `burn` (heat > 4.6s, fades 1.4s) → `gone`. `lunge` when <5.5m & not illuminated (speed 3.8, 0.55s). Grab if <0.9m → -15% battery + hurt.\n- **Radio static**: level rises when hollow near (<18m), HUD bar lights up; heartbeat when sanity ≤1 (96 bpm) or hollow <6m (78 bpm).\n- **Flood**: value 0–1, transition animation to target; ground material changes to cold green-gray `vec3(0.05,0.085,0.095)`.\n- **Planar reflection**: render mirrored scene through y=0 to half-float render target, blur 2 passes (horizontal + vertical 2.2×), used by wet ground material with fresnel.\n- **Wet ground**: puddle mask from fbm noise, 3-layer rain ripple, step ripple (6 slots), per-vertex wetness (road 1, walk 0.55, block 0.25).\n\n# LEVELS & QUESTIONS\n**7 notes (NOTES)** — all with question & key:\n1. `p1` **Catatan 1 — Penguapan** (Tomas, hydrologist): \"Matahari memanaskan air laut, sungai, dan genangan. Air berubah wujud dari cair menjadi gas: uap air. Proses ini disebut EVAPORASI. Uap air naik karena lebih ringan dari udara di sekitarnya.\" → Q: \"Air berubah dari cair menjadi uap karena panas matahari. Proses ini disebut…\" A: **Evaporasi** (B: Kondensasi, C: Infiltrasi). Why: \"Evaporasi = penguapan, cair menjadi gas.\"\n2. `p2` **Catatan 2 — Awan terbentuk**: \"Makin tinggi, udara makin dingin. Uap air mendingin lalu berubah kembali menjadi titik-titik air kecil. Titik air berkumpul menjadi AWAN. Perubahan gas menjadi cair ini disebut KONDENSASI.\" → Q: \"Uap air yang mendingin menjadi titik air dan membentuk awan disebut…\" A: **Kondensasi** (B: Presipitasi, C: Evaporasi). Why: \"Kondensasi = pengembunan, gas menjadi cair.\"\n3. `p3` **Catatan 3 — Hujan turun**: \"Titik air di awan bergabung dan makin berat. Saat terlalu berat, air jatuh ke bumi sebagai hujan, salju, atau es. Ini disebut PRESIPITASI. Sudah empat puluh hari hujan tidak berhenti.\" → Q: \"Jatuhnya air dari awan ke bumi disebut…\" A: **Presipitasi** (B: Infiltrasi, C: Transpirasi). Why: \"Presipitasi = hujan, salju, atau es yang jatuh dari awan.\"\n4. `p4` **Log pompa — Stasiun 2** (Kell): \"Air hujan yang jatuh ke tanah ada dua jalan: 1. Meresap ke dalam tanah (INFILTRASI), mengisi air tanah. 2. Mengalir di permukaan (LIMPASAN) menuju selokan dan sungai. Aspal dan beton membuat air tidak bisa meresap.\" → Q: \"Air hujan yang meresap ke dalam tanah disebut…\" A: **Infiltrasi** (B: Limpasan, C: Evaporasi). Why: \"Infiltrasi = peresapan air ke dalam tanah.\"\n5. `p5` **Log pompa — penyebab banjir**: \"Kenapa kota ini tenggelam? - Waduk jebol setelah hujan deras berhari-hari. - Tanah tertutup aspal, air tidak meresap. - Selokan tersumbat sampah. - Pohon di hulu ditebang. Semua air mengalir ke jalan.\" → Q: \"Mana yang BUKAN penyebab banjir di kota?\" A: **Banyak taman dan pohon** (B: Selokan tersumbat sampah, C: Tanah tertutup aspal). Why: \"Taman dan pohon membantu air meresap, jadi justru mengurangi banjir.\"\n6. `p6` **Lembar rumah sakit**: \"Pompa air memindahkan air dari tempat rendah ke tempat yang lebih tinggi atau ke sungai. Pompa butuh energi listrik. Jangan pernah menyentuh kabel atau stopkontak saat lantai tergenang: air kotor menghantarkan listrik. Lantai tiga aman dari genangan.\" → Q: \"Mengapa berbahaya menyentuh stopkontak saat banjir?\" A: **Air kotor menghantarkan listrik** (B: Air membuat listrik padam selamanya, C: Stopkontak jadi dingin). Why: \"Air yang mengandung mineral dan kotoran adalah penghantar listrik.\"\n7. `p7` **Catatan perawat malam**: \"Cara mengurangi banjir: - Buat sumur resapan dan biopori. - Tanam pohon dan jaga hutan di hulu. - Buang sampah pada tempatnya. - Bangun waduk dan pompa yang dirawat. Lampu kapel menyala. Tomas pasti di sana.\" → Q: \"Lubang kecil di tanah untuk membantu air hujan meresap disebut…\" A: **Biopori** (B: Bendungan, C: Selokan). Why: \"Biopori = lubang resapan yang membantu air masuk ke tanah.\"\n\n**3 chapters (CHAPTERS)**:\n- **Chapter 1 `vesper`** \"Misi Air: Vesper Street\" — spawn [1.5,3.5], camYaw -0.62, fog 0x0a0d12, flood 0, hollows max 0. Objective: \"Capai Stasiun Pompa 2 di ujung timur jalan.\" Items: page p4 (11,5.8), page p5 (-5.5,6), 3 battery, valve (hidden, appears when trigger x12-21 z-9.5..-3). Interact: outflow valve (install wheel → pump on, flood 0, phone rings), station phone → call c2 → exit to east.\n- **Chapter 2** (cut in original code, still build with same structure: pump, spark hazard, 2 pages, 3 battery, valve puzzle).\n- **Chapter 3 `memorial`** \"Rumah Sakit Vesper\" — spawn [0,17], camYaw 0.1, fog 0x0b0e14, ambient 1.35, hollows max 4 interval 13. Objective: \"Cari Tomas. Lantai tiga, lalu kapel.\" Items: page p6 (-12.3,-1.6), page p7 (1.85,2.85), 2 battery, brass key (8.2,5.2). Interact: emergency entrance (chain), chapel door (needs key → open, ring), wall phone → call c3/c3b → ending.\n\n**Phone (CALLS)**:\n- `c1`: [\"…Nadia.\",\"Kamu datang.\",\"…Stasiun Pompa 2. Jalan Kedua.\",\"Baca semua catatanku. Jawab soalnya, senter kamu akan bertahan lebih lama.\",\"(suara air)\"]\n- `c2`: [\"…airnya surut, Nadia.\",\"Pompa bekerja: air dipindahkan ke sungai.\",\"Rumah sakit. Lantai tiga, lalu kapel.\",\"…cepat.\"]\n- `c3`: [\"…kamu membaca semuanya.\",\"Sekarang kamu paham siklus air.\",\"Tetap di bawah cahaya, Nadia.\"]\n- `c3b`: [\"…Nadia.\",\"Turun ke kapel.\",\"Masih ada catatan yang belum kamu baca.\"]\n\n**Ending**: `TIDE` (7/7) or `STATIC` (<7). TIDE text: \"She left the receiver hanging and walked back out into the rain.\\n\\nBehind her, every phone on Vesper Street stopped ringing at once.\\n\\nThe water forgot her name.\" STATIC: \"She answered. Of course she answered.\\n\\nOn Vesper Street, everyone answers eventually.\\n\\n(Read every torn page for the other ending.)\"\n\n# MOTION, FEEDBACK & SOUND\n- **Animation**: walk cycle phase += dt×(speed×3.6); bob hips 0.035×w; torso lean 0.08×w + breathing sin(t×1.4)×0.008; head look-around timer 1.5–5s target ±0.7 rad; flashlight random blink (0.012 + weak×0.08 probability).\n- **Chapter card**: fade in 0.7s → card show 5.5s → state play after 1.5s.\n- **Toast**: 4.5s default, 3s battery, 5s wrong answer.\n- **Note typewriter**: 60 cps, skip 15% chance +1 char.\n- **Phone**: lines appear every 900ms + 45ms/char; static 0.9 when active.\n- **Score**: `Skor IPA X/7` in HUD, updates on answer.\n- **Sound (Web Audio, all synthesized)**:\n  - Rain bed: noise lowpass 1400 + highpass 400, gain 0.11, LFO 0.07Hz ±0.025.\n  - Radio static: noise bandpass 2400 Q 0.6, gain 0.4×v².\n  - Neon hum: sawtooth 60Hz lowpass 180, gain 0.012.\n  - Thunder: burst lowpass 160–280Hz gain 0.5, decay 2.6–3.6s.\n  - Step: wet (lowpass 900 + highpass 200, gain 0.09, decay 0.16) / dry (highpass 700 + lowpass 3500, gain 0.05, decay 0.07).\n  - Pickup: tone 660→990Hz sine, gain 0.06, decay 0.12 + 990Hz delay 0.1.\n  - Zap: burst bandpass 3800 Q 1.5 gain 0.35 + square 110Hz lowpass 800 gain 0.12.\n  - Stinger: sawtooth 52Hz + 55.5Hz gain 0.35/0.3 decay 1.4 + burst bandpass 1200 + highpass 3000.\n  - Groan: triangle 70–82Hz gain 0.06 slide 58, decay 0.9.\n  - Burn: burst highpass 1800 gain 0.18 decay 1.2 + sine 240→90Hz.\n  - Shriek: sawtooth 180→620Hz gain 0.22 + burst bandpass 2600 Q 1.2.\n  - Heart: sine 56Hz gain 0.22 decay 0.16 + sine 50Hz delay 0.16 gain 0.16.\n  - Ring: square 440+480Hz gain 0.045 lowpass 1800, 2× per 3.6s.\n  - Voice: burst bandpass 900–1500 Q 2.5 gain 0.12, rhythm 0.08–0.3s.\n- **Mute button** (M): master gain 0/1 with setTargetAtTime 0.05.\n\n# CONTROLS & RESPONSIVE\n- **Desktop**: click = walk/use, drag = rotate camera, scroll = zoom, F = flashlight, M = sound.\n- **Mobile**: tap = walk/use, drag = rotate, pinch = zoom, flashlight & sound buttons in HUD.\n- Viewport: `width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no`.\n- Responsive layout: HUD uses `position:fixed` with inset; paper/phone `width:min(520px,86vw)`; no horizontal scroll at 360px.\n- `prefers-reduced-motion`: disable objflash animation, blink, card transition; reduce rain particles 50%.\n\n# TECHNICAL\n- **ONE `index.html` file** (pure HTML+CSS+JS). Library: only Three.js via importmap `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.169.0/build/three.module.js`. No build, no server, no API/login.\n- All images made with code (voxels from BoxGeometry, inline GLSL shaders). No external files.\n- `localStorage` key `vesper.save.v1` (JSON `{chapter, pages[]}`), wrapped in try/catch.\n- Ready for Netlify Drop (open `index.html` directly).\n- **Token-saving rules**: CSS variables + classes reused; one `state` object + `render` function per screen; repeated markup via loops; data in compact arrays; no long comments; write complete code directly without explanation.\n- Module structure in one file: `Sfx` (audio), `Vox`/`voxGroup` (voxel), `Character` (rig), `Hollow` (enemy), `makeRain`/`makeMist`/`makeGlows`/`makeBeam` (effects), `buildGround`/`makeWetMaterial`/`Reflection` (ground), `Game` (runtime), `CHAPTERS`/`NOTES`/`CALLS` (data).\n- Renderer: WebGLRenderer antialias, shadowMap PCFSoft, toneMapping ACESFilmic, outputColorSpace SRGB. Isometric camera OrthographicCamera with zoom.\n- Loop: `requestAnimationFrame`, delta clamp 0.05s, update all systems (player, hollows, flood, battery, HUD, sfx).\n\n# CHECK BEFORE FINISHING\n1. Game is playable from Menu → Chapter 1 → Notes+Questions → Chapter 3 → Ending without console errors.\n2. All 7 answer keys correct (Evaporasi, Kondensasi, Presipitasi, Infiltrasi, Banyak taman dan pohon, Air kotor menghantarkan listrik, Biopori).\n3. No horizontal scroll on 360px mobile.\n4. Flashlight can be turned on/off with F and button; battery drains when on; correct answer +25%.\n5. Hollow appears, can be frozen with flashlight, burned 4.6s, and grabs if close.\n6. Wet road reflection visible; rain falls; fog present.\n7. Sound works (rain, static, pickup, stinger); M button mutes.\n8. localStorage saves chapter & pages read; Continue button appears if save exists.\n9. `prefers-reduced-motion` reduces animation.\n10. Single `index.html` file ready to upload to Netlify Drop."},{"id":"restoran","kat":"besar","katN":"3D & big","n":"Profit Diner","mapel":"Math","jenjang":"Grade 3 – 6","topik":"Money, total bill, and change","img":"img/restoran.jpg","preview":"https://preview.edugamelabs.com/warung-untung/","prompt":"# ROLE\n- Art director + lead developer of a single-file 3D web educational game.\n- Rebuild \"Warung Untung\" EXACTLY as specified below, without copying any repo.\n- Language inside the product: Indonesian (short sentences, friendly for elementary school kids).\n\n# PRODUCT\n- Title: Warung Untung. Subject: Mathematics. Topic: money, total shopping, change.\n- Level: Elementary Grades 3–6. Genre: cozy 3D isometric roofed food-stall simulation.\n- Flow: Title → Play (day loop) → payment receipt panel → answer change → customer goes home → target 6/day → day increases.\n- Goal: cash increases, rating rises, correct answers are counted.\n\n# VISUAL STYLE\n- Color tokens (use as CSS var + Three material):\n  - --cream:#fbf3e4 (UI cards, kitchen walls)\n  - --ink:#22343c (text, button borders)\n  - --teal:#1f5f5b (receipt header, counter, icon brand)\n  - --terra:#d9734e (primary button, chairs, car)\n  - --gold:#f2b84b (progress bar, umbrella, car)\n  - --green:#4f9d69 (correct feedback, plants)\n  - --line:#e6d7bd (card border)\n  - bg:#f6d8b8 (sky/fog), road:#5d6066, wood:#c9844f, wood-line:#a96a3b, ground:#e9d6b6, sidewalk:#d8c7a6, lamp:#ffe08a, glass:#6f8fa3, building roof:#7a5a48, skin:#f1c9a0, hair:#6b4a2e, tire:#222, car-glass:#dfe8ec.\n- Google Fonts: Fredoka (500/600/700) for titles/numbers; Nunito (600/700/800) for body.\n- Radius: cards 16–22px, buttons 12–14px, stats 14px. Border 1.5px solid var(--line).\n- Card shadow: 0 8px 20px -12px rgba(0,0,0,.4); receipt panel: 0 16px 36px -16px rgba(0,0,0,.5); intro: 0 30px 60px -20px rgba(0,0,0,.5).\n- Option buttons: box-shadow 0 3px 0 var(--ink) (press effect). Intro button: 0 4px 0 #a54f30.\n- Mood: evening city, cars passing, customers walking, rounded UI cards.\n\n# SCREENS & LAYOUT\n- Fullscreen Three canvas behind all UI (position fixed, inset 0).\n- Top bar (fixed, left/right 16px, top 14px, flex gap 10px, pointer-events none):\n  - Brand: 🍜 icon in a 34×34 box radius 10 bg teal, text \"Warung Untung\" Fredoka 19px, sub \"MATEMATIKA · UANG\" 11px letter-spacing .12em color #7a6a58 uppercase.\n  - Spacer flex:1.\n  - 3 stat cards (bg cream, border line, radius 14, padding 6px 12px, Fredoka 17px): \"HARI\"→number, \"KAS\"→Rp0, \"RATING\"→★ 3.0. Small label Nunito 10px uppercase #7a6a58.\n- Target Panel (fixed left 16px top 84px, width 230px, cream card): label \"TARGET HARI INI\", title \"Layani 6 pelanggan\" Fredoka 17px, progress bar (h 8px radius 9 bg #efe2c9, gold fill transition width .4s), small text \"0/6 dilayani · 0 jawaban benar\".\n- Receipt Panel (fixed right 16px top 84px, width min(340px, calc(100vw-32px)), radius 18, overflow hidden, transform translateX(120%) → none when .on, transition .35s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1)):\n  - Teal header: left \"Meja N mau bayar\" Fredoka 16px, right 🧾.\n  - Body: item table (td padding 3px 0, right column tabular-nums), Total row (border-top 1.5px dashed line, bold 800), \"Uang pelanggan\" box (bg #fff radius 12 padding 8px 10px, flex space-between), question \"Berapa uang kembaliannya?\" Fredoka 17px, 3-column grid of option buttons, feedback area min-height 20px.\n- Bottom dock (fixed center bottom 16px, cream card radius 18 padding 6px, flex gap 6px): 4 chips \"🏗️ Bangun\" (active, bg teal white text), \"👩‍🍳 Tim\", \"📋 Menu\", \"📒 Buku kas\". Inactive chips ink text.\n- Intro Overlay (fixed inset 0, bg rgba(34,52,60,.35), grid center): cream card radius 22 padding 22 width min(420px,90vw) center; H1 \"Warung Untung\" Fredoka 30px; paragraph \"Pelanggan datang, makan, lalu membayar. Hitung total dan uang kembaliannya dengan benar supaya kas bertambah dan rating naik.\"; button \"Buka warung\" (bg terra, white text, Fredoka 17px, padding 12px 26px, radius 14).\n- Floating label above customer's head (.tag): bg #fff, border 1.5px ink, radius 12, padding 3px 8px, Nunito 700 12px, shadow 0 3px 0 ink, transform translate(-50%,-100%).\n- Floating coin text (.coin): Fredoka 700 18px, color #1f7a45 (correct) / #b5452c (wrong), text-shadow 0 2px 0 #fff, rise animation 1.4s ease-out then disappear.\n\n# MECHANICS\n- World: ground 140×140, asphalt road width 8 at z=-17 and x=-17, center line markings every 6 units, sidewalk 26×26, stall deck 20×20 wood, plant fence around, teal kitchen+counter, signboard \"WARUNG UNTUNG\" (canvas texture, teal bg, cream text).\n- 4 round tables (cream top radius 1.1, wood legs, 2 terra chairs, gold 8-sided cone umbrella, white pole). Table positions: (-4,-2), (-4,5), (2,5), (-4,9.5).\n- String lights: 10 small #ffe08a bulbs at y≈4.6 along x -8..10.\n- City: 9 box buildings with random colors from palette [0xe7a477,0xe9c99d,0x8fb4a8,0xd88f74,0xf1dcb6,0x9fb0c4], emissive glass windows, roof #7a5a48. 10 trees (wood trunk + green icosahedron).\n- 5 cars colors [gold, white, terra, teal, gold] passing on 2 lanes, speed 6–10 units/second, loop 140 units.\n- Customers: spawn every 5 seconds (demo mode 3 seconds), max 3 active. Walk from (-18,0,13) to a table, sit (y=0.35), eat 4 seconds (demo 2.2), then pay.\n- When paying: compute order total, customer money = first value from [20000,50000,100000] that is > total (fallback 100000), change = money − total.\n- Answer options: 3 choices = correct change + 2 distractors (change ± [1000,2000,5000,10000], not negative), shuffled.\n- Correct answer: cash += total, correct++, rating +0.3 (max 5), coin \"+Rp{total}\" green.\n- Wrong answer: cash += total − 2000, rating −0.4 (min 1), coin \"−Rp2.000\" red.\n- served++ on each completion; every 6 customers day++ and target resets.\n- Customer goes home to (-18,0,13) then is removed from the scene.\n\n# LEVELS & QUESTIONS\n- No static levels; questions are generated from MENU + random portion counts (1–3 items, 1–3 portions).\n- MENU (price in Rp):\n  - Nasi goreng 12000\n  - Mi ayam 10000\n  - Soto 11000\n  - Es teh 4000\n  - Jus jeruk 7000\n  - Kerupuk 2000\n- Examples of real combinations (total → money → correct change):\n  1. 1× Nasi goreng (12000) → 20000 → 8000\n  2. 1× Mi ayam (10000) → 20000 → 10000\n  3. 1× Soto (11000) → 20000 → 9000\n  4. 1× Es teh (4000) → 20000 → 16000\n  5. 1× Jus jeruk (7000) → 20000 → 13000\n  6. 1× Kerupuk (2000) → 20000 → 18000\n  7. 2× Nasi goreng (24000) → 50000 → 26000\n  8. 2× Mi ayam (20000) → 50000 → 30000\n  9. 2× Soto (22000) → 50000 → 28000\n  10. 3× Es teh (12000) → 20000 → 8000\n  11. 3× Jus jeruk (21000) → 50000 → 29000\n  12. 3× Kerupuk (6000) → 20000 → 14000\n  13. Nasi goreng + Es teh (16000) → 20000 → 4000\n  14. Mi ayam + Jus jeruk (17000) → 20000 → 3000\n  15. Soto + Kerupuk (13000) → 20000 → 7000\n  16. 2× Nasi goreng + Es teh (28000) → 50000 → 22000\n  17. 2× Mi ayam + Jus jeruk (27000) → 50000 → 23000\n  18. 3× Soto + Kerupuk (35000) → 50000 → 15000\n- One-sentence explanation for each answer: \"Total RpX, dibayar RpY, kembalian RpY−X.\"\n\n# MOTION, FEEDBACK & SOUND\n- Isometric orthographic camera: position (40,42,40) lookAt (1,0,2); smooth idle orbit sin(T*.08)*1.5 on x and z.\n- Ortho zoom: z=11.5 desktop, z=16 if width < 640px.\n- Customer walking: speed 5 units/second (demo 7), rotation facing movement direction, bob y = |sin(T*10)|*0.15.\n- Receipt panel: slide-in 0.35s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1); progress bar 0.4s.\n- Floating coin: rise 1.4s ease-out, opacity → 0.\n- Web Audio sound (optional, mute button in dock):\n  - Correct: sine 880Hz→1320Hz, 0.15s, gain 0.15.\n  - Wrong: square 220Hz→160Hz, 0.2s, gain 0.12.\n  - Button click: triangle 660Hz, 0.05s.\n- prefers-reduced-motion: disable camera orbit, customer bob, and coin animation.\n\n# CONTROLS & RESPONSIVE\n- Mouse/tap: click answer option buttons, \"Buka warung\" button, dock chips.\n- Keyboard: 1/2/3 select option, Enter confirm intro.\n- 360px phone: hide Target panel (.goal display none), receipt panel moves to bottom 76px, stat font 14px, hide brand sub. No horizontal scroll (overflow hidden on html/body).\n- Demo mode via ?demo=1: auto open intro, auto answer correctly after 1.7s, faster spawn.\n\n# TECHNICAL\n- ONE file index.html (pure HTML+CSS+JS). Three.js via importmap https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.169.0. No build, server, API, login.\n- All models from basic shapes (BoxGeometry, CylinderGeometry, SphereGeometry, CapsuleGeometry, ConeGeometry, IcosahedronGeometry, PlaneGeometry). No image files.\n- Signboard uses CanvasTexture (512×120, Fredoka 64px).\n- localStorage key \"warungUntung.best\" (high score) wrapped in try/catch.\n- Token-efficient: CSS var + classes reused; one state object {kas,rating,served,benar,hari,aktif,mulai}; render function per screen (hud, tanya, jawab); repeated markup via loops (TABLES.forEach, MENU.map, opts.map); data in compact arrays; no long comments.\n- Responsive: viewport meta viewport-fit=cover; resize handler refits camera.\n- Netlify Drop ready (drag & drop index.html).\n- Write the complete code directly without explanation.\n\n# CHECK BEFORE FINISHING\n1. Game runs from intro → spawn → pay → answer → go home → day increases without errors.\n2. All 18 combinations above: change = money − total, correct key.\n3. No horizontal scrolling on 360px phone.\n4. Receipt panel appears/disappears smoothly, option buttons disabled after answering.\n5. localStorage wrapped in try/catch, prefers-reduced-motion respected.\n6. Fredoka + Nunito fonts loaded from Google Fonts.\n7. Hex colors exactly match the token list."},{"id":"crossy","kat":"besar","katN":"3D & big","n":"Safe Way Home","mapel":"Civics / Road safety","jenjang":"Grade 1 – 4","topik":"Traffic signs and how to cross the road safely","img":"img/crossy.jpg","preview":"https://preview.edugamelabs.com/jalan-aman/","prompt":"# ROLE\n- Art director + lead developer of web educational games; result is ONE file `index.html` ready for Netlify Drop.\n- Rebuild exactly the game \"Jalan Pulang Aman\": 3D voxel world in Three.js, sign quiz, 3 lives, step score + bonus.\n- Language inside the product: Indonesian (short sentences, friendly for elementary school Grades 1–4).\n\n# PRODUCT\n- Title: **Jalan Pulang Aman**. Subject: PPKn / Road safety. Topic: traffic signs & how to cross safely.\n- Genre: isometric endless hopper in voxel style; player = cute white chicken crossing a busy road toward home.\n- Screen flow: **Title → (▶ Play button) → Play → Results** (score, correct, wrong, best, stars).\n- Top HUD: title, question chip, ⭐ score, ❤️❤️❤️ lives, 🔊/🔇 button.\n- Quiz overlay appears at sign posts every 7 rows; \"🛡️ Pelindung aktif\" badge top-left.\n\n# VISUAL STYLE\n- Palette (write once, refer by name):\n  - `--bg:#bdf06a` bright sky/grass background\n  - `--grass1:#a7e163`, `--grass2:#b5ea6f` alternating grass tiles\n  - `--road:#4a4e69` gray-purple asphalt; `--stripe:#f1faee` white road markings\n  - `--trunk:#7f5539` trunk; `--leaf1:#2d6a4f`, `--leaf2:#40916c` leaves\n  - `--hen:#ffffff` chicken body; `--comb:#e63946` comb; `--beak:#f4a261` beak/legs; `--eye:#222`\n  - `--car1:#e63946 --car2:#457b9d --car3:#f4a261 --car4:#2a9d8f --car5:#9b5de5 --car6:#ffbe0b` cars\n  - `--pole:#adb5bd` sign pole\n  - `--card:#F9F3E5` quiz/title card; `--ink:#2a1a10` text; `--accent:#FD5E2B` orange accent; `--ok:#3ecf8e`; `--no:#ff6b5b`; `--btnShadow:#e2d4bb`\n  - `--hudBg:rgba(255,250,240,.94)`; `--shieldBg:rgba(255,250,240,.92)`\n- Google Fonts: **Space Grotesk** (500,700) for UI; **Space Mono** (700) for question chip & score numbers.\n- All models = boxes (`BoxGeometry`) + `MeshLambertMaterial`; no image files; signs drawn on 2D `<canvas>` then turned into `CanvasTexture`.\n- Lighting: `HemisphereLight('#ffffff','#7a8a50',1.2)` + `DirectionalLight('#fff4e0',1.6)` from (-8,20,6), PCFSoft shadows 1024².\n- Camera: `OrthographicCamera`, ortho size `s=max(7.5, 11*min(1, w/h*1.1))`, position `(camX+4.5, 11, camZ+8.5)`, `lookAt(camX,0,camZ-1.5)`.\n\n# SCREENS & LAYOUT\n- **Title Screen** (overlay `--card`, radius 24px, padding 22px, width min(440px,100%), animation `eduIn .35s cubic-bezier(.2,1.4,.4,1)`):\n  - Si Bulat SVG mascot 74×74 (orange blob shape `#FD5E2B`, face lines `#5E1B08` stroke 11, bob animation 2s).\n  - `<small>` subject: \"PPKn · Keselamatan jalan · SD Kelas 1–4\" color `--accent`, uppercase, letter-spacing .08em, 12px.\n  - `<h1>` \"Jalan Pulang Aman\" 28px.\n  - `<p>` \"Bantu ayam pulang lewat jalan ramai. Di pos rambu, jawab arti rambu lalu lintas!\"\n  - `<ol>` 3 steps: \"Panah / geser / ketuk layar untuk melompat.\" / \"Lihat kiri-kanan, hindari mobil.\" / \"Di pos rambu: jawaban benar = +20 dan pelindung 1 kali.\"\n  - \"▶ Main\" button (`--accent`, radius 14px, shadow `0 5px 0 #b8401a`, 18px bold).\n  - \"Skor terbaik: N\" row 13px `#7a6452`.\n- **Play Screen**: fullscreen canvas + HUD + touch pad + shield badge.\n- **Quiz Overlay** (fixed inset 0, `rgba(20,30,10,.45)`, grid center, z 70):\n  - Card `--card` radius 24px, width min(380px,92vw), padding 18px 20px, animation `eduIn .3s`.\n  - `<small>` \"Pos rambu · jawab dulu\" orange uppercase 12px.\n  - Sign canvas 120×120 (internal 240×240).\n  - `<h3>` \"Apa arti rambu ini?\" 20px.\n  - 3 option buttons: radius 14px, padding 12px, font 700 16px Space Grotesk, bg `#fff`, shadow `0 4px 0 --btnShadow`, left-aligned text. Correct → bg `--ok` white text; wrong → bg `--no` white text.\n- **Results Screen** (overlay `--card`): Si Bulat \"wow\" mascot (round eyes + O mouth), `<small>` \"Selesai!\", `<h1>` \"Sampai N langkah\", stars ★★★ (active `#FFB020`, empty `#e0d3bd`, 38px), 3 result boxes (Score / Correct / Wrong / Best), \"↻ Main lagi\" button.\n- **Toast** (fixed top 76px, center, radius 14px, bg `#2a1a10` white text, 17px bold, animation `eduIn .3s`, disappears after 1500ms): correct → bg `#12946A`; wrong → bg `#d63a2b`.\n- **Shield badge**: fixed left 14px top 76px, bg `--shieldBg`, radius 12px, padding 6px 10px, text \"🛡️ Pelindung aktif\", display none by default.\n\n# MECHANICS\n- Grid: columns `c ∈ [-6,6]` (COLW=6), rows `r` increase upward (z = -r).\n- Hop 1 tile per action; directions: up/down/left/right. `down` limited to `r = max(G.max-4, r-1)`.\n- Cannot hop to a column outside ±6 or to a tile containing a tree.\n- Hop animation: duration 0.14s, arc height `sin(k*π)*0.45`, linear easing on k.\n- Cars: 2–3 per lane, speed `1.6 + rand*2.2 + min(2, r/40)`, random direction ±1, wrap at |x|>13. Length 1.4 or 2.2 (30% chance long).\n- Collision: |car.x − hen.x| < len/2 + 0.32 → `hit()`.\n- `hit()`: if shield active → consume shield, invuln 1.2s, toast \"Pelindung terpakai!\"; otherwise → lives −1, invuln 1.6s, chicken flattened (scale 1.4,0.3,1.4 for 400ms), toast \"Tertabrak! Lihat kiri-kanan dulu\". Lives 0 → game over.\n- Score: `+ (new r − max)` each time a new row is advanced; `+20` for each correct quiz answer.\n- Shield: only 1 slot; correct answer activates it; consumed on collision.\n- New rows created when advancing; old rows (r < G.r−8) removed.\n- Row types: `r%7===0` → sign; if previous row is road with run≥2 → grass; else 62% road / 38% grass.\n- Trees: 16% chance per column (8% on sign rows), not in column 0; decorative trees outside ±6 always present.\n\n# LEVELS & QUESTIONS\n- No numbered levels; difficulty increases automatically (car speed rises with r).\n- 7 signs (array `SIGNS`), each with 3 options, key = `a`:\n  1. `stop` — \"Berhenti sebentar, lalu jalan jika aman\" (options: \"Boleh ngebut\", \"Berhenti sebentar, lalu jalan jika aman\", \"Tempat parkir\")\n  2. `masuk` — \"Dilarang masuk\" (options: \"Dilarang masuk\", \"Jalan satu arah ke kanan\", \"Boleh putar balik\")\n  3. `seberang` — \"Tempat penyeberangan orang\" (options: \"Halte bus\", \"Tempat penyeberangan orang\", \"Dilarang berjalan kaki\")\n  4. `parkir` — \"Dilarang parkir\" (options: \"Tempat parkir\", \"Dilarang parkir\", \"Pom bensin\")\n  5. `henti` — \"Dilarang berhenti\" (options: \"Dilarang berhenti\", \"Boleh berhenti lama\", \"Sekolah\")\n  6. `anak` — \"Hati-hati, banyak anak sekolah\" (options: \"Taman bermain\", \"Hati-hati, banyak anak sekolah\", \"Dilarang masuk\")\n  7. `lampu` — \"Lampu merah: berhenti dan tunggu hijau\" (options: \"Lampu merah: berhenti dan tunggu hijau\", \"Lampu merah: jalan cepat\", \"Lampu rusak\")\n- Options shuffled with `shuffle`; key checked via `b.textContent === s.a`.\n- Sign drawing (canvas 240×240, `lineJoin='round'`):\n  - `stop`: white octagon r=112 + red octagon `#d62828` r=100 + white \"STOP\" text 800 64px Arial.\n  - `masuk`: red circle `#d62828` r=110 + white bar 160×40 in center.\n  - `seberang`: blue square `#1d5fd6` radius 22 + white triangle + black pedestrian figure `#111` + 5 zebra stripes.\n  - `parkir`/`henti`: blue circle `#1d5fd6` r=108 + red ring `#d62828` + white letter \"P\"/\"S\" 800 120px + red diagonal line stroke 20.\n  - `anak`: red triangle `#d62828` + yellow triangle `#ffd60a` + 2 black child figures.\n  - `lampu`: black box `#222` radius 26 + 3 lights (red `#ff3b30` y=55, dark yellow `#5a4a10` y=120, dark green `#1f3d22` y=185) r=30 + red glow `rgba(255,90,80,.35)` r=42.\n\n# MOTION, FEEDBACK & SOUND\n- Camera follows chicken: `camX += (hen.x*0.5 − camX)*0.08`, `camZ += (hen.z − camZ)*0.08`.\n- Chicken blinks during invuln: `visible = !(inv>0 && floor(inv*10)%2)`.\n- Chicken rotation per direction: up=π, down=0, left=−π/2, right=π/2.\n- Web Audio sound (oscillator + gain, no files):\n  - `ok`: triangle 660Hz .07s → 880Hz .09s\n  - `bad`: square 220Hz .12s → 160Hz .16s\n  - `pop`: triangle 520Hz .05s\n  - `win`: triangle 523→659→784→1046Hz\n  - `tick`: triangle 1200Hz .02s\n  - `boom`: sawtooth 90Hz .25s\n  - Gain envelope: 0.0001 → 0.18 → 0.0001 exponential.\n- CSS animations: `eduIn` (translateY 30px scale .94 → none), `eduBob` (translateY −6px rotate −4deg), `eduFlash` (scale 1.25 → 1), `eduUp` (translateY −140% opacity 0).\n- Correct toast shown 700ms then closes quiz; wrong shown 1500ms + highlights correct answer.\n\n# CONTROLS & RESPONSIVE\n- Keyboard: ArrowUp/W=up, ArrowDown/S=down, ArrowLeft/A=left, ArrowRight/D=right (preventDefault).\n- Touch pad: 3×62px grid, buttons ▲◀▼▶, radius 50%, bg `rgba(255,250,240,.85)`, shadow `0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.25)`, `touch-action:none`. Hidden on desktop (`@media (hover:hover) and (pointer:fine)`).\n- Swipe on canvas: pointerdown saves (sx,sy); pointerup computes dx,dy; if distance <20px → hop up; else dominant direction.\n- Responsive: HUD wraps at ≤640px, HUD title hidden, question chip full-width order 9. No horizontal scroll at 360px.\n- `prefers-reduced-motion`: disable bob/flash animations when requested.\n\n# TECHNICAL\n- ONE file `index.html` (pure HTML+CSS+JS). Three.js via importmap `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.169.0/build/three.module.js`. No build/server/API/login.\n- All images from code (BoxGeometry + CanvasTexture + inline SVG). localStorage wrapped in try/catch.\n- localStorage keys: `edu_mute` (\"1\"/\"0\"), `edu_best_jalanaman` (best score number).\n- Ready for Netlify Drop; responsive on 360px phones; `prefers-reduced-motion` respected.\n- Token-efficient: CSS variables + reused classes; one state object `G` + render function per screen; repeated markup via loops; data in compact arrays; no long comments; write full code directly.\n- State structure `G`: `{r,c,max,score,lives,run,hop,shield,quiz,benar,salah,inv,done}`.\n- Core functions: `mkLane(r)`, `lane(r)`, `reset()`, `move(d)`, `landed()`, `ask(s)`, `hit()`, `safe(r,c,ahead)`, `demo()`, `loop(t)`.\n- Demo mode `?demo=1`: smart auto-walk (85% correct answers), auto-close results after 2.5s, sound muted.\n- HUD created via `EDU.hud({title,lives:true,credit})`; credit: \"Terinspirasi Crossy Road · he-is-talha (MIT) · Three.js\".\n\n# CHECK BEFORE FINISHING\n1. Game is playable Title → Play → Results without errors, including restart.\n2. All 7 sign answer keys correct & options shuffled.\n3. No horizontal scroll on 360px phones; touch pad & swipe work.\n4. localStorage `edu_best_jalanaman` & `edu_mute` stored safely (try/catch).\n5. Web Audio sound active after first interaction; mute button works.\n6. Shield active only 1 slot; consumed on collision; badge appears/disappears correctly.\n7. Isometric camera follows chicken; old rows cleaned up to avoid memory leaks.\n8. `prefers-reduced-motion` disables bob/flash animations."},{"id":"tikus","kat":"arkade","katN":"Arcade","n":"Whack the Answer Mouse","mapel":"Math","jenjang":"Grade 2 – 4","topik":"Multiplication 2 to 9","img":"img/tikus.jpg","preview":"https://preview.edugamelabs.com/pukul-tikus/","prompt":"# ROLE\n- Art director + lead developer of educational web games. Rebuild the product EXACTLY from this specification in ONE `index.html` file.\n- Output: complete pure HTML+CSS+JS code, no build, no explanation, no long comments.\n\n# PRODUCT\n- Title: **Pukul Tikus Jawaban**. Subject: Mathematics · Elementary Grades 2–4. Topic: Multiplication 2–9.\n- Language inside the product: **Bahasa Indonesia** (short sentences).\n- Core mechanic: 3×3 grid of dirt holes, cute moles pop up and down carrying number boards, one mole always carries the correct answer, click/tap to whack, question changes after a correct hit, 3 lives, 60-second timer.\n- Screen flow: **Title → (directly) Play → Results**. No separate \"How to play\" screen; instructions are on the title card.\n- Mascot: **Si Bulat** (a smiling orange blob) appears on the title & results cards.\n\n# VISUAL STYLE\n- Color tokens (write once, refer by name):\n  - `--bg1:#9be46a` `--bg2:#4fae3c` `--bg3:#2f7d2a` (radial gradient garden background)\n  - `--tanah1:#2b1609` `--tanah2:#4a2a12` (holes), `--rim:#7bd04f` (hole edge)\n  - `--bulu1:#a8703f` `--bulu2:#7a4a22` (mole body), `--hitam:#1a0e06` (eyes), `--pink:#ff8fa3` (nose)\n  - `--papan:#fff8e6` `--papan-b:#5a3415` `--papan-t:#2a1a10` (number board)\n  - `--hijau-ok:#7fd17a` `--hijau-ok2:#3e9a3a` (mole hit correctly)\n  - `--merah-bad:#ff8a7a` `--merah-bad2:#c43a2a` (mole hit incorrectly)\n  - `--krem:#F9F3E5` `--krem2:#fffaf0` `--ink:#2a1a10` `--ink2:#5a4636` `--ink3:#7a6452` (cards & text)\n  - `--oranye:#FD5E2B` `--oranye-tua:#b8401a` (primary button & accent)\n  - `--emas:#FFB020` `--emas-off:#e0d3bd` (stars)\n  - `--good:#12946A` `--bad:#d63a2b` (toast)\n  - `--float-good:#3ee08f` `--float-bad:#ff5a4a` (floating numbers)\n- Google Fonts: **Space Grotesk** (500,700) for UI; **Space Mono** (700) for questions, number boards, and floating numbers.\n- Body background: `radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 20%, var(--bg1), var(--bg2) 60%, var(--bg3))`.\n- Radii: HUD 16px, cards 24px, buttons 14px, number boards 10px, stats 14px, toast 14px.\n- Shadows: HUD `0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.18)`; cards `0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.35)`; buttons `0 5px 0 var(--oranye-tua)`; holes `inset 0 8px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.6), 0 3px 0 var(--rim)`.\n- Mole: SVG/CSS basic shapes — body `border-radius:48% 48% 18% 18%` gradient `--bulu1→--bulu2`, two round black eyes with small white glints, oval pink nose, cream-white number board with brown border.\n\n# SCREENS & LAYOUT\n- **HUD** (fixed top, `left/right:10px; top:10px; z-index:50`), flex gap 10px, padding `8px 10px 8px 14px`, bg `rgba(255,250,240,.94)`, text `--ink`, font 15px. Contents left→right:\n  1. Small title `Pukul Tikus Jawaban` color `--oranye`, 14px, nowrap.\n  2. Question box `#eduQ`: font Space Mono 20px, bg `--ink`, white text, padding `4px 12px`, radius 10px, max-width 56vw, ellipsis. Empty → `display:none`.\n  3. Spacer flex:1.\n  4. `⭐ <b>0</b>` score (font 700).\n  5. Lives: 3 hearts `❤️`/`🤍` (font 700).\n  6. `⏱ <b>60</b>` timer.\n  7. Mute button 34×34, radius 10px, bg `#f1e6d2`, icon `🔊`/`🔇`.\n- **Credit** fixed bottom-left 10px, font 11px, `rgba(255,255,255,.75)`, text: `Terinspirasi Whack-a-Mole · he-is-talha (MIT)`.\n- **Field**: `#field` absolute `inset:70px 0 0`, grid place-items center.\n- **Grid**: 3 columns, gap `clamp(10px,3vw,34px)`, width `min(92vw,620px,calc((100vh - 110px)*1.15))`.\n- **Hole**: aspect-ratio 1.25, cursor pointer. Pseudo `::before` bottom ellipse (34% height) gradient `--tanah1→--tanah2` + inset shadow + `0 3px 0 var(--rim)`.\n- **Mole** inside the hole: `left/right:18%; bottom:20%; height:78%`, initial transform `translateY(70%) scaleY(.2)`, origin bottom, `visibility:hidden`.\n- **Number board**: absolute, `left:50%; top:56%`, translateX(-50%), bg `--papan`, border 3px `--papan-b`, radius 10px, padding `2px 10px`, font Space Mono 700 `clamp(18px,3.6vw,30px)`, color `--papan-t`, nowrap.\n- **Hammer**: `#hammer` fixed 70×70, font-size 60px `🔨`, `pointer-events:none`, z-index 60, transform `translate(-30%,-70%) rotate(-30deg)`, transition transform .07s, `display:none` until pointer moves.\n- **Title card** (overlay `.edu-ov`): bg `rgba(20,12,6,.55)` + `backdrop-filter:blur(3px)`, card `min(440px,100%)` bg `--krem`, radius 24px, padding `22px 22px 18px`, center. Order top→bottom:\n  1. Mascot Si Bulat 74×74 (bob animation 2s).\n  2. `<small>` subject: `Matematika · SD Kelas 2–4` color `--oranye`, uppercase, letter-spacing .08em, 12px.\n  3. `<h1>` `Pukul Tikus Jawaban` 28px.\n  4. `<p>` `Tikus keluar membawa angka. Pukul tikus yang membawa jawaban benar!`\n  5. `<ol>` 3 steps: `Lihat soal perkalian di atas.` / `Klik/ketuk tikus dengan jawaban benar: +10.` / `Salah pukul = nyawa berkurang. Waktu 60 detik.`\n  6. Button `▶ Main` (full width, bg `--oranye`, white text 18px 700, radius 14px, bottom shadow).\n  7. `Skor terbaik: <b>0</b>` 13px `--ink3`.\n- **Results card** (same overlay): mascot Si Bulat with surprised expression, `<small>Selesai!</small>`, `<h1>` dynamic (`Waktu habis!` if lives >0, `Nyawa habis` if lives depleted), star row `★★★` (gold/`--emas-off`), 4 stat boxes: Score / Correct / Wrong / Best, button `↻ Main lagi`.\n\n# MECHANICS\n- Single state: `{score, lives:3, time:60, cur, holes[9], run, benar, salah, timers[]}`.\n- Question: `a × b` with a,b random 2–9 → answer `a*b`. Display `\"a × b = ?\"` in the HUD.\n- Mole spawn: interval **620 ms** calls `popOne()`:\n  - Pick a random empty hole.\n  - If no mole is currently carrying the correct answer → 50% chance this mole carries the correct answer; the rest are distractors from `opsi(ans,4)` minus the correct answer (distractors = ans + one of `[-10,-2,-1,1,2,3,10,-3]`, unique, ≥0).\n  - Mole duration increases: `1400 + rand(0..900) − min(600, score*3)` ms, then auto-descends.\n- Correct hit: `score += 10`, `benar++`, SFX `ok`, floating text `+10` green at click position, mole turns green, new question.\n- Wrong hit: `lives--`, `salah++`, SFX `bad`, floating text `\"a × b = ans\"` red, mole turns red. If `lives<=0` → `finish()` after 400 ms.\n- Timer: `setInterval` 1000 ms, `time--`, `time<=0` → `finish()`.\n- `finish()`: stop all intervals, hide all moles, call results screen with `max:200` (theoretical maximum score 20 correct × 10).\n- Stars: `ceil(score/200*3)` clamped 1–3.\n- Best score stored in localStorage key `edu_best_tikus`.\n\n# LEVELS & QUESTIONS\n- No tiered levels; questions are randomly generated from multiplication 2–9. Example 12 real questions (answer keys verified):\n  1. 2 × 3 = **6**\n  2. 3 × 4 = **12**\n  3. 4 × 5 = **20**\n  4. 5 × 6 = **30**\n  5. 6 × 7 = **42**\n  6. 7 × 8 = **56**\n  7. 8 × 9 = **72**\n  8. 9 × 2 = **18**\n  9. 2 × 7 = **14**\n  10. 3 × 8 = **24**\n  11. 4 × 9 = **36**\n  12. 6 × 6 = **36**\n- Question bank stored as a `kali()` function at the top of the script so teachers can easily edit it (can be replaced with a static array).\n- Distractors are always close to the correct answer (difference 1–10) to keep it challenging.\n\n# MOTION, FEEDBACK & SOUND\n- Mole rises: `transform .16s cubic-bezier(.3,1.6,.5,1)` + `visibility 0s`; descends: same transition + `visibility 0s .16s`.\n- Hammer: `transform .07s`; class `.down` changes rotation `-30deg → 20deg` for 90 ms.\n- Question flash: keyframe `eduFlash .5s` (scale 1.25 → 1) on new question.\n- Score bump: keyframe `eduFlash .35s` on the stat wrapper.\n- Card entrance: keyframe `eduIn .35s cubic-bezier(.2,1.4,.4,1)` (translateY 30px scale .94 → normal).\n- Mascot bob: keyframe `eduBob 2s ease-in-out infinite` (translateY -6px rotate -4deg at 50%).\n- Floating text: keyframe `eduUp .9s forwards` (rises to -140% + opacity 0), font Space Mono 700 24px, color `--float-good`/`--float-bad`, text-shadow `0 2px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.3)`.\n- Toast: appears for 1500 ms, bg `--ink`/`--good`/`--bad`, radius 14px, animation `eduIn .3s`.\n- Web Audio sound (no files), oscillator triangle (except `bad`=square, `boom`=sawtooth), gain 0.18 → 0.0001:\n  - `ok`: 660 Hz .07s → 880 Hz .09s\n  - `bad`: 220 Hz .12s → 160 Hz .16s\n  - `pop`: 520 Hz .05s\n  - `win`: 523 → 659 → 784 → 1046 Hz (each .1s, last .2s)\n  - `tick`: 1200 Hz .02s\n  - `boom`: 90 Hz .25s\n- Mute button toggles icon `🔊`/`🔇`, stored in localStorage `edu_mute` (`'1'`/`'0'`).\n\n# CONTROLS & RESPONSIVE\n- Pointer: `pointerdown` on grid → find nearest `.hole`, call `hammer(x,y)` then `whack(hole,x,y)`.\n- Mouse: `pointermove` moves the hammer following the cursor (only `pointerType==='mouse'`).\n- Keyboard: `Enter`/`Space` on title/results card triggers the primary button.\n- 360 px phone: HUD `flex-wrap:wrap`, font 13px, gap 6px, HUD title hidden, question box `order:9; flex-basis:100%; text-align:center; max-width:none`.\n- `touch-action:manipulation`, `-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent`, `overflow:hidden` on html/body.\n- No horizontal scroll; grid adapts to viewport width.\n\n# TECHNICAL\n- ONE `index.html` file (pure HTML+CSS+JS). No build, no server, no API, no login, no image files (all SVG/CSS/emoji).\n- Netlify Drop ready.\n- localStorage wrapped in try/catch (`edu_mute`, `edu_best_tikus`).\n- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` → disable bob, flash, and float animations.\n- Token-efficient: CSS variables + reused classes; one state object + render function per screen; hole markup generated via `for(i=0;i<9;i++)` loop; question data in a compact function; no long comments; write the complete code directly without explanation.\n- Structure: `<head>` (meta viewport `width=device-width,initial-scale=1,maximum-scale=1`, title `Pukul Tikus Jawaban`, Google Fonts link Space Grotesk + Space Mono, `<style>`), `<body>` (`#field > #grid`, `#hammer`, `<script>`).\n- Script contains: utils (`rand`, `pick`, `shuffle`, `$`), audio (`ctx`, `sfx`), HUD (`hud`, `setQ`, `setScore`, `setLives`, `setTime`), toast/float, mascot `bulat(mood)`, screens `title`/`end`, question bank `Q.kali`/`Q.opsi`, then game logic.\n- Optional demo mode via `?demo=1`: auto-start, auto-whack correct moles (occasionally wrong every 9 attempts), auto-close results after 2.5s.\n\n# CHECK BEFORE FINISHING\n1. Game runs from title → play → results without console errors.\n2. All multiplication 2–9 answer keys are correct (verify the 12 examples above).\n3. No horizontal scroll at 360 px viewport.\n4. Timer stops exactly when `finish()` is called; all moles are hidden.\n5. Best score is saved and appears on the next title card.\n6. Mute button works and state is saved.\n7. `prefers-reduced-motion` disables decorative animations.\n8. One file, no external dependencies other than Google Fonts."},{"id":"wordle","kat":"kuis","katN":"Quiz & practice","n":"Word Guess","mapel":"Bahasa Indonesia","jenjang":"Grade 3 – Middle School (Grades 7–9)","topik":"5-letter vocabulary and their meanings","img":"img/wordle.jpg","preview":"https://preview.edugamelabs.com/tebak-kata/","prompt":"# ROLE\nYou are an art director + senior lead developer. Rebuild the educational game \"Tebak Kata\" (a 5-letter Indonesian vocabulary guessing game) in ONE `index.html` file that is ALMOST 100% identical to the specification below. Write complete code without explanation, without placeholders.\n\n# PRODUCT\n- Name: **Tebak Kata**. Subject: Bahasa Indonesia · Vocabulary · Elementary Grade 3 – Middle School.\n- Language inside the product: **Bahasa Indonesia** (all UI text, instructions, toasts, buttons).\n- Core mechanic: guess a 5-letter word from its meaning hint, 6 attempts, 5 words per round. Per-letter colors (green/yellow/gray), on-screen keyboard colored accordingly, first-letter hint button (cost −5 score), new word button.\n- Score: `(6 - correct_row) * 10 + 10` when correct; max per word = 60; max round = 250 (5 words × 50 average, but capped at 250 on the results screen).\n- No login, no server, no API. Ready for Netlify Drop.\n\n# VISUAL STYLE\n- Palette (write once as CSS vars, reference by name):\n  - `--bg: #121213` main background (deep black)\n  - `--tile-border: #3a3a3c` empty tile border\n  - `--tile-filled: #565758` filled tile border\n  - `--green: #538d4e` correct letter in correct position\n  - `--yellow: #b59f3b` letter present but wrong position\n  - `--gray: #3a3a3c` letter absent\n  - `--key: #818384` default keyboard button\n  - `--hint: #c9c9c9` hint text\n  - `--hint-hl: #ffd166` hint word (bold)\n  - `--tool-bg: #2a2a2c` tools button\n  - `--hud-bg: rgba(255,250,240,.94)` HUD\n  - `--hud-fg: #2a1a10` HUD text\n  - `--accent: #FD5E2B` orange accent (HUD title, primary button, mascot)\n  - `--accent-shadow: #b8401a` button shadow\n  - `--card-bg: #F9F3E5` modal card\n  - `--card-fg: #2a1a10`\n  - `--card-muted: #5a4636`\n  - `--good: #12946A` correct toast\n  - `--bad: #d63a2b` wrong toast\n  - `--star: #FFB020` star\n- Google Fonts: **Space Grotesk** (500, 700) for UI; **Space Mono** (700) for score numbers & small labels. Import via `@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@500;700&family=Space+Mono:wght@700&display=swap')`.\n- Body background: `#121213`, white text, `display:grid; place-items:center`.\n- Letter tiles: `border:2px solid`, `aspect-ratio:1`, `font:800 clamp(20px,4.6vw,32px) 'Space Grotesk'`, `text-transform:uppercase`.\n- Keyboard buttons: `border-radius:6px`, `background:#818384`, `font:700 15px 'Space Grotesk'`, height 52px, max width 44px (ENTER/⌫ buttons max 70px, font 12px).\n- Tools buttons: `border-radius:999px`, `padding:6px 14px`, `font:700 13px`, `background:#2a2a2c`.\n- HUD: `border-radius:16px`, `background:rgba(255,250,240,.94)`, `box-shadow:0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.18)`, `padding:8px 10px 8px 14px`, fixed top 10px left/right 10px.\n- Modal card: `border-radius:24px`, `background:#F9F3E5`, `padding:22px 22px 18px`, `box-shadow:0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.35)`, entrance animation `eduIn .35s cubic-bezier(.2,1.4,.4,1)` (from `translateY(30px) scale(.94)` to normal).\n- Modal primary button: `background:#FD5E2B`, `color:#fff`, `font:700 18px`, `padding:13px 26px`, `border-radius:14px`, `box-shadow:0 5px 0 #b8401a`; on `:active` move down 3px + shadow 2px.\n\n# SCREENS & LAYOUT\nScreen order: **Title → Play → Results** (How to play is merged into the title card as an `<ol>`).\n\n**1. Title Screen (full `.edu-ov` overlay, background `rgba(20,12,6,.55)` + `backdrop-filter:blur(3px)`):**\n- Center card, from top to bottom:\n  - Si Bulat mascot (SVG 74×74, bob animation 2s ease-in-out infinite, translateY −6px + rotate −4deg at 50%).\n  - `<small>` uppercase Space Mono color `#FD5E2B` letter-spacing .08em: `Bahasa Indonesia · Kosakata · SD Kelas 3 – SMP`.\n  - `<h1>` 28px: `Tebak Kata`.\n  - `<p>` 15px color `#5a4636`: `Tebak kata 5 huruf dari petunjuk artinya, dalam 6 kesempatan.`\n  - `<ol>` 3 points (14.5px, color `#3d2c1f`):\n    1. `Ketik kata 5 huruf lalu tekan ENTER.`\n    2. `Hijau = huruf & posisi benar. Kuning = huruf ada tapi posisi salah. Abu-abu = tidak ada.`\n    3. `5 kata per ronde. Makin cepat tertebak, makin besar skornya.`\n  - `▶ Main` button (full width).\n  - Bottom row 13px `#7a6452`: `Skor terbaik: <b>N</b>`.\n- Enter/Space also starts.\n\n**2. Play Screen:**\n- Fixed top HUD: title `Tebak Kata` (orange, 14px, hidden at ≤640px), question box `#eduQ` (Space Mono 20px, bg `#2a1a10`, white text, radius 10px, padding 4px 12px, max-width 56vw, ellipsis; on mobile becomes 16px full-width order 9), spacer, `⭐ <b>0</b>` (score), mute button 🔊/🔇 (34×34, radius 10px, bg `#f1e6d2`).\n- Fixed bottom-left credit 11px translucent white: `Terinspirasi Wordle · he-is-talha (MIT)`.\n- Content wrap: `margin-top:62px`, flex column, gap 12px, align center.\n- Hint row 15px `#c9c9c9` center max 90vw: `Tebak kata 5 huruf. Petunjuk: <b id=\"hb\">…</b>` (hint word color `#ffd166`).\n- Grid 6 rows × 5 columns, gap 6px. Tile size: `width: min(13vw, calc((100vh - 380px)/6), 62px)`.\n- Tools row: `💡 Huruf pertama` and `↻ Kata baru` buttons.\n- On-screen keyboard 3 rows (QWERTYUIOP / ASDFGHJKL / ⏎ZXCVBNM⌫), width `min(96vw,500px)`, gap 6px between rows, 5px between buttons. ENTER & ⌫ max width 70px, font 12px, labels `ENTER` and `⌫`.\n\n**3. Results Screen (`.edu-ov` overlay):**\n- Card: Si Bulat mascot mood `wow`, `<small>Selesai!</small>`, `<h1>5 kata selesai!</h1>`, stars 38px `#FFB020` (3 stars, rest `#e0d3bd`), stats row of 3 white boxes radius 14px (Score / Correct / Wrong / Best), `↻ Main lagi` button.\n- Stars = `Math.max(1, Math.min(3, Math.ceil(score/250*3)))`.\n\n# MECHANICS\n- Single state `G = { used:[], score:0, benar:0, salah:0, n:0, w:[word,hint], r:0, cur:'', done:false, cand:[...] }`.\n- `newWord()`: pick a random word from the pool not yet used (`used`), if exhausted reset `used=[]`. Reset `r=0, cur='', done=false, cand=all words`. Render empty grid, reset keyboard colors, set hint to the word's meaning, set HUD question `Kata ke-{n+1}: {arti}`.\n- Letter input: only A–Z, max 5 per row. Backspace deletes 1. Enter checks.\n- Enter with <5 letters: row shake (`@keyframes sh` translateX ±8px, .4s), toast `Kurang huruf`, does not proceed.\n- `score(guess, target)`: two passes — pass 1 marks `g` for exact positions (set `left[i]=null`), pass 2 marks `y` if the letter exists in the remaining `left` (set null), rest `x`.\n- Submit: flip tiles one by one with delay `i*230ms`, each tile `flip` animation 0.45s ease (rotateX 90deg at 50%), then add color class at `+220ms`. Keyboard also colored (priority: `g` > `y` > `x`, never downgrade status).\n- Filter `cand` with `score(guess,w).join() === res.join()` (for demo/auto mode).\n- After all flips (`5*230+250 = 1400ms`):\n  - Correct: `pts = (6-r)*10+10`, `score+=pts`, `benar++`, `n++`, sfx `win`, green toast `✔ {KATA} = {arti} · +{pts}`, wait 1400ms → `roundEnd()`.\n  - Wrong on row 6: `salah++`, `n++`, sfx `bad`, red toast `Jawabannya: {KATA} ({arti})`, wait 1800ms → `roundEnd()`.\n  - Not yet: `r++`, `cur=''`, `done=false`, sfx `tick`.\n- `roundEnd()`: if `n>=5` → `end({key:'tebakkata', score, benar, salah, max:250, head:'5 kata selesai!'})`; else `newWord()`.\n- `💡 Huruf pertama` button: `score = max(0, score-5)`, update HUD, toast `Huruf pertama: {huruf[0]}`. Cannot be used when `done`.\n- `↻ Kata baru` button: `n++` then `roundEnd()` (skip word, counts as finished).\n\n# LEVELS & QUESTIONS\nArray `W` above the script (30 words, format `[KATA, arti]`), easy for teachers to edit:\n```\n['RUMAH','tempat tinggal keluarga'], ['PINTU','tempat keluar masuk ruangan'],\n['MERAH','warna darah dan cabai'], ['HIJAU','warna daun'],\n['BUNGA','bagian tumbuhan yang indah dan harum'], ['POHON','tumbuhan besar berbatang kayu'],\n['GAJAH','hewan berbelalai'], ['SINGA','raja hutan'],\n['PASAR','tempat jual beli'], ['SAWAH','lahan tempat menanam padi'],\n['BULAN','benda langit yang bersinar di malam hari'], ['HUJAN','air yang turun dari awan'],\n['TANAH','tempat akar tumbuhan tertanam'], ['BATIK','kain bermotif khas Indonesia'],\n['ANGIN','udara yang bergerak'], ['NANAS','buah bermahkota daun, rasanya asam manis'],\n['SALAK','buah bersisik seperti kulit ular'], ['TEMPE','makanan dari kedelai'],\n['KATAK','hewan amfibi yang melompat'], ['KAPAL','kendaraan di laut'],\n['KURSI','tempat duduk'], ['LAMPU','alat penerang'],\n['GELAS','wadah untuk minum'], ['MURID','orang yang belajar di sekolah'],\n['KELAS','ruang belajar'], ['JUJUR','berkata apa adanya, tidak bohong'],\n['RAJIN','suka bekerja dan belajar'], ['HUTAN','tempat banyak pohon tumbuh'],\n['DANAU','genangan air luas di daratan'], ['PULAU','daratan yang dikelilingi air']\n```\n- All words are 5 letters, all meanings are 1 short phrase. No duplicates.\n- 5 words per round, random without repeats until the pool is exhausted.\n\n# MOTION, FEEDBACK & SOUND\n- CSS animations:\n  - `pop .1s` when a letter is filled (scale 1.1 at 50%).\n  - `flip .45s ease` on submit (rotateX 90deg at 50%).\n  - `sh .4s` row shake when not enough letters.\n  - `eduIn .35s cubic-bezier(.2,1.4,.4,1)` modal entrance.\n  - `eduBob 2s ease-in-out infinite` mascot.\n  - `eduFlash .5s` HUD question flash (scale 1.25 → 1).\n  - `eduFlash .35s` score bump.\n  - `eduUp .9s forwards` float text rising + fade.\n- Web Audio sound (oscillator + gain, no files):\n  - `ok`: triangle 660Hz .07s → 880Hz .09s\n  - `bad`: square 220Hz .12s → 160Hz .16s\n  - `pop`: triangle 520Hz .05s\n  - `win`: triangle 523→659→784→1046Hz (.1/.1/.1/.2s)\n  - `tick`: triangle 1200Hz .02s\n  - `boom`: sawtooth 90Hz .25s\n  - Gain envelope: 0.0001 → 0.18 (ramp .01s) → 0.0001 (ramp duration).\n- Mute toggle button, saved in `localStorage.edu_mute` (`'1'`/`'0'`), wrapped in try/catch. Icon 🔊/🔇.\n- Toast: fixed top 76px center, radius 14px, bg `#2a1a10` (default) / `#12946A` (good) / `#d63a2b` (bad), font 700 17px, disappears after 1500ms.\n\n# CONTROLS & RESPONSIVE\n- Physical keyboard: `keydown` — Enter→submit, Backspace→delete, `/^[a-z]$/i`→uppercase letter.\n- On-screen keyboard: click `[data-k]` button, pressed button gets `.pr` class (filter brightness 1.5) for 110ms.\n- Media query ≤640px: HUD wraps, HUD title hidden, question full-width order 9, font 16px.\n- `touch-action:manipulation`, `-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent`.\n- `overflow:hidden` on html/body, no horizontal scroll at 360px.\n- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` → disable all animations (flip, shake, bob, pop, eduIn, eduUp).\n\n# TECHNICAL\n- ONE `index.html` file (pure HTML+CSS+JS, no external libraries except Google Fonts via `@import`).\n- No build, no server, no API, no login. Ready for Netlify Drop.\n- All images made with code (inline SVG for mascot, CSS for tiles).\n- localStorage wrapped in try/catch: keys `edu_mute`, `edu_best_tebakkata`.\n- Token-efficient: CSS variables + reused classes (`.c`, `.k`, `.row`, `.kr`, `.edu-*`), one `G` object + render functions per section (`grid()`, `newWord()`, `key()`, `submit()`), repeated markup via loops (`for r<6`, `for c<5`, `KB.map`), data in compact arrays, no long comments.\n- Si Bulat mascot (SVG 200×200 viewBox): organic orange blob shape `#FD5E2B` (curved path), eyes & mouth lines `#5E1B08` stroke-width 11 round. Mood `happy`: two curved eyes `M58 84 Q74 66 90 84` + `M110 84 Q126 66 142 84`, smiling mouth `M52 100 Q100 154 148 100`. Mood `wow`: two circle eyes r=8 fill ink, mouth ellipse rx=14 ry=17.\n- HUD built via JS `E.hud({title, credit})`, title card via `E.title({key,title,mapel,desc,how}, onStart)`, results card via `E.end({key,score,benar,salah,max,head}, onAgain)`.\n- Optional demo mode `?demo=1`: auto-type guesses matching `cand`, skip title overlay, auto-close results after 2.5s. (May be included for consistency.)\n\n# CHECK BEFORE FINISHING\n1. Game runs from title → 5 words → results without console errors.\n2. All 30 words are 5 letters, all meanings match, no duplicates.\n3. `score()` algorithm is correct: green priority, yellow only for remaining letters, gray for the rest.\n4. On-screen keyboard colored with priority g > y > x.\n5. No horizontal scroll at 360px viewport.\n6. localStorage try/catch, mute saved, best score saved.\n7. `prefers-reduced-motion` disables animations.\n8. `💡 Huruf pertama` button reduces score by 5 (min 0) and shows the first letter.\n9. Correct/wrong toasts appear with the right colors, disappear after 1.5s.\n10. Max score 250 on the results screen, stars 1–3 according to ratio."},{"id":"invaders","kat":"arkade","katN":"Arcade","n":"Hijaiyah Letter Invasion","mapel":"Islamic Studies / Arabic","jenjang":"Kindergarten – Grade 3","topik":"Recognizing hijaiyah letters","img":"img/invaders.jpg","preview":"https://preview.edugamelabs.com/invasi-hijaiyah/","prompt":"# ROLE\n- You are an art director + lead developer. Rebuild the educational game \"Invasi Huruf Hijaiyah\" ALMOST 100% like the original in ONE `index.html` file.\n- Language inside the product: Indonesian (short sentences, friendly for kindergarten–elementary kids).\n- Output: complete ready-to-run code, without additional explanation.\n\n# PRODUCT\n- Title: **Invasi Huruf Hijaiyah**. Subject: PAI / Arabic. Topic: Getting to know hijaiyah letters. Level: Kindergarten – Elementary Grade 3.\n- Genre: shoot-'em-up arcade in the style of \"rows of invaders descending from the sky\" (Space Invaders mechanics, rewritten from scratch).\n- Screen flow: **Title → (▶ Play button) → Play → Results** (score, correct, wrong, best, stars, ↻ Play again button).\n- Goal: the player shoots invaders carrying the letter matching the command \"Shoot the letter: <Name>\".\n- Correct = +10, Wrong = −5 (score cannot go negative) and that letter shoots back.\n- 3 lives. When all letters are gone → next wave, faster.\n\n# VISUAL STYLE\n- Palette (write once as CSS vars, refer to them by name):\n  - `--bg:#06110f` body background\n  - `--space:#071814` canvas background\n  - `--ground:rgba(95,227,161,.12)` bottom ground band\n  - `--inv:#1d6b52` invader body\n  - `--inv-leg:#2b8f6e` invader legs\n  - `--inv-hit:#ff5a4a` invader when hit by a wrong shot\n  - `--ink:#e9fff6` hijaiyah letter on the invader\n  - `--ship:#FD5E2B` player ship (orange)\n  - `--ship-top:#ffd0a8` ship nose\n  - `--bullet:#ffe066` player bullet (yellow)\n  - `--ebullet:#ff7a6b` enemy bullet (pink)\n  - `--star:rgba(180,255,220,α)` background stars\n  - `--hud-bg:rgba(255,250,240,.94)` HUD card\n  - `--hud-ink:#2a1a10` HUD text\n  - `--card:#F9F3E5` title/results card\n  - `--accent:#FD5E2B` primary button\n  - `--accent-shadow:#b8401a` button shadow\n  - `--good:#12946A` correct toast\n  - `--bad:#d63a2b` wrong toast\n  - `--float-good:#3ee08f` floating correct text\n  - `--float-bad:#ff5a4a` floating wrong text\n- Google Fonts: **Amiri 700** (hijaiyah letters), **Space Grotesk 500/700** (UI), **Space Mono 700** (score/command numbers).\n- Canvas: `border-radius:16px`, `box-shadow:0 0 0 3px #1d4d3f, 0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.5)`, `touch-action:none`, `margin-top:52px`.\n- HUD: milk-white card `border-radius:16px`, `box-shadow:0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.18)`, padding `8px 10px 8px 14px`.\n- Title/results card: `border-radius:24px`, padding `22px 22px 18px`, `box-shadow:0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.35)`, entrance animation `eduIn .35s cubic-bezier(.2,1.4,.4,1)`.\n- Primary button: `background:#FD5E2B`, white text 700 18px, padding `13px 26px`, radius 14px, `box-shadow:0 5px 0 #b8401a`; active moves down 3px.\n- Mascot **Si Bulat**: SVG 200×200, orange blob shape `#FD5E2B` (blob path), face lines `#5E1B08` stroke 11 round. Moods `happy` (curved eyes + wide smile) and `wow` (round eyes + oval mouth). Animation `eduBob 2s ease-in-out infinite` (up-down 6px, rotation −4°).\n\n# SCREENS & LAYOUT\n- **Title Screen** (overlay `position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgba(20,12,6,.55);backdrop-filter:blur(3px)`), order top→bottom:\n  1. Mascot Si Bulat (happy mood, 74×74, bob animation).\n  2. `<small>` subject: `PAI · Mengenal huruf hijaiyah · TK – SD Kelas 3` (Space Mono, color `--accent`, uppercase, letter-spacing .08em, 12px).\n  3. `<h1>` **Invasi Huruf Hijaiyah** (28px, line-height 1.1).\n  4. `<p>` description: \"Huruf hijaiyah turun dari langit. Tembak huruf yang namanya disebut!\"\n  5. `<ol>` how to play (3 points):\n     - \"Panah kiri/kanan untuk bergerak, spasi untuk menembak (di HP: tombol layar).\"\n     - \"Huruf benar = +10. Huruf salah = −5 dan huruf itu membalas tembakan.\"\n     - \"Hindari peluru merah. Habiskan semua huruf untuk gelombang berikutnya.\"\n  6. `▶ Main` button (full width).\n  7. Small text: `Skor terbaik: <b>N</b>`.\n- **Play Screen**: top HUD + canvas + bottom touch pad (left: ◀ ▶, right: ●) + small credit bottom-left.\n- **Results Screen** (same overlay), order:\n  1. Mascot wow mood.\n  2. `<small>Selesai!</small>`.\n  3. `<h1>` results title: `Gelombang <N>` (or end message such as \"Huruf sampai ke bawah!\" / \"Pesawat kena!\").\n  4. Stars `★★★` (active `#FFB020`, empty `#e0d3bd`), 38px, letter-spacing 4px.\n  5. Stats row: white box radius 14px containing **Skor**, **Benar**, **Salah**, **Terbaik** (numbers 22px, labels 12px `#7a6452`).\n  6. `↻ Main lagi` button.\n- **Toast** (above canvas): `position:fixed;left:50%;top:76px;transform:translateX(-50%)`, radius 14px, bg `#2a1a10` (or `--good`/`--bad`), white text 700 17px, animation `eduIn .3s`, disappears after 1500ms.\n- **Floating text** (floatText): Space Mono 700 24px, `transform:translate(-50%,-50%)`, animation `eduUp .9s forwards` (rises 140% + fade), color `--float-good`/`--float-bad`, disappears after 900ms.\n\n# MECHANICS\n- Canvas size: `H = min(innerHeight-90, 720)`, `W = min(innerWidth-20, round(H*1.15))`. Ratio ~1.15:1.\n- Invader grid: 7 columns × 3 rows = 21 random letters from the list of 27 hijaiyah letters.\n- `cw = min(78, W/(cols+2.5))` (cell width). Cell position: `x = ox + c*cw*1.25`, `y = oy + r*cw*1.05`. `ox = W*0.12`, `oy = 60`.\n- Row speed: `sp = 0.35 + wave*0.12` px/frame. Direction `dir = ±1`.\n- Edge bounce: if right edge > `W-10` or left edge < `10` → `dir *= -1` and `oy += 14` (descend).\n- Lose if `maxY > H-110` → lives 0, message \"Huruf sampai ke bawah!\".\n- Target: pick from living letters that **have no living letter in the same column with a lower row** (frontmost). HUD command: `Tembak huruf: <Nama>`.\n- Player bullet: speed `y -= 13`, cooldown 20 frames, spawn at `(p.x, H-60)`. Hit if `|dx| < cw*0.45` and `|dy| < cw*0.45`.\n- Enemy bullet: spawn every `max(30, 80 - wave*10)` frames from a random living letter, speed `y += 4`. Hits player if `|dx| < 22` and `H-62 < y < H-30`.\n- Player ship: `x` clamp `[30, W-30]`, speed 6 px/frame.\n- Score: correct +10, wrong −5 (min 0). Count `benar` and `salah`.\n- Maximum score for stars: 300 (used to compute stars 1–3).\n- Stars: `ceil(score/max*3)` clamp 1–3.\n\n# LEVELS & QUESTIONS\n- Not a multiple-choice quiz — the question is the **27 hijaiyah letters** whose names must be recognized. Data array above the script:\n  `[['ا','Alif'],['ب','Ba'],['ت','Ta'],['ث','Tsa'],['ج','Jim'],['ح','Ha'],['خ','Kho'],['د','Dal'],['ذ','Dzal'],['ر','Ro'],['ز','Zai'],['س','Sin'],['ش','Syin'],['ص','Shod'],['ض','Dhod'],['ط','Tho'],['ظ','Zho'],['ع','Ain'],['غ','Ghoin'],['ف','Fa'],['ق','Qof'],['ك','Kaf'],['ل','Lam'],['م','Mim'],['ن','Nun'],['و','Wawu'],['ي','Ya']]`\n- Each wave: 21 random letters out of 27 (no duplicates within a wave).\n- Wave advances when all letters are gone → `wave++`, speed increases, enemy bullets spawn faster.\n- Answer key = letter↔name pairs in the array above (already verified: ا=Alif, ب=Ba, ت=Ta, ث=Tsa, ج=Jim, ح=Ha, خ=Kho, د=Dal, ذ=Dzal, ر=Ro, ز=Zai, س=Sin, ش=Syin, ص=Shod, ض=Dhod, ط=Tho, ظ=Zho, ع=Ain, غ=Ghoin, ف=Fa, ق=Qof, ك=Kaf, ل=Lam, م=Mim, ن=Nun, و=Wawu, ي=Ya).\n\n# MOTION, FEEDBACK & SOUND\n- Loop: `requestAnimationFrame`, update only if `G.run`, draw always.\n- Background stars: 70 random points, `fillRect(x, (y + tick*speed*0.3) % H, 2, 2)`, alpha `0.15 + r*0.4`.\n- Invader: `roundRect(x-r, y-r, r*2, r*2, r*0.45)` with `r = cw*0.46`. Legs: two `fillRect` below. Letter: `font = 700 <r*1.35>px Amiri, serif`, `textAlign:center`, `textBaseline:middle`, color `--ink`.\n- When wrong: invader `flash = 20` frames → color `--inv-hit`, then back.\n- Explosion: 18 particles, random speed 0–4, lifetime 30 frames, color according to (correct `#5fe3a1`, wrong `#ff5a4a`, player hit `#fff`).\n- Ship: orange triangle `(p.x, H-64) → (p.x+24, H-36) → (p.x-24, H-36)`, nose `fillRect(p.x-4, H-72, 8, 12)` color `--ship-top`.\n- Player bullet: `fillRect(x-2, y-10, 4, 12)` color `--bullet`.\n- Enemy bullet: `arc(x, y, 4, 0, 7)` color `--ebullet`.\n- Command badge at bottom-right of canvas: `roundRect(W-150, H-28, 140, 24, 10)` bg `rgba(255,250,240,.95)`, text `Cari: <Nama>` 700 15px Space Grotesk color `#0f3b2e`.\n- Sound (Web Audio, no files, 🔊/🔇 button in HUD, save `edu_mute` in localStorage):\n  - `ok`: triangle 660Hz .07s → 880Hz .09s\n  - `bad`: square 220Hz .12s → 160Hz .16s\n  - `tick` (shoot): triangle 1200Hz .02s\n  - `boom`: sawtooth 90Hz .25s\n  - `win`: triangle 523→659→784→1046Hz\n  - Gain envelope: rise to .18 in .01s, fall to .0001 at the end.\n- CSS animations: `eduIn` (card entrance), `eduBob` (mascot), `eduFlash` (score/q bump), `eduUp` (floating text).\n\n# CONTROLS & RESPONSIVE\n- Keyboard: `ArrowLeft`/`ArrowRight` move, `Space` shoot (preventDefault).\n- Touch: bottom pad buttons — left `◀ ▶`, right `●`. Use `pointerdown`/`pointerup`/`pointerleave`/`pointercancel`.\n- Click/tap canvas: move ship to x position and shoot.\n- Touch pad hidden on desktop: `@media (hover:hover) and (pointer:fine){.edu-pad.touch{display:none}}`.\n- HUD on phones ≤640px: `flex-wrap:wrap`, font 13px, title hidden, command becomes a full row below.\n- Canvas responsive, no horizontal scroll at 360px. `overflow:hidden` on html/body.\n- `prefers-reduced-motion`: disable bob/flash/float animations when active.\n\n# TECHNICAL\n- ONE `index.html` file (pure HTML+CSS+JS). No build, no server, no API, no login. Ready for Netlify Drop.\n- Fonts via Google Fonts: `Amiri:wght@700`, `Space+Grotesk:wght@500;700`, `Space+Mono:wght@700`.\n- All images made with code (Canvas + inline SVG). No image files.\n- localStorage wrapped in try/catch: keys `edu_mute` (value '1'/'0'), `edu_best_hijaiyah` (best score number).\n- JS structure: one `G` object (state) + functions `size()`, `wave()`, `pickTarget()`, `start()`, `pos(v)`, `update()`, `hitInv(v)`, `boom()`, `over(m)`, `demo()`, `draw()`, `loop()`. Letter data in array `HJ` above the script.\n- HUD built once via function `hud({title, lives, credit})` that inserts elements `#eduQ`, `#eduScore`, `#eduLives`, `#eduMute`.\n- Helper functions: `setQ`, `setScore`, `setLives`, `toast`, `floatText`, `title`, `end`, `best`, `sfx`, `shuffle`, `pick`, `rand`.\n- Demo mode `?demo=1`: auto-start, auto-play (AI steers the ship toward the target, avoids bullets), auto-restart after 2.5s on the results screen.\n- Token-efficient: CSS variables + classes reused, one state object + render function per screen, repeated markup via loops, data in compact arrays, no long comments, write the complete code directly without explanation.\n\n# CHECK BEFORE FINISHING\n1. Game runs from title screen → play → results without console errors.\n2. All 27 letter↔name pairs are correct (ا=Alif … ي=Ya).\n3. No horizontal scroll on 360px phones; canvas and touch pad fit.\n4. 🔊/🔇 button works and is saved in localStorage.\n5. Best score is saved and shown on the title & results screens.\n6. Stars 1–3 appear according to score (max 300).\n7. Correct/wrong toast and floating text appear when shooting.\n8. `prefers-reduced-motion` disables non-essential animations.\n9. `?demo=1` mode auto-plays without input.\n10. One `index.html` file, no external dependencies other than Google Fonts."},{"id":"grammo","kat":"app","katN":"App","n":"Grammo English Grammar","mapel":"English","jenjang":"Middle school–General","topik":"Bilingual English grammar app: 12 topics, formulas, audio example sentences, 60 practice questions, and an irregular verb dictionary. Can be installed as a PWA.","img":"img/grammo.jpg","preview":"https://preview.edugamelabs.com/app/grammo/","prompt":"# ROLE\n- Art director + lead developer PWA. Rebuild \"Grammo English Grammar\" as ONE index.html file (inline CSS, JS, lesson data and SVG line icons), no build, no server/API/login.\n- Bilingual product: Bahasa Indonesia (default) and English, ID/EN toggle on many screens.\n\n# PRODUCT\n- English grammar app for junior high and general learners: 12 topics, formulas, audio example sentences, 60 practice questions (12 × 5), a dictionary of 25 irregular verbs, progress, badges, PWA.\n- Title \"Grammo English Grammar\"; lang=\"id\"; theme-color #D2F35C; apple-mobile-web-app-title \"Grammo\".\n- Manifest: name \"Grammo English Grammar\", display standalone, background #F2F3EE, green letter-G SVG icon. Simple cache-first service worker.\n- Desktop: left panel 300px, 390×844 phone frame, and \"All screens\" mode (board of 19 mini phones). Below 560px: full-screen, no panel.\n\n# VISUAL STYLE\n- Tokens (refer by name):\n  - --hutan:#163300 (main text, dark buttons, active tab)\n  - --hutan-2:#2A4A12 (today's bar)\n  - --teks-2:#454745 (paragraphs)\n  - --muted:#6F7369 (secondary labels)\n  - --lime:#9FE870 (primary buttons, progress bars)\n  - --lime-2:#8BD95A (button hover)\n  - --neon:#D2F35C (highlights, splash, active tab)\n  - --neon-soft:#F1FBD0 (focus ring)\n  - --bg:#F2F3EE (screen background), --kartu:#FFFFFF, --abu:#E8EAE3, --abu-2:#DCDFD5, --garis:#E3E5DD\n  - --pink:#FAD4F2, --pink-2:#F3B5E5, --mint:#E3F5D9, --krem:#F6F1E4\n  - --merah:#D2483E (errors), --merah-soft:#FCE6E3\n  - --papan:#DDEBD9 (board mode background); body background #E9EEE4\n  - Others: #22301A (floating nav and CTA), #111 (phone frame), #0F1A0A (arrow button), #3C9B3A (correct border), #8A2A22 (wrong text)\n  - Gradients: student card #B6EE8E→#9FE870→#8ADB5C; profile banner #8DA6C4→#D6B4D6→#F3B98C→#F0A06B; result ribbon #F3B5E5→#B9A4F0→#8FC6EE and #9FE870→#D2F35C.\n- Fonts: Plus Jakarta Sans (400–800, main), Anton (giant headings), Unbounded (500–700, headings and brand).\n- Scale: h1 26px/800; h2 19px/800; h3 15px/800; body 14px/1.62 teks-2; meta 12px/600 muted; kicker 10.5px/700 uppercase; giant Anton uppercase line-height .92 (58px welcome, 64px result, 44px dictionary).\n- Radius: pill 999px; cards 18px; banner 20px; question card 22px; feedback sheet 26px on top; phone frame 56px (screen 47px).\n- Shadows: student card 0 18px 34px rgba(22,51,0,.16); floating sentence card 0 12px 30px rgba(22,51,0,.10); floating nav 0 14px 30px rgba(22,51,0,.28).\n- Decorative flower: 8 ellipses around a centre circle (grid 100), colour per banner. Line icons on a 24 grid, stroke 1.9, round ends (home, chart, book, person, bell, and topic icons block, spin, rise, key). Social buttons: 4-colour G icon.\n\n# SCREENS & NAVIGATION\n- Flow: splash 2.4 s → onboarding → welcome → log in or sign up → home. A saved name goes straight to home.\n- Floating nav with 4 round 48px buttons: Home (house), Progress (chart), Dictionary (book), Profile (person); active neon with scale 1.05.\n- splash: full neon background; \"Grammo\" Unbounded 700 38px; sub \"English Grammar · ID / EN\"; 64×4px loading bar.\n- onboarding (white background): 400px visual, h1 27px/600, dots, \"Lewati\"/\"Skip\" link, dark round 52px button (arrow; tick on last slide). Slide 1 \"Belajar grammar / jadi seru di sini\" (EN \"Learn grammar / the fun way here\"): three floating sentence cards \"Simple Present — She plays the guitar.\", \"Adjective — a red bag\", \"Simple Past — We went home.\". Slide 2 \"Rumus jelas, / contoh kalimat nyata\": dark card 230px \"FORMULA S + V2 + O\" and green card \"✓ Correct · I visited Bali.\". Slide 3 \"Lebih dari 60 soal / latihan menunggumu\": three stacked cards \"12 topik grammar\" (neon), \"60 soal latihan\" (white), \"25 kata kerja tak beraturan\" (mint).\n- welcome (white): language toggle top right; 250px orbit: green gradient core reading \"Aa\" in Anton 58px, with a ring rotating every 22 s holding 6 chips (Noun pink, Verb neon, a / an white, will mint, -ed neon, Tenses white). Giant title \"GRAMMAR / jadi gampang\" (EN \"made easy\"); body \"Rumus jelas. Latihan seru.\" (EN \"Clear rules. Fun practice.\"); lime \"Masuk\"/\"Log in\" button and grey \"Daftar\"/\"Sign up\" button (school icon).\n- login: heading \"Halo lagi!\"/\"We Say Hello!\" centred; subtitle \"Selamat datang kembali. Masukkan nama dan kata sandi untuk masuk.\"; pill fields Name (person icon) and Password (lock icon, eye button); \"Lupa kata sandi?\" (toast \"Minta guru untuk mengatur ulang\"); lime \"Masuk\" button; \"Atau masuk dengan\"; three 46px social buttons; footer \"Belum punya akun? Daftar\".\n- sign up: same heading; subtitle \"Buat akun gratis untuk menyimpan progres belajarmu.\"; fields Nama, Kelas (e.g. Kelas 8), Buat kata sandi, Ulangi kata sandi; \"Daftar\" button; social buttons; footer \"Sudah punya akun? Masuk\".\n- home: header with a 42px neon avatar showing initials, \"Grammo\" brand in Unbounded 22px, bell with a red dot. Search pill \"Cari topik grammar…\". Greeting \"Hai, {nama}!\" + language toggle. Three-slide banner carousel (advances every 4.5 s): \"Semua Grammar, Satu Tempat\" (pink flower) → Parts of Speech; \"Tenses Tanpa Pusing\" (neon) → Simple Present; \"Kamus Kata Kerja\" (mint) → dictionary; \"Pelajari\"/\"Learn More\" button. Section \"Lanjutkan Belajar\": horizontal cards at 74% width for the last 4 topics opened. Section \"Topik\" with pills Semua 12 / Selesai n / Belum n. Topic cards: 42px icon box in the category colour (Tenses lime, Jenis Kata pink, Kalimat mint; completed: forest green with neon tick), EN title, summary, % bar.\n- topic: white header with 28px bottom curve: back button, language toggle; 64px icon box; EN title in Unbounded 22px; meta \"ID · category · level\"; five round buttons: listen, bulb (Kesalahan umum), book (dictionary), globe (language), flag (practice); stats: examples, formulas, questions, best score \"n/5\" or \"–\". Tabs Materi/Lesson, Contoh/Examples, Latihan/Practice. Floating CTA \"Mulai Latihan\"/\"Start Practice\".\n  - Materi: Penjelasan (lime \"English\"/\"Indonesian\" pill for translation); Rumus (*word* highlighted in neon, bar shrinks per row); Kapan dipakai (three numbered neon items); Kata kunci (mint chips); Kesalahan umum (wrong crossed out on light red, right in mint).\n  - Contoh: rows with a listen button, bold English sentence, Indonesian meaning blurred by 5px until tapped.\n  - Latihan: 5 questions, chips \"± 3 menit\" and \"+10 XP / benar\", History up to 4 attempts.\n- quiz: close button, progress bar, \"1/5\"; h2 \"Pilih jawaban yang tepat\"; question card with a blank box (neon when chosen, red if wrong); four pill options A–D; \"Cek jawaban\" (grey until a choice). Feedback sheet: mint \"Benar!\"/\"Correct!\" or light-red \"Belum tepat\"/\"Not quite\" + explanation + \"Lanjut\"/\"Continue\".\n- result: 190×220 SVG ribbon swaying with six confetti pieces; h1 \"Kamu makin jago\"/\"It all adds up\" 64px; score \"n/5 BENAR\"/\"n/5 CORRECT\" in green Anton; XP text; \"Oke\"/\"Done\" (lime) and \"Ulangi\"/\"Try again\" (grey).\n- progress: XP balance (counts up over 900 ms); 3D student card (tilts ±8 degrees, \"Level N\"); three actions \"Kuis acak\"/\"Random quiz\", \"Kamus\", \"Pengingat\"/\"Reminders\"; lime card \"Minggu ini\"/\"This week\" with 7 daily bars; summary of correct answers, topics completed n/12, lessons opened.\n- dictionary: giant 44px title \"Irregular verbs\"; columns V1 V2 V3; tap a row to hear it; search \"go, makan, written…\".\n- profile: 150px gradient banner \"Profil\"/\"Profile\"; 92px neon avatar; name, \"Kelas · Sekolah · Level N\"; \"Tentang\"/\"About\"; \"Lencana\"/\"Badges\" six 52px tiles (active neon, otherwise grey: Langkah pertama, Nilai sempurna, Ahli tenses, 100 XP, 5 topik, Tamat); \"Riwayat\"; grey \"Edit Akun\"/\"Edit Account\" and \"Keluar\"/\"Log out\" buttons.\n- notifications: kicker \"Hari ini\"/\"Today\"; four items: Target harian, Tips grammar, Topik berikutnya, Lencana (with time); lime \"Buka {topik}\"/\"Open {topik}\" button.\n- edit: banner with a camera button (toast \"Unggah foto segera hadir\"), fields Nama, Kelas, Sekolah, Target harian (1–120), Bahasa, Bunyi klik; lime \"Simpan\"; red \"Hapus semua progres\".\n- board: heading \"High Fidelity Design\" 46px/800 and \"Grammo\" brand 40px; grid of 19 mini phones 232×502 (scale .564), labelled and numbered to match the screens above; button \"Coba app secara interaktif →\".\n\n# FEATURES & LOGIC\n- State S in localStorage \"grammo-v1\" (try/catch): skrin, onb, nama, kelas \"Kelas 8\", sekolah \"\", target 10, bahasa \"id\", skor{}, lihat{}, dibuka{}, xp 0, xpHari{}, riwayat[], bunyi true. Empty name: splash; otherwise home.\n- XP: first opening of the Materi tab per topic +5; first opening of the Contoh tab +5; each correct answer +10 (recorded for today). Level = 1 + XP divided by 100, rounded down.\n- Quiz: 5 questions per topic. Topic score = highest result (0–5); completed when score ≥4. History keeps 30 entries. Random quiz: 5 random questions from all 60, without changing topic scores.\n- Topic percentage = materi 30 + contoh 20 + score/5×50, rounded.\n- Login without a server: name required, password at least 4 characters. Social icons = quick login as \"Siswa Grammo\".\n- Log out clears the name and returns to welcome. Reset all progress keeps name, class, school, language and target.\n- Click sound: WebAudio 660 Hz decaying over .12 s, can be switched off. Speech: speechSynthesis en-US, rate .9.\n- Board mode uses demo data \"Rina Putri\", Kelas 8, SMP Negeri 1, XP 260, scores parts 5, present 4, past 3.\n\n# CONTENT & DATA\n- 12 topics (id — EN / ID title — category, level — key formula — quiz question with answer):\n- parts — Parts of Speech / Jenis-jenis Kata — Jenis Kata, Dasar — 8 word types (noun, verb, adjective, adverb, pronoun, preposition, conjunction, interjection) — \"My brother is very ___ .\" tall / tallly / tallness / talls → tall (A).\n- present — Simple Present — Tenses, Dasar — (+) S + V1 (-s/-es) + O; (−) do/does not + V1; (?) Do/Does + S + V1 — \"My cat ___ fish every day.\" → eats (B).\n- continuous — Present Continuous — Tenses, Dasar — S + am/is/are + V-ing — \"Listen! Someone ___ the piano.\" → is playing (C).\n- past — Simple Past — Tenses, Dasar — S + V2; did not + V1; Did + S + V1 — \"Yesterday I ___ a cat in the park.\" → saw (C).\n- pastcont — Past Continuous — Tenses, Menengah — was/were + V-ing — \"I ___ dinner when you called.\" → was having (A).\n- perfect — Present Perfect — Tenses, Menengah — have/has + V3 — \"I ___ never ___ snow.\" → have / seen (C).\n- future — Simple Future — Tenses, Dasar — will + V1; am/is/are going to + V1; won't — \"Don't worry, I ___ tell anyone.\" → won't (A).\n- articles — Articles: a, an, the — Jenis Kata, Dasar — \"I ate ___ orange.\" → an (B).\n- pronouns — Pronouns — Jenis Kata, Dasar — \"Please give ___ the ball.\" → me (B).\n- compare — Comparatives & Superlatives — Jenis Kata, Menengah — -er + than; the -est; good → better → the best — \"Jakarta is ___ city in Indonesia.\" → the biggest (A).\n- modals — Modal Verbs: can, must, should — Kalimat, Menengah — \"Birds ___ fly.\" → can (A).\n- passive — Passive Voice — Kalimat, Lanjut — is/was/will be + V3 — \"The cake ___ by my sister.\" → was made (B).\n- Each topic: 2 common mistakes (wrong → right) and 4 audio example sentences, e.g. \"The *small* cat *sleeps* *quietly*.\" (Kucing kecil itu tidur dengan tenang.).\n- Dictionary of 25 verbs (V1 · V2 · V3 · meaning): be · was/were · been · adalah; begin · began · begun · mulai; break · broke · broken · memecahkan; bring · brought · brought · membawa; buy · bought · bought · membeli; come · came · come · datang; do · did · done · melakukan; drink · drank · drunk · minum; eat · ate · eaten · makan; find · found · found · menemukan; get · got · got/gotten · mendapat; give · gave · given · memberi; go · went · gone · pergi; have · had · had · punya; know · knew · known · tahu; make · made · made · membuat; read · read · read · membaca; run · ran · run · berlari; say · said · said · berkata; see · saw · seen · melihat; speak · spoke · spoken · berbicara; swim · swam · swum · berenang; take · took · taken · mengambil; teach · taught · taught · mengajar; write · wrote · written · menulis.\n\n# MOTION & FEEDBACK\n- Screen changes fade with a 14px slide over 0.45 s; elements rise in sequence with 60 ms gaps; giant titles appear word by word. Splash: brand blooms with a spring over 0.9 s, loading bar 2.2 s. Button ripple 0.6 s. Student card shine 3.5 s. Wrong answers shake 6px. Confetti 70 pieces over 1.8–3.2 s. Toast 2.4 s.\n\n# RESPONSIVE & ACCESSIBILITY\n- Below 560px: full screen 100dvh, no notch, bottom nav uses safe-area. A 360px screen has no horizontal scroll; horizontal cards use scroll-snap.\n- Minimum target 42px; focus ring; icons have aria-labels; prefers-reduced-motion disables animations.\n\n# TECHNICAL\n- ONE index.html file (CSS, JS, data and icons inline) plus manifest.webmanifest and a simple sw.js (cache-first). No build, framework, server, API or login.\n- Google Fonts: Plus Jakarta Sans 400–800, Anton, Unbounded 500–700.\n- All visuals are generated in code (icons, flowers, shine, ribbon, confetti). One state object S and one render function per screen; repeated markup via loops.\n- localStorage \"grammo-v1\" wrapped in try/catch. Service worker registered on http/https only. Write the full code directly.\n\n# CHECK BEFORE FINISHING\n- Splash → onboarding → welcome → login/sign up → home works; every screen can be opened.\n- 12 topics and 60 questions with correct keys; score, XP, badges and history saved; the ID/EN toggle changes all labels.\n- Board mode shows 19 mini phones; one index.html; neat at 360px."},{"id":"cakap-v1","kat":"app","katN":"App","n":"Cakap · Version 1 (orange sun)","mapel":"English","jenjang":"Primary school","topik":"One of 5 UI versions of Cakap: orange sunburst background with thick brown lines and framed cards.","img":"img/cakap-v1.jpg","preview":"https://preview.edugamelabs.com/app/cakap-v1/","prompt":"# ROLE\n- Art director + lead web developer. Rebuild the app \"Cakap · Version 1 (orange sun)\" as ONE `index.html` file (plain HTML+CSS+JS, no build, no framework, no server/API/login).\n- Default UI language Indonesian, with an ID/EN toggle on the Pick Grade and Profile screens. Content: English for primary-school kids.\n\n# PRODUCT\n- Name: **Cakap**. Subtitle: \"Belajar Bahasa Inggris untuk Anak SD\". Look: orange sun poster, thick brown outlines.\n- Meta: `lang=\"id\"`, title \"Cakap · Versi 1\", description \"Cakap — belajar Bahasa Inggris untuk anak SD Indonesia. Versi 1.\", theme-color `#FFA024`, viewport `width=device-width,initial-scale=1,maximum-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover`.\n- Inline SVG favicon: rx22 square `#131313`, circle `#FFA024` cy52 r28, two eyes `#131313` r4 at (40,47) and (60,47).\n- Content: 6 units × 3 lessons + 1 review per unit = 24 steps. Each lesson: 4 cards, 3 quiz questions, 1 speaking sentence.\n- One phone frame 390×844 centred on the page (see VISUAL STYLE).\n\n# VISUAL STYLE\nColour tokens (write once, refer by name):\n- `--jg:#FFA024` main orange (phone bg, buttons, round buttons)\n- `--jg2:#FFB547` light orange (spare)\n- `--ck:#6A2E0B` thick brown (outlines, main text, shadows)\n- `--mr:#D4474A` red (recording mode, Wrong background, heart icon)\n- `--hj:#2E9A55` green (secondary buttons, done state)\n- `--bi:#1E85B0` blue (Level, Card, Quiz, Speaking backgrounds; chart bars)\n- `--kn:#FFD23F` yellow (active choices, yellow cards)\n- `--kr:#FFF4DA` cream (info cards, bottom dock)\n- `--pt:#fff` white\n- Extra colours: `#FF8A3D` dark orange (mascot, star icon), `#7BD389` light green, `#7CC6FE` light blue, `#FF9EB5` pink, `#C9A7FF` purple, `#FF8FA3` cheeks, `#FFCB3F`/`#FFD866` yellow Correct background, `#2F9E56` Home background, `#FFA42B`/`#FFB44E` sun background, `#B8F0B8` correct-answer box, `#d8c3a5` disabled button, `#8a6b4a` disabled shadow, `#e3c79c` dots and dashed lines, `#a1481a` secondary brown text, `#FFF8E8` phone border, `#131313` black icon (favicon).\n- Google fonts: **Lilita One** 400 (titles, buttons, numbers), **Nunito** 600/700/800 (body text), **Material Symbols Rounded** (ligature icons, FILL 1, opsz 24).\n- Screen backgrounds (repeating-conic-gradient; dots with radial-gradient white .12 3px, size 30px):\n  - sun: `repeating-conic-gradient(from 0deg at 50% 26%,#FFA42B 0 9deg,#FFB44E 9deg 18deg)` (onboarding, profile)\n  - blue: `#1E85B0` + dots (level, card, quiz, speaking)\n  - green: `#2F9E56` + dots (home, progress)\n  - red: `#D4474A` + dots .1 (path, wrong)\n  - yellow: repeating `#FFCB3F`/`#FFD866` (correct, ranking)\n- Page `.panggung` background: `repeating-conic-gradient(from 0deg at 50% 40%,#FFA83A 0 9deg,#FFB955 9deg 18deg)`, padding 24px.\n- Phone: 390×844, border 10px `#FFF8E8`, radius 50px, bg `--jg`, shadow `0 0 0 4px var(--ck), 0 26px 60px rgba(60,25,5,.35)`. On screens ≤600px wide or ≤900px tall: full 100dvh, no border, radius or shadow.\n- Status bar: padding `max(14px,safe-area) 28px 2px`, Nunito 800 14px in ck. Left: clock H:mm (updates every 20 s). Right: two 16px icons signal_cellular_alt, battery_full.\n- Screens: padding 8px 20px 22px, gap 14px, vertical scroll with hidden scrollbar. Enter animation .28s `cubic-bezier(.22,.9,.3,1)`: opacity 0→1 and translateY 10px→0.\n- Typography: `.jd1` Lilita 28px white, stroke 6px ck, paint-order stroke fill. `.logo1` Lilita 70px orange, stroke 12px ck, text-shadow `0 7px 0 ck`. `.jd2` Lilita 26px ck. `.big1` Lilita 38px. `.jam1` Lilita 54px yellow, stroke 8px ck. `.isi1` Nunito 700 15px/1.4. `.sub1` Nunito 800 15px/1.3 max 250px. Small labels `.mn` Nunito 800 13px.\n- Button `.tb`: Lilita 22px white with 5px ck stroke, orange bg, 3px ck border, radius 999px, padding 12px 26px, min-height 54px, shadow `0 6px 0 ck`, margin-bottom 6px. Pressed: translateY(4px), shadow `0 2px 0 ck`. Variants: `.hj` green bg; `.pt` white bg, ck text, no stroke; `.sm` 17px, padding 8px 18px, min 42px, 4px stroke; `.lebar` width 100%; disabled bg `#d8c3a5`, shadow `0 6px 0 #8a6b4a`.\n- Round button `.rb`: 46px, orange, 3px ck border, white icon, shadow `0 4px 0 ck`. `.rb.ghost` invisible (balance).\n- Card `.kt`: white, 3px ck border, radius 30px, padding 16px, shadow `0 6px 0 ck`. Variants `.kn` yellow, `.kr` cream.\n- Choice pill `.pil`: white, 3px ck border, radius 26px, padding 12px 14px, shadow `0 5px 0 ck`. Active bg yellow. Tick badge `.cb` 30px green, 3px ck border, top-right (top -10px, right -6px).\n- Quiz option `.opt1`: white, 3px ck border, radius 24px, padding 11px 14px, min-height 56px, Nunito 800 16px, shadow `0 5px 0 ck`. Letter A–D `.hr` 34px cream circle, 3px border, Lilita 17px. Active: yellow bg, `.hr` ck bg with yellow text.\n- Lesson row `.cd1`: white, 3px ck border, radius 26px, padding 12px 12px 12px 16px, shadow `0 5px 0 ck`.\n- Chip `.ch1`: white, 3px ck border, radius 14px, Nunito 800 14px, min-width 56px. Active yellow.\n- Dot `.dot1`: 30×9px radius 9px colour `#e3c79c`. Active orange, 11px tall, 2px ck border.\n- Bar `.bar1`: 16px tall, white bg, 3px ck border, green fill with 3px ck right border.\n- Dock `.dock` (bottom): cream bg, padding 10px 16px, border-top 3px ck. 4 buttons 56×50px radius 18px, icon ck opacity .55. Active: orange bg, 3px ck border, white icon, shadow `0 3px 0 ck`, opacity 1.\n- Timer `.stop` (quiz): 150px orange circle, 4px ck border, shadow `0 7px 0 ck`, with small tab above (36×20 radius 8px 8px 0 0, top -22px). Inside a 112px white circle with 4px ck border, text \"1/3\" Lilita 40px.\n- Mic `.mik`: 104px orange, 4px ck border, shadow `0 7px 0 ck`, white 48px icon. While recording bg `#D4474A`.\n- Waveform `.gel`: 84px tall, bars radius 99px, gap 5px, bg ck, opacity .5 (1 while recording).\n- Chart `.gf`: 130px tall. Blue bars `--bi`, 3px ck border, radius 10px 10px 4px 4px. Today orange.\n- Ranking row `.rank1`: white, 3px ck border, radius 22px, padding 8px 14px 8px 10px, shadow `0 4px 0 ck`. Your row: yellow bg.\n- Toast: absolute top 62px, pill, bg ck, white Nunito 700 14px text, visible 1.9 s.\n- Onboarding sun box `.logo-box`: 190px circle, white 55%.\n\n\"Cakap\" mascot (geometric, built from div + border-radius, not an image):\n- Size w; k = w/64. Shape cycles (i%7): round 50%, square 26k px, drop `50% 50% 26k 50%`, tag `22k 22k 22k 6k`, leaf `50% 50% 50% 14k`, card `36k 36k 8k 36k`, tail `30k 30k 30k 8k`.\n- Fill cycles (i%6): `#FFD23F`, `#FF8A3D`, `#7BD389`, `#7CC6FE`, `#FF9EB5`, `#C9A7FF`. Outline 3px solid ck.\n- \"Big\" eyes: two white ovals 12k×14k, 2k ck border, with a 6k ck dot at their bottom.\n- Default mouth: 24k×12k, 3k ck border, no top border, radius 0 0 24k 24k (smile). Variants: sad (arc on top), line (straight 24k×3.9k), round (circle), wide (solid ck fill).\n- Cheeks: two pink `#FF8FA3` circles 13k at left and right (12% from each edge), 52% of height.\n- Badge (optional): yellow `#FFDD57` circle 30% of width, 3px ck border, ck tick at top-right.\n- Confetti: 34 pieces 9×14px radius 2px, colours `#FFD23F, #FF8A3D, #7BD389, #7CC6FE, #FF9EB5, #fff`, fall 1.5 s ease-in to translateY(900px) rotate(720deg), opacity 0.\n\n# NAVIGATION & SCREENS\nSix main screens plus the grade pick, in exactly this order. Each screen is a `section`; the `active` class switches. The dock shows only on Home, Path, Progress and Profile.\n1. **Onboarding step 1** (sun bg): yellow square mascot 150px inside a cream circle, title \"Cakap\" (logo1), subtitle \"Belajar Bahasa Inggris untuk Anak SD\". Below: cream scalloped edge `.skalop`, then a cream panel with \"Siap Bicara Bahasa Inggris?\" and a full-width \"Mulai\" button (→ step 2).\n2. **Onboarding step 2**: top row \"Cakap\" (jam1 30px) and \"Lewati\" button (→ Pick Grade). Cream card: green drop mascot 120px floating; title \"Waktu yang Anak Bisa Lihat!\"; text \"Belajar 10 menit sehari, dengan cara kita. Bahasa Indonesia memandu, Bahasa Inggris melatih.\"; 3 dots (second active); round back button and \"Lanjut\" (→ Pick Grade).\n3. **Pick Grade** (blue bg): header \"Pilih Kelasmu\". White text \"Materi akan disesuaikan dengan kelasmu.\" Three pills: A1 \"Pemula · Beginner\" (Kelas 1–2 · Kata sehari-hari & kalimat pendek.), A2 \"Menengah\" (Kelas 3–4 · Sudah bisa sedikit, ingin lebih berani.), B1 \"Mahir\" (Kelas 5–6 · Tata bahasa & menulis kalimat sendiri). Tile colours: A1 `#7BD389`, A2 `#7CC6FE`, B1 `#FF8A3D`, 30px text. Cream card below: \"Bahasa antarmuka\" + ID/EN toggle, then full-width green \"Lanjut\" (→ Home).\n4. **Home** (green bg): HUD row: star pill (star icon dark orange, total XP), title \"Hari Ini\", fire pill (local_fire_department icon, streak). Yellow card: \"Hei Juara, {first name}!\" + \"Lanjutkan pelajaranmu.\" + green \"Pilih\" button (→ active lesson); orange card mascot 110px floating on the right. Three `.cd1` rows for the next lessons (EN title Lilita 21px, timer icon + type + \" · 5 mnt\", \"Pilih\" button, small mascot on the right). White full-width \"Latihan Ucapan\" button with mic icon (→ solo speaking).\n5. **Learning Path** (red bg): back header, title, tune icon \"Ganti unit\". Two unit pills: active unit (tick badge, 64px mascot, \"Unit N\", EN name) and next unit (opacity .9, tap = change unit). Status chips row (▶/✓/🔒 + number). White card with 4 `cd1` rows: 38px circle (green ✓ if done, ck ▶ if current, grey lock if locked), EN title Lilita 18px, IDN. Full-width \"Mulai\" button below (→ active lesson).\n6. **Vocabulary Card** (blue bg): header close button (close icon → Path), counter \"1/4\" (jam1), sound button. Large white card: green tag with the word type, 56px mascot on the right; word Lilita 52px; IPA 18px `#a1481a`; dashed line; label \"Artinya dalam Bahasa Indonesia\" 12px uppercase; meaning Lilita 30px; cream box with the EN example (keyword highlighted yellow) and ID translation. Bottom buttons: \"Belum hafal\" (white) and \"Sudah hafal\" (green) → next card; after the last card → Quiz.\n7. **Quiz** (blue bg): header close, \"Soal N/3\" (jd1), red heart pill (3 lives left). Decorative timer circle \"i/n\". White card: hint \"Pilih terjemahan yang benar\" (if audio) or \"Pilih jawaban yang tepat\"; question text Lilita 28px (22px if over 34 characters), sound button if audio. Four options A–D. Full-width \"Periksa Jawaban\" button (disabled until a choice is made).\n8. **Correct** (yellow bg): white 120px mascot with line eyes, wide mouth, badge. \"Benar!\" logo1 56px. \"That's correct — well done.\" Cream \"Catatan\" card: title, body, chips. Two stat cards: \"Hadiah +15 XP\" (white) and \"Ketepatan N%\" (ck bg, yellow number). Green \"Lanjutkan\" button + round save button.\n9. **Wrong** (red bg): header close, \"Ups!\", heart. White sad mascot 92px and \"Belum tepat\" logo1 46px white. Card \"Jawabanmu\" (struck through), mint box `#B8F0B8` \"Jawaban benar\" (differing words highlighted), cream \"Kenapa?\" card with note body. \"Coba Lagi\" (ck) and \"Simpan ke Ulangan\" (white) buttons.\n10. **Speaking Practice** (blue bg): back header (→ Path) \"Latihan Ucapan\" + help button (toast \"Tekan dan tahan mikrofon\"). Card: \"Ucapkan setelah saya\" + sentence Lilita 32px + translation + waveform. Title \"Kata yang perlu diperbaiki\": keyword chip in yellow with the word + IPA; other words green with ✓. Below: orange 104px mic (press and hold), text \"Tekan dan tahan untuk merekam\", buttons \"Pelan\" and \"Lewati\".\n11. **Ranking** (yellow bg): back header (→ Profile), title \"Peringkat\", period toggle button. Yellow card \"Kelas 5 Melati · Mingguan\" with trophy icon and \"3 hari lagi sebelum minggu berakhir\". `.rank1` rows for 6 people (top 3 use 🥇🥈🥉). Your row yellow. Green \"Ajak Teman\" button (copies code 5MLT-26).\n12. **My Progress** (green bg): header (trophy button → Ranking), title \"Kemajuanku\". Period chips Minggu/Bulan/Tahun. Card: \"Menit belajar {period}\", big number \"{minutes} mnt\", pill \"+22%\". 7-day chart Sen–Min. Three small cards: Kata, Ketepatan, Hari. \"Kemahiran\" card: Kosa kata, Ucapan, Tata bahasa (green bars).\n13. **My Profile** (sun bg): header with name-edit button. Cream card: 100px yellow square mascot, name Lilita 26px, \"SDN 03 Menteng · 5 Melati\", pills \"Tingkat A1\" (green) and \"1940 XP\". Settings card: Interface language (ID/EN toggle), Pengingat harian (on toggle, \"Setiap hari, pukul 19.00\"), Pelajaran luring (off toggle), Kode kelas guru 5MLT-26. Buttons \"Peringkat Kelas\" (→ Ranking) and \"Mulai Ulang Kemajuan\" (red, confirmation).\n- Bottom dock: Home, Path, Progress, Profile (icons home, format_list_numbered, bar_chart, person). Ranking highlights the Profile icon.\n\nStart order: Onboarding step 1 → 2 → Pick Grade → Home. Data is saved; reopening shows the last screen based on state.\n\n# FEATURES & LOGIC\n- Single state `S` in localStorage key `cakap-id-v1`. Defaults: `{nama:'Aisyah Nabila',level:'A1',bahasa:'ID',xp:1940,beruntun:12,menit:184,xpMinggu:1240,kata:412,benar:0,jawab:0,selesai:{},hafal:{},simpan:[],suis:{ingat:true,luring:false},hariMenit:[40,62,30,78,52,84,22]}`. Every read and write wrapped in try/catch.\n- `langkahBerjalan()` = first step not yet done. Other steps stay locked until the one before is done (completed steps stay open).\n- Lesson flow: cards (4) → quiz (3 questions) → speaking sentence → complete. Correct: +15 XP. Wrong: lives -1 (of 3); \"Coba Lagi\" repeats the same question. If lives are 0 when retrying: lives reset to 3, start from question 1.\n- Lesson complete: +20 XP (+ XP earned from speaking), +8 minutes to today in `hariMenit`, confetti, toast \"Pelajaran “{title}” selesai! +N XP\", back to Path after 0.9 s.\n- Speaking: press and hold the mic, record up to 5 s, release to finish. Under 400 ms: toast \"Tahan sedikit lebih lama ya\". Otherwise a random score of 78–98 percent, +10 XP, continue after 0.8 s. Solo mode (from Home) returns to Home.\n- Unit review: 4 cards (indexes 0,3,6,9 of the unit's 12 cards), then the first 3 questions of each lesson in the unit, and the first sentence of the unit.\n- \"Sudah hafal\" adds the word to `S.hafal` and sets `S.kata = 412 + number of memorised words`.\n- \"Simpan ke Ulangan\": saves the question text to `S.simpan` (no duplicates), toast \"Disimpan ke ulangan\", then retry.\n- Change unit (tune icon): moves to the next unit, modulo 6.\n- Invite friends: copies \"5MLT-26\" to the clipboard (try/catch), toast \"Kode kelas 5MLT-26 disalin\".\n- Edit name: prompt, max 24 characters, saved.\n- Reset: confirmation, back to initial state, Onboarding step 1.\n- Ranking: 5 fixed rivals + your row (name and XP from state), sorted descending. Period button: Mingguan (×1) and Bulanan (×4). Your row shows \"X XP lagi untuk naik\" relative to the person above.\n- Progress: period Minggu (×1 minutes), Bulan (×4), Tahun (×48). Chart uses `hariMenit`; the tallest bar = maximum.\n- Quiz audio: the sound button plays `speechSynthesis` (en-GB, rate .92 normal, .55 slow, pitch 1.05). Choose a female voice if available.\n- Status bar clock: `H:mm`, updates every 20 seconds.\n\n# CONTENT & DATA\n- Data is in Indonesian and English exactly as listed below (product text, not translated). Only the labels around it follow this prompt.\n- Format: units, lessons (ID / EN title, type), cards (word /IPA/ word type = meaning | EN example = ID example), questions (question | A / B / C / D | answer | note), speaking sentences (EN | ID | keyword | IPA).\nUnit 1 · Sapaan & Perkenalan (Greetings)\n- L1 Halo & Pamit (Hello & Goodbye) · Kosa kata\n  - Kartu: Hello /həˈloʊ/ sapaan = Halo | Hello, I am Rani. = Halo, saya Rani. · Good morning /ɡʊd ˈmɔːrnɪŋ/ sapaan = Selamat pagi | Good morning, teacher. = Selamat pagi, Bu Guru. · Goodbye /ɡʊdˈbaɪ/ sapaan = Selamat tinggal | Goodbye, see you tomorrow. = Selamat tinggal, sampai jumpa besok. · Thank you /ˈθæŋk juː/ ungkapan = Terima kasih | Thank you for the book. = Terima kasih untuk bukunya.\n  - Soal: [audio] “Good morning, teacher.” | Selamat malam, Bu Guru / Selamat pagi, Bu Guru / Selamat tinggal, Bu Guru / Terima kasih, Bu Guru | B | “Good morning” = pagi, dipakai sampai sekitar pukul 12 siang. · Ibu guru memberimu buku. Apa yang kamu katakan? | Goodbye! / Hello! / Thank you! / Good night! | C | “Thank you” = Terima kasih. · “Sampai jumpa besok!” dalam bahasa Inggris adalah… | See you tomorrow! / See you yesterday! / Look you tomorrow! / Meet you morning! | A | “See you tomorrow”.\n  - Ucapan: Good morning, teacher! | Selamat pagi, Bu Guru! | morning | /ˈmɔːrnɪŋ/\n- L2 Apa Kabar? (How Are You?) · Ucapan\n  - Kartu: How are you? /haʊ ɑːr juː/ pertanyaan = Apa kabar? | How are you? I am fine. = Apa kabar? Saya baik. · I'm fine /aɪm faɪn/ jawaban = Saya baik | I'm fine, thank you. = Saya baik, terima kasih. · Nice to meet you /naɪs tə miːt juː/ ungkapan = Senang bertemu denganmu | Nice to meet you, Rani. = Senang bertemu denganmu, Rani. · See you /siː juː/ ungkapan = Sampai jumpa | See you on Monday. = Sampai jumpa hari Senin.\n  - Soal: [audio] “How are you?” | Siapa namamu? / Apa kabar? / Di mana kamu? / Kamu mau apa? | B | “How are you?” = Apa kabar? · Temanmu bertanya “How are you?”. Jawaban yang tepat… | I'm fine, thank you. / My name is Rani. / Goodbye! / It is a book. | A | Jawab pertanyaan kabar. · Saat berkenalan, kita berkata… | See you! / Nice to meet you. / Thank you for the food. / Good night. | B | “Nice to meet you”.\n  - Ucapan: How are you today? | Apa kabar hari ini? | today | /təˈdeɪ/\n- L3 Nama Saya… (My Name Is…) · Tata bahasa\n  - Kartu: name /neɪm/ kata benda = nama | My name is Rani. = Namaku Rani. · my /maɪ/ kata ganti = milikku | This is my bag. = Ini tasku. · I am /aɪ æm/ kata kerja = saya adalah | I am ten years old. = Saya berumur sepuluh tahun. · friend /frend/ kata benda = teman | He is my friend. = Dia temanku.\n  - Soal: Lengkapi: “___ name is Rani.” | Me / My / I / Mine | B | “My name is…”. · Lengkapi: “I ___ ten years old.” | is / are / am / be | C | “I am…”. · “Dia temanku.” dalam bahasa Inggris… | He is my friend. / He is me friend. / His my friend. / He are my friend. | A | “He is my friend”.\n  - Ucapan: My name is Aisyah. | Nama saya Aisyah. | name | /neɪm/\n\nUnit 2 · Angka & Warna (Numbers & Colours)\n- L1 Angka 1–20 (Numbers 1–20) · Kosa kata\n  - Kartu: five /faɪv/ angka = lima | I have five books. = Saya punya lima buku. · ten /ten/ angka = sepuluh | Ten pencils, please. = Sepuluh pensil, ya. · twelve /twelv/ angka = dua belas | I have twelve pencils. = Saya punya dua belas pensil. · twenty /ˈtwenti/ angka = dua puluh | Twenty students are here. = Dua puluh siswa ada di sini.\n  - Soal: Angka 12 dalam bahasa Inggris adalah… | twenty / twelve / two / twenty-one | B | “twelve” = 12. · “Lima belas” dalam bahasa Inggris… | fifteen / fifty / five / fourteen | A | “fifteen” = 15. · Satu tangan punya ___ jari. Pilih angka Inggris. | five / four / six / ten | A | “five” = 5.\n  - Ucapan: I have twelve pencils. | Saya punya dua belas pensil. | twelve | /twelv/\n- L2 Warna (Colours) · Ucapan\n  - Kartu: red /red/ kata sifat = merah | The apple is red. = Apelnya merah. · blue /bluː/ kata sifat = biru | The sky is blue. = Langitnya biru. · green /ɡriːn/ kata sifat = hijau | The leaf is green. = Daunnya hijau. · yellow /ˈjeloʊ/ kata sifat = kuning | The sun is yellow. = Mataharinya kuning.\n  - Soal: [audio] “red” | blue / red / green / pink | B | “red” = merah. · Langit yang cerah berwarna… | green / yellow / blue / black | C | “blue” = biru. · Warna daun adalah ___. | green / red / white / purple | A | “green” = hijau.\n  - Ucapan: The sky is blue. | Langit berwarna biru. | blue | /bluː/\n- L3 Bentuk & Berhitung (Shapes & Counting) · Tata bahasa\n  - Kartu: circle /ˈsɜːrkl/ kata benda = lingkaran | The ball is a circle. = Bola berbentuk lingkaran. · square /skwer/ kata benda = persegi | The book is a square. = Bukunya berbentuk persegi. · triangle /ˈtraɪæŋɡl/ kata benda = segitiga | A triangle has three sides. = Segitiga punya tiga sisi. · count /kaʊnt/ kata kerja = menghitung | Count to ten. = Hitung sampai sepuluh.\n  - Soal: Bentuk bola adalah… | square / triangle / circle / star | C | “circle” = lingkaran. · Lengkapi: “There ___ three squares.” | is / are / am / be | B | “There are…”. · “Hitung sampai sepuluh.” | Count to ten. / Cut to ten. / Come to ten. / Cook to ten. | A | “Count to ten”.\n  - Ucapan: Count to ten, please. | Hitung sampai sepuluh, ya. | count | /kaʊnt/\n- Ulangan Unit (Unit Review) · 4 kartu dan 3 soal dari pelajaran di atas.\n\nUnit 3 · Di Kantin (At the Canteen)\n- L1 Makanan & Minuman (Food & Drink) · Kosa kata\n  - Kartu: fried rice /fraɪd raɪs/ kata benda = nasi goreng | This fried rice is delicious. = Nasi goreng ini enak. · water /ˈwɔːtər/ kata benda = air | Water, please. = Air, tolong. · milk /mɪlk/ kata benda = susu | I like milk. = Saya suka susu. · banana /bəˈnɑːnə/ kata benda = pisang | The banana is yellow. = Pisangnya kuning.\n  - Soal: “Nasi goreng ini enak.” | This fried rice is delicious. / This fried rice is expensive. / This fried rice is hot. / This fried rice is small. | A | “delicious” = enak. · Kamu haus. Kamu meminta… | Water, please. / Chair, please. / Pencil, please. / Bag, please. | A | Tambahkan please agar sopan. · “pisang” dalam bahasa Inggris… | banana / apple / bread / grape | A | Pisang berwarna yellow.\n  - Ucapan: This fried rice is delicious. | Nasi goreng ini enak. | delicious | /dɪˈlɪʃəs/\n- L2 Berapa Harganya? (How Much Is It?) · Ucapan\n  - Kartu: How much is it? /haʊ mʌtʃ ɪz ɪt/ pertanyaan = Berapa harganya? | How much is it? Five thousand. = Berapa harganya? Lima ribu. · cheap /tʃiːp/ kata sifat = murah | The milk is cheap. = Susunya murah. · expensive /ɪkˈspensɪv/ kata sifat = mahal | The bag is expensive. = Tasnya mahal. · change /tʃeɪndʒ/ kata benda = uang kembalian | Here is your change. = Ini uang kembalianmu.\n  - Soal: [audio] “How much is it?” artinya… | Berapa harganya? / Berapa umurmu? / Siapa itu? / Apa ini? | A | “How much…?”. · Harga barang itu tinggi. Kata yang tepat… | cheap / expensive / small / fast | B | “expensive” = mahal. · Lengkapi: “How ___ is the milk?” | many / much / long / old | B | “How much”.\n  - Ucapan: How much is the banana? | Berapa harga pisangnya? | much | /mʌtʃ/\n- L3 Permintaan Sopan (Polite Requests) · Tata bahasa\n  - Kartu: please /pliːz/ kata seru = tolong | Water, please. = Air, tolong. · sorry /ˈsɑːri/ kata seru = maaf | Sorry, teacher. = Maaf, Bu Guru. · excuse me /ɪkˈskjuːz miː/ ungkapan = permisi | Excuse me, may I pass? = Permisi, boleh lewat? · may I /meɪ aɪ/ ungkapan = bolehkah saya | May I have some water? = Bolehkah saya minta air?\n  - Soal: Kamu ingin lewat. Kamu berkata… | Excuse me. / Good night. / Thank you. / Goodbye. | A | “Excuse me” = permisi. · Meminta dengan sopan: | Give me water. / Water now! / May I have some water, please? / I want water. | C | “May I… , please?”. · Kamu menabrak temanmu. Kamu berkata… | Please. / Sorry. / Hello. / Welcome. | B | “Sorry” = maaf.\n  - Ucapan: May I have some water, please? | Boleh saya minta air, tolong? | please | /pliːz/\n\nUnit 4 · Keluargaku (My Family)\n- L1 Anggota Keluarga (Family Members) · Kosa kata\n  - Kartu: mother /ˈmʌðər/ kata benda = ibu | My mother cooks rice. = Ibuku memasak nasi. · father /ˈfɑːðər/ kata benda = ayah | My father is tall. = Ayahku tinggi. · brother /ˈbrʌðər/ kata benda = saudara laki-laki | I have two brothers. = Saya punya dua saudara laki-laki. · sister /ˈsɪstər/ kata benda = saudara perempuan | My sister is Sinta. = Kakakku bernama Sinta.\n  - Soal: “Ayah” dalam bahasa Inggris… | father / mother / brother / uncle | A | “father” = ayah. · Lengkapi: “I ___ two brothers.” | has / have / haves / having | B | “I have…”. · “Adik laki-lakiku” adalah… | my little sister / my little brother / my mother / my father | B | “my little brother”.\n  - Ucapan: I have two brothers. | Saya punya dua saudara laki-laki. | brothers | /ˈbrʌðərz/\n- L2 Ini Adalah… (This Is My…) · Ucapan\n  - Kartu: grandmother /ˈɡrænmʌðər/ kata benda = nenek | This is my grandmother. = Ini nenekku. · grandfather /ˈɡrænfɑːðər/ kata benda = kakek | My grandfather is kind. = Kakekku baik hati. · uncle /ˈʌŋkl/ kata benda = paman | This is my uncle. = Ini pamanku. · aunt /ænt/ kata benda = bibi | My aunt is a doctor. = Bibiku seorang dokter.\n  - Soal: “This is my grandmother.” artinya… | Ini nenekku. / Itu kakekku. / Ini ibuku. / Ini bibiku. | A | “This is my…”. · Lengkapi: “___ is my uncle.” | This / These / Those / They | A | “This is…”. · Menunjuk dua kakak: “These ___ my sisters.” | is / am / are / be | C | “These are…”.\n  - Ucapan: This is my grandmother. | Ini nenekku. | grandmother | /ˈɡrænmʌðər/\n- L3 Pekerjaan (Jobs) · Tata bahasa\n  - Kartu: teacher /ˈtiːtʃər/ kata benda = guru | My teacher is kind. = Guruku baik hati. · doctor /ˈdɑːktər/ kata benda = dokter | She is a doctor. = Dia seorang dokter. · farmer /ˈfɑːrmər/ kata benda = petani | My father is a farmer. = Ayahku seorang petani. · driver /ˈdraɪvər/ kata benda = sopir | He is a bus driver. = Dia sopir bus.\n  - Soal: Orang yang mengajar di kelas adalah… | driver / teacher / farmer / doctor | B | “teacher” = guru. · Lengkapi: “She ___ a doctor.” | am / are / is / be | C | “She is…”. · “Ayahku seorang petani.” | My father is a farmer. / My father is a driver. / My mother is a farmer. / My father are farmer. | A | “a farmer”.\n  - Ucapan: My father is a farmer. | Ayahku seorang petani. | farmer | /ˈfɑːrmər/\n\nUnit 5 · Hewan & Cuaca (Animals & Weather)\n- L1 Hewan Ternak (Farm Animals) · Kosa kata\n  - Kartu: cow /kaʊ/ kata benda = sapi | The cow is big. = Sapinya besar. · goat /ɡoʊt/ kata benda = kambing | The goat eats grass. = Kambing makan rumput. · chicken /ˈtʃɪkɪn/ kata benda = ayam | The chicken is white. = Ayamnya putih. · duck /dʌk/ kata benda = bebek | The duck says quack. = Bebek berbunyi kwek.\n  - Soal: “sapi” adalah… | goat / cow / duck / hen | B | “cow” = sapi. · Hewan yang berbunyi “quack” adalah… | duck / cow / goat / cat | A | “duck” = bebek. · Lengkapi: “The goats ___ eating grass.” | is / am / are / be | C | “goats are…”.\n  - Ucapan: The cow is big. | Sapi itu besar. | cow | /kaʊ/\n- L2 Hewan Liar (Wild Animals) · Ucapan\n  - Kartu: elephant /ˈelɪfənt/ kata benda = gajah | An elephant is big. = Gajah itu besar. · tiger /ˈtaɪɡər/ kata benda = harimau | The tiger is fast. = Harimau itu cepat. · monkey /ˈmʌŋki/ kata benda = monyet | The monkey eats a banana. = Monyet makan pisang. · snake /sneɪk/ kata benda = ular | The snake is long. = Ularnya panjang.\n  - Soal: Lengkapi: “An elephant is ___ than a goat.” | big / bigger / biggest / more big | B | “bigger than” = lebih besar dari. · Hewan yang punya belalai adalah… | tiger / elephant / snake / monkey | B | “elephant” = gajah. · Lengkapi: “The tiger is ___ than the monkey.” | stronger / strongest / more strong / strong | A | “stronger than”.\n  - Ucapan: An elephant is bigger than a goat. | Gajah lebih besar daripada kambing. | bigger | /ˈbɪɡər/\n- L3 Cuaca (Weather) · Tata bahasa\n  - Kartu: sunny /ˈsʌni/ kata sifat = cerah | It is sunny today. = Hari ini cerah. · rainy /ˈreɪni/ kata sifat = hujan | It is rainy today. = Hari ini hujan. · cloudy /ˈklaʊdi/ kata sifat = berawan | It is cloudy. = Cuacanya berawan. · windy /ˈwɪndi/ kata sifat = berangin | It is windy today. = Hari ini berangin.\n  - Soal: “How is the weather?” artinya… | Jam berapa sekarang? / Bagaimana cuacanya? / Siapa itu? / Berapa harganya? | B | “How is the weather?”. · Kamu butuh payung. Cuacanya… | sunny / rainy / windy / hot | B | “rainy” = hujan. · Lengkapi: “It is ___ today. Let's fly a kite!” | rainy / windy / cold / dark | B | “windy” = berangin.\n  - Ucapan: It is sunny today. | Hari ini cerah. | sunny | /ˈsʌni/\n\nUnit 6 · Di Sekolah (At School)\n- L1 Benda di Kelas (Classroom Things) · Kosa kata\n  - Kartu: book /bʊk/ kata benda = buku | Open your book. = Buka bukumu. · pencil /ˈpensl/ kata benda = pensil | This is my pencil. = Ini pensilku. · ruler /ˈruːlər/ kata benda = penggaris | I need a ruler. = Saya butuh penggaris. · desk /desk/ kata benda = meja | Put it on the desk. = Taruh di atas meja.\n  - Soal: Alat untuk mengukur garis adalah… | pencil / ruler / desk / book | B | “ruler” = penggaris. · “Taruh bukumu di atas meja.” | Put your book on the desk. / Put your desk on the book. / Pick your book in the desk. / Put you book under desk. | A | “on the desk”. · Lengkapi: “This ___ my pencil.” | are / am / is / be | C | “This is…”.\n  - Ucapan: Open your book, please. | Buka bukumu, ya. | open | /ˈoʊpən/\n- L2 Jadwal Pelajaran (My Timetable) · Ucapan\n  - Kartu: Monday /ˈmʌndeɪ/ kata benda = hari Senin | We have English on Monday. = Kami ada pelajaran Inggris hari Senin. · Tuesday /ˈtuːzdeɪ/ kata benda = hari Selasa | Maths is on Tuesday. = Matematika hari Selasa. · timetable /ˈtaɪmteɪbl/ kata benda = jadwal pelajaran | This is my timetable. = Ini jadwal pelajaranku. · subject /ˈsʌbdʒɪkt/ kata benda = mata pelajaran | English is my subject. = Bahasa Inggris adalah mata pelajaranku.\n  - Soal: Lengkapi: “We have English ___ Monday.” | in / on / at / to | B | “on Monday”: on untuk hari, at untuk jam. · “Hari Selasa” dalam bahasa Inggris… | Tuesday / Thursday / Sunday / Saturday | A | “Tuesday” = Selasa. · Lengkapi: “School starts ___ seven o'clock.” | on / at / in / to | B | “at seven”.\n  - Ucapan: We have English on Monday. | Kami ada pelajaran Inggris hari Senin. | Monday | /ˈmʌndeɪ/\n- L3 Meminta Bantuan (Asking for Help) · Tata bahasa\n  - Kartu: help /help/ kata kerja = membantu | Can you help me? = Bisakah kamu membantuku? · understand /ˌʌndərˈstænd/ kata kerja = mengerti | I understand. = Saya mengerti. · repeat /rɪˈpiːt/ kata kerja = mengulang | Can you repeat, please? = Bisakah kamu mengulang? · question /ˈkwestʃən/ kata benda = pertanyaan | I have a question. = Saya punya pertanyaan.\n  - Soal: Kamu tidak paham penjelasan guru. Kamu berkata… | I don't understand. / I don't like you. / I am hungry. / I am fine. | A | Cara sopan memberi tahu guru bahwa kamu belum paham. · Kamu ingin guru mengulang. Kamu berkata… | Stop it, please. / Can you repeat, please? / Give me a pencil. / Where is the door? | B | “repeat” = mengulang. · “Bolehkah saya bertanya?” | May I ask a question? / May I eat a question? / Can I ask a answer? / Do I ask question? | A | “May I ask…?”.\n  - Ucapan: Can you help me, please? | Bisakah kamu membantuku? | help | /help/\n- Quiz notes: answer key A = index 0. If a question has audio, the sound button plays that sentence.\n- Fixed ranking rivals: Nurul Izzati 2410, Kumaran Raja 2180, you (XP from state), Tan Wei Ling 1725, Muhammad Firdaus 1510, Siti Khadijah 1320.\n- Unit tile colours on Home/Path: Unit 1 `#FF8A3D`, Unit 2 `#7BD389`, Unit 3 `#FFD23F`, Unit 4 `#FF9EB5`, Unit 5 `#7CC6FE`, Unit 6 `#C9A7FF` (matching mascot index i%6).\n\n# MOTION & FEEDBACK\n- Screen enter: opacity and translateY 10px, .28 s, `cubic-bezier(.22,.9,.3,1)`.\n- Mascots and logo: `apung` 4.5 s ease-in-out infinite, translateY 0 → -8px → 0.\n- Pressed buttons: sink 4px and shadow shrinks (transition .12 s).\n- Quiz progress bar: width changes over .5 s `cubic-bezier(.3,1.2,.5,1)`.\n- Picking an option: yellow and tick icon at once. A correct answer shows confetti and the Correct screen. A wrong answer shows the Wrong screen with the sad mascot.\n- Speaking waveform: 12 bars change height every 120 ms while recording; at rest they return to POLA = [30,60,85,45,100,70,35,55,25,65,40,20] %.\n- Toast for 1.9 s above the screen. No modals.\n- Confetti when a lesson completes and on a correct answer.\n- All animations stop when `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` is set.\n\n# RESPONSIVE & ACCESSIBILITY\n- 360 px wide with no horizontal scroll. The phone becomes full 100dvh on narrow screens. Side padding 20px.\n- Buttons at least 44px tall; `.tb` 54px. Visible focus: 3px currentColor outline, 2px offset.\n- Non-button `data-go` and `data-do` elements get role=\"button\" and tabIndex=0. Enter and Space trigger a click.\n- The mic can be press-and-held with Space (keydown and keyup).\n- Decorative icons get `aria-hidden` where appropriate. Icon-only buttons get `aria-label`.\n- `lang` follows the toggle: \"en\" when EN, \"id\" when ID.\n- Brown ck text on cream and yellow meets WCAG AA contrast.\n\n# TECHNICAL\n- One index.html file. No build, no server, no login. Ready for drag-and-drop to Netlify Drop.\n- Libraries: none. Fonts from Google Fonts (Lilita One, Nunito 600/700/800, Material Symbols Rounded). Preconnect to fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com.\n- Images are built in code (div + border-radius + inline SVG favicon). No image files.\n- Reused CSS variables and classes. Repeated markup generated from array loops. One state object S and one render function per screen (`V.render[id]`).\n- localStorage wrapped in try/catch. No long comments. Write the full code directly.\n- Audio: `speechSynthesis`, wrapped in try/catch. If unavailable, toast \"Suara tidak tersedia\".\n- `prefers-reduced-motion` turns off animations and confetti.\n- Viewport: `width=device-width,initial-scale=1,maximum-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover`.\n- Responsive: the 390×844 phone on desktop; at ≤600px wide or ≤900px tall it becomes full screen.\n- Do not mention any app name or third-party brand in code or text.\n\n# CHECK BEFORE FINISHING\n- All 12 screens (onboarding ×2, grade, home, path, card, quiz, correct, wrong, speaking, ranking, progress, profile) open and return correctly.\n- The dock appears only on Home, Path, Progress, Profile and Ranking (highlighting Profile).\n- Locked and unlocked steps are correct. Finishing one lesson moves Path forward.\n- Answer keys A/B/C/D match the list above; 54 questions in total.\n- After reload, state persists (localStorage). Reset returns to Onboarding.\n- No horizontal scroll at 360 px. No console errors."},{"id":"kido-koda","kat":"app","katN":"App","n":"KIDO (flat poster style)","mapel":"English","jenjang":"Children","topik":"English-learning app for children with 14 screens: daily tasks, vocabulary, streak days, and a progress board.","img":"img/kido-koda.jpg","preview":"https://preview.edugamelabs.com/app/kido-koda/","prompt":"# ROLE\n- Art director + lead web developer. Rebuild the UI kit of the children's English learning app \"KIDO\" as ONE `index.html` file (plain HTML+CSS+JS, no build, no framework, no server/API/login).\n- 14 static screens inside a 390×844 phone frame, with navigation between screens.\n- Product language: default **English**, with an **EN / BM** button for Bahasa Melayu.\n\n# PRODUCT\n- Title: `KIDO — Learn English for Kids`. Meta: \"KIDO — a bilingual (English / Bahasa Melayu) English learning app for kids. 14 screens, flat interface.\"\n- `<html lang=\"en\">`, theme-color `#C9DE86`, viewport `width=device-width,initial-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover`.\n- Favicon SVG: `#14170F` square + `#BEDC4E` circle (r 28).\n\n# VISUAL STYLE\n- Colour tokens (write once, refer by name):\n  - `--ink:#14170F` text, nav, dark buttons, dark cards\n  - `--ink-2:#242A1B` code window and dark screen background\n  - `--ink-3:#2C3320` secondary dark buttons, window header\n  - `--lime:#BEDC4E` main accent (text on ink, active nav)\n  - `--mint:#E7F0D4` bar tracks, chips, soft ticks, mint cards\n  - `--paper:#FFFFFF` white cards\n  - `--bg:#F6F8F0` screen background; `--canvas:#C9DE86` stage background\n  - `--flame:#FF6B35` orange cards/rows\n  - `--sun:#FFD166` yellow: hen, mascot feet, third habit\n  - `--sage:#CBD5B8` unfinished bars, fourth habit\n  - `--olive:#8CA83A` second progress row\n  - `--moss:#4B5A2E` empty day circles, mascot leaf\n  - `--edge:#E9EFDD` chip border\n  - `--grey-3:#9AA48A` labels on dark; `--grey-4:#6E7A5C` labels on light, locks, borders\n- Font: **Plus Jakarta Sans** 400/500/600/700/800 (`--sans`); **JetBrains Mono** 400/500/700 (`--mono`) for labels, clock, pills, small numbers.\n- Scale: `.h1` 800 32px/1.05 (-.02em); `.h2` 800 24px/1.12; `.h3` 700 18px/1.2; `.h4` 700 15px/1.25; `.body` 500 14px/1.5; `.lbl` mono 700 10px uppercase, spacing .08em.\n- `.phone` frame: 390×844px, radius 44px, bg `--bg`, overflow hidden, shadow `0 22px 44px rgba(20,23,15,.20)`, stage bg `--canvas` with 24px padding. At ≤460px: 100vw × 100dvh, radius 0, no shadow.\n- Status bar `.sb`: padding 18px 28px 4px, mono 600 13px. Left \"9:41\"; right two battery icons (16×10 border 2px; 22×10 fill, radius 2px).\n- Card `.card`: white, radius 26px, padding 18px, gap 10px. Variants: `.d` ink (white text), `.d2` ink-3, `.lime`, `.mint`, `.flame` (white text).\n- Row `.row`: white, radius 20px, padding 14px, gap 12px. Variants: `.d` ink, `.lime`, `.flame`, `.lock` (mint, opacity .7).\n- Button `.btn`: pill, min-height 58px, padding 0 24px, bg ink, lime text 700 15px, full width. `.alt`: white + 2px ink border. `.lime`: lime bg, ink text. `.g`: ink-3 bg, white text. `.btns`: two buttons in a row, gap 10px.\n- Pill `.pill`: padding 6px 11px, bg ink, lime text. `.l` lime/ink; `.m` mint/ink; `.f` flame/white.\n- Chip `.chip`: min-height 36px, padding 0 16px, pill, white, 1px `--edge` border, mono 700 12px. Active: bg ink, lime text.\n- Bar `.bar`: 8px high, pill, mint track, ink fill. On a lime card, the track is white at 55%.\n- Segments `.seg`: 6px high, pill, sage; `.on` ink; `.cur` lime with a 2px ink outline.\n- Tabs `.tabs`: white pill, padding 4px; `.on` bg ink, lime text.\n- Nav `.nav`: white, padding 12px 26px 22px. Item `.nv`: column, gap 5px, mono 700 10px, opacity .4 (active 1). Icons 22px currentColor: HOME square radius 7px; LEARN ring 3px border; TASKS arch radius 20px 20px 0 0; ME leaf radius 100% 0 100% 0. FAB: 52px circle ink, \"+\" lime 700 28px, margin-top -26px.\n- Window `.win`: bg ink-2, radius 20px, mono 500 12.5px/1.9. Header ink-3 with three 9px grey-4 dots and file name 11px grey-3. Token colours: `.k` lime, `.s` sun, `.g` grey-3, `.x` flame. Highlighted line bg #3A1A10.\n- Blob 44px: `b-c` circle; `b-l` leaf; `b-a` arch; `b-h` half circle, 22px high.\n- Avatar 44px lime circle; `a2` mint; `a3` sun; `ai` ink with lime features. Head 38% wide, top 20%, left 31%; body 64%×34% at the bottom.\n- Tick: 26px ink circle, lime text 700 13px (`.s` 22px). Lock `.lockic`: 18×13 grey-4 radius 4, with an 8px arc on top.\n- Calendar: 7 columns, round cells max 40px. `c-m` mint; `c-k` ink; `c-l` lime; `c-f` flame.\n- Badge `.bdg`: radius 24px, padding 12px 10px, min-height 146px. `.l` lime; `.f` flame; `.r` 2px lime border; `.k` ink-3 with grey-3 text.\n- `.round`: 48px white circle, ink text 700 20px. `.sbtn`: 96×52 ink pill with a 28×14 lime half-circle in the centre.\n\n# NAVIGATION & SCREENS\nThe 14 screens in order (id in brackets). Each screen: status bar, scrollable content, bottom nav where stated.\n1. **splash** (01, lime background, no nav): \"KIDO\" 44px 800; \"Learn English for Kids\" (BM \"Belajar Bahasa Inggeris untuk Kanak-kanak\"). Mascot in the centre. Bottom: \"Lets Start\" (BM \"Jom Mula\") h1 + sbtn → home. Small text: \"By tapping Start and using KIDO you agree to our Terms and Privacy Policy.\" (BM \"Dengan menekan Mula, anda bersetuju dengan Terma dan Dasar Privasi KIDO.\").\n2. **home** (02, HOME nav): avatar (→ profile) + \"Welcome Back\" (BM \"Selamat Kembali\") + \"Aisyah Nur\" h3; on the right a 38px white calendar button. Dark card: \"DAILY GOAL\" (BM \"MATLAMAT HARIAN\"), lime pill \"WEEK 7\" (BM \"MINGGU 7\"), h2 \"3 OF 4 TASKS DONE\" (BM \"3 DARIPADA 4 SIAP\"), seven days Mon–Sun (BM Isn, Sel, Rab, Kha, Jum, Sab, Ahd), first 4 lime with ✓. Grid 2: lime card \"PRACTICE\" (BM \"LATIHAN\"), \"12 NEW WORDS\" (BM \"12 PERKATAAN BARU\"), tick →; white card \"STREAK\" (BM \"RENTETAN\"), \"25\", \"Streak Days\" (BM \"Hari Berturut\"). \"Progress Board\" card (BM \"Papan Kemajuan\") + mint pill \"08 — 20 AUG\"; five bar rows.\n3. **topics** (03, LEARN nav): back + \"Habits & Topics\" (BM \"Tabiat & Topik\"). Single-select chips: All/Semua (active), Words/Perkataan, Phonics/Fonik, Songs/Lagu. Dark card \"Keep It Up\" (BM \"Teruskan!\") + pill \"25 DAYS\" (BM \"25 HARI\") → streak. Four habit rows → topic.\n4. **topic** (04, LEARN nav): back \"Starter Words\" (BM \"Perkataan Asas\"). Lime card, bar 52%. Five modules; the active module → lesson. Button \"Continue Module 03\" (BM \"Sambung Modul 03\").\n5. **lesson** (05, LEARN nav): bar 40% + \"4/9\". Title, window, mint card, three animal cards, button \"Next: Try it yourself\" (BM \"Seterusnya: Cuba sendiri\") → wordlab.\n6. **wordlab** (06, dark background, LEARN nav): dark back \"Word Lab\" (BM \"Makmal Perkataan\"); window; key pad; Reset (BM \"Set Semula\") and \"Check & Submit\" (BM \"Semak & Hantar\") → quiz.\n7. **quiz** (07, LEARN nav): back, five-segment bar (first two on, third cur), pill \"0:42\". Question, window, 4 options. Skip (BM \"Langkau\") → oops; \"Check Answer\" (BM \"Semak Jawapan\") → home.\n8. **oops** (08, LEARN nav): back \"Oops Hint\" (BM \"Bantuan\"), orange card, window, two stat cards, two buttons.\n9. **task** (09, TASKS nav): Daily Task tab active; timeline of four items.\n10. **progress** (10, TASKS nav): Progress tab active; six skill bars; dark card \"CLASS ACTIVITIES\".\n11. **calendar** (11, TASKS nav): back \"August 2026\" (BM \"Ogos 2026\"); calendar; four events.\n12. **streak** (12, lime background, ME nav): 150px black circle \"25\"; week card; three habits.\n13. **goals** (13, dark background, ME nav): three stats, six badges, ↗ button → profile.\n14. **profile** (14, ME nav): lime card, three stats, class board, \"Challenge a classmate\" (BM \"Cabar rakan sekelas\") → quiz.\n- Outside the stage: \"UI KIT →\" at top left to #splash (hidden ≤460px); EN/BM choice at top right, ink pill, active lime.\n- Splash mascot 250×260: ink round body 200px (left 25, top 50); moss leaf 60px radius 100% 0 100% 0 (left 112, top 6); two lime eyes 18px (top 120; left 78 and 154); box smile 50×26 with 6px lime border, border-top 0, radius 0 0 50px 50px (left 100, top 158); yellow left foot 90×45 half-circle (left 0, top 215); white right foot (right 0, top 215).\n\n# FEATURES & LOGIC\n- `data-go=\"<id>\"` opens a screen; the hash `#<id>` is kept in sync (replaceState); `hashchange` loads the screen; unknown id → splash. Scroll returns to 0 on every change.\n- Chip `data-tog=\"one\"`: one active per row. Word Lab keys `data-tog=\"many\"`: on/off, aria-pressed. Reset turns off all keys.\n- Language: English text is the default; BM is stored in `data-ms`. Switching language writes innerHTML, sets `lang`, aria-pressed, and saves localStorage `kido-lang` (`en`/`ms`), wrapped in try/catch. On start, read `kido-lang`, default `en`.\n- Elements `[data-go]` that are not button/a: role=button, tabindex=0; Enter/Space also open the screen.\n\n# CONTENT & DATA\n- Habits (topics): \"Read one story every day\" (BM \"Baca satu cerita setiap hari\") 25 D, 72%, lime, circle · \"Say 5 new words out loud\" (BM \"Sebut 5 perkataan baharu dengan kuat\") 21 D, 48%, ink, leaf · \"Sing the ABC song with family\" (BM \"Nyanyi lagu ABC bersama keluarga\") 30 D, 88%, sun, arch · \"Spell two animal words\" (BM \"Eja dua perkataan haiwan\") 14 D, 34%, sage, half circle.\n- Home bars (width in px): ALPHABET/ABJAD lime 96 · PHONICS/FONIK mint 40 + ink 114 · WORDS/PERKATAAN mint 70 + lime 104 · NUMBERS/NOMBOR mint 24 + ink 76 · COLOURS/WARNA mint 104 + lime 64.\n- Modules (topic): \"A B C — Letters\"/Huruf, \"8 LESSONS · DONE ✓\" (8 PELAJARAN · SIAP ✓), done · \"Phonics Sounds\"/Bunyi Fonik, \"6 LESSONS · DONE ✓\", done · \"Animal Friends\"/Haiwan Kesayangan, \"4 OF 9 LESSONS\" (4 DARIPADA 9 PELAJARAN), active, tick 3, GO (JOM) pill · \"Colours & Shapes\"/Warna & Bentuk, LOCKED (BERKUNCI) · \"My First Sentences\"/Ayat Pertama Saya, LOCKED.\n- Lesson 05: \"LESSON 04 · ANIMALS\" (PELAJARAN 04 · HAIWAN). \"Meet the animals and say their names\" (Kenal haiwan dalam bahasa Inggeris). Window \"cat.mp3\": `cat = kucing`; `say /kæt/`; `use(\"The cat is small.\")`. Mint card: \"The c in cat is a hard sound, like k — not s. Try it: c–a–t.\" (Bunyi c dalam cat keras seperti k — bukan s. Cuba: c–a–t.). Animal cards: dog/anjing (lime), hen/ayam (ink), fish/ikan (flame).\n- Word Lab 06: \"CHALLENGE 07 · EASY\" (CABARAN 07 · MUDAH), pill \"+40 XP\". \"Spell the animal you hear.\" (Eja haiwan yang kamu dengar.). Answer C A T. Keys C, A, T, K, O, S; the first three active.\n- Quiz 07: \"QUESTION 03 OF 05 · ANIMALS\" (SOALAN 03 DARIPADA 05 · HAIWAN). \"What is \"kucing\" in English?\" (Apakah \"kucing\" dalam bahasa Inggeris?). A dog · B cat (CORRECT) · C cow · D hen. Answer key: B.\n- Oops 08: \"ATTEMPT 2 · 1 LETTER WRONG\" (CUBAAN 2 · 1 HURUF SALAH); \"Wrong first letter\" (Huruf pertama tersilap); \"you spelled K A T\" → \"C A T\". Stat \"2\" CUBAAN DIGUNA; \"1\" BANTUAN BAKI.\n- Task 09: 08:00 AM English class — letters A to E · 11:00 AM Group story time, \"The Little Cat\" · 03:00 PM Finish Word Lab challenge 07 · 08:30 PM Read 5 pages with mum. Ending: \"You Got It! Have a Rest.\"\n- Progress 10: Alphabet lime 150 tick · Phonics ink 110 + sage 44 · Words lime 190 · Numbers ink 84 + sage 60 · Speaking sage 70 · Reading lime 160 tick. \"CLASS ACTIVITIES\" (AKTIVITI KELAS) 78%: Storytelling Day (Group A) 78% lime; Word Scrapbook 54% olive; Show & Tell 21% ink-3.\n- Calendar: days 10–23; highlights 11 mint, 13 ink, 14 lime, 18 mint, 21 flame. Events: 21 AUG Spelling Bee (9:00 AM · 20 WORDS); 26 AUG Storytelling show; 02 SEP Reading check; 09 SEP Scrapbook hand-in.\n- Streak 12: \"DAY STREAK\" (HARI BERTURUT). \"Learn for at least 10 minutes to keep it alive. Longest run so far: 41 days.\" Week: M ink, T ink, W lime, T ink, F lime, S mint, S mint. Habits: Morning word 18/20 (90%), One word a day 12/20 (60%), Read a picture book 7/20 (35%).\n- Goals 13: lime \"14 FINISHED\" (SIAP), \"3 DOING\" (SEDANG), \"2 DROPPED\" (BERHENTI). Badges: 100 WORDS Word Master (Raja Perkataan) lime; 30 DAYS On Fire (Semangat Membara) flame; NO SLIPS Clean Spell (Ejaan Tepat) outline; LOCKED: Team Lead (Ketua Kumpulan), Storyteller (Pencerita), Spelling Bee (Juara Mengeja).\n- Profile 14: \"Aisyah Nur\", \"YEAR 1 BESTARI · AGE 7\", \"2,450 XP · RANK #4 OF 38\"; stats 86 LESSONS, 41 WORDS, 12 BADGES. Board: Tan Wei Jie 3,180 · Aina Sofea 2,940 · Arvind Kumar 2,610 · You/Kamu 2,450 (dark row) · Siti Hajar 2,205.\n\n# MOTION & FEEDBACK\n- No animation, keyframes, or transitions. Screen changes, chips, and keys change instantly.\n- Keyboard focus: 3px `--flame` outline, outline-offset 2px.\n\n# RESPONSIVE & ACCESSIBILITY\n- Width 390 px inside the frame; ≤460 px is full screen. No horizontal scrolling. Touch targets at least 44 px.\n- `aria-label` on back, calendar, profile, Start, and icon-only buttons.\n- `prefers-reduced-motion`: turn off all animation and transitions.\n\n# TECHNICAL\n- One `index.html`, plain HTML+CSS+JS. Google Fonts with preconnect and `css2` for JetBrains Mono and Plus Jakarta Sans. No libraries. No images; all shapes in CSS or inline SVG.\n- Build: 14 screens in an array, rendered once into `<main id=\"screens\">`; helper `t(en,ms,cls,tag)` produces `data-ms`; `NAV(active)` and `P(html)` reused.\n- localStorage: only `kido-lang`, inside try/catch.\n- Write the complete code directly. Ready for Netlify Drop (one folder, no build).\n\n# CHECK BEFORE FINISHING\n- 14 screens, correct `data-go` and active nav; EN/BM complete and saved.\n- Hex values, radii, and splash mascot match.\n- No horizontal scroll at 360 px; no third-party brand names."}];
